export const content: Record<string, string> = {
  "优胜美地": "Yosemite",
  "花岗岩巨壁与瀑布": "Granite walls and waterfalls",
  "花岗岩巨壁和瀑布的天下：酋长岩、半穹顶、优胜美地瀑布都挤在一条约 11 公里长的冰川山谷里。春季（4–6 月）瀑布最壮观；夏秋可以走 Tioga Road 去高山草甸；南边的 Mariposa Grove 有 500 多棵巨杉。": "A kingdom of granite walls and waterfalls: El Capitan, Half Dome, and Yosemite Falls all crowd into a glacier-carved valley about 7 miles long. The falls peak in spring (April–June). In summer and fall, Tioga Road climbs to high-country meadows, and Mariposa Grove in the south holds more than 500 giant sequoias.",
  "4–6 月瀑布最盛；9–10 月人少，Tioga Road 还开着。": "Waterfalls peak April–June. September–October is quieter, and Tioga Road is still open.",
  "优胜美地山谷": "Yosemite Valley",
  "冰川点路": "Glacier Point Road",
  "Tioga Road 高山区": "Tioga Road high country",
  "Wawona / 巨杉林": "Wawona / Mariposa Grove",
  "Hetch Hetchy（西北角）": "Hetch Hetchy (northwest)",
  "园内的 Yosemite Valley Lodge、Curry Village、The Ahwahnee 离景点最近，通常提前约一年开放预订，旺季很快订满；订不到可以住西边的 El Portal、Mariposa，南边的 Oakhurst（去巨杉林方便），或北边的 Groveland。夏秋走 Tioga Road 往东，也可以住东门外的 Lee Vining。": "In-park lodging at Yosemite Valley Lodge, Curry Village, and The Ahwahnee puts you closest to the sights. Reservations usually open about a year out and fill fast in peak season. If you can't get in, stay west in El Portal or Mariposa, south in Oakhurst (handy for Mariposa Grove), or north in Groveland. In summer and fall you can also cross Tioga Road and stay in Lee Vining, outside the east entrance.",
  "红杉与国王峡谷": "Sequoia & Kings Canyon",
  "地球上体积最大的树": "The largest trees on Earth",
  "两个相连的公园，主角是巨杉：谢尔曼将军树按体积是地球上最大的树。红杉公园在南（Giant Forest），国王峡谷在北（Grant Grove、Cedar Grove），两边开车约 1 小时。": "Two adjoining parks built around giant sequoias. The General Sherman Tree is the largest tree on Earth by volume. Sequoia is to the south (Giant Forest) and Kings Canyon to the north (Grant Grove, Cedar Grove), about an hour's drive apart.",
  "5–10 月最方便；冬季山路要带雪链，Cedar Grove 封路。": "May–October is easiest. In winter, carry tire chains on mountain roads; the road to Cedar Grove closes.",
  "Foothills（山脚）": "Foothills",
  "Giant Forest（红杉）": "Giant Forest (Sequoia)",
  "Grant Grove（国王峡谷）": "Grant Grove (Kings Canyon)",
  "Cedar Grove（峡谷底）": "Cedar Grove (canyon floor)",
  "Foothills 游客中心": "Foothills Visitor Center",
  "园内有 Wuksachi Lodge（红杉这边）和 John Muir Lodge（国王峡谷这边）；园外最方便的是南门外的 Three Rivers，去 Giant Forest 要爬约 1 小时盘山路。Visalia 酒店多、价格低，但离得更远。": "In-park options are Wuksachi Lodge on the Sequoia side and John Muir Lodge on the Kings Canyon side. The most convenient town is Three Rivers, outside the south entrance, though Giant Forest is still about an hour up a winding road. Visalia has more hotels at lower prices but is farther away.",
  "尖峰石阵": "Pinnacles",
  "火山岩尖峰与加州神鹫": "Volcanic spires and California condors",
  "2,300 万年前一座火山在今天洛杉矶北边的羚羊谷一带喷发，随后被圣安德烈亚斯断层劈成两半，西边这一半跟着太平洋板块往西北挪了约 310 公里，剩下的火山角砾岩被风雨削成一片红褐色的尖峰和石墙。巨石塌进窄峡谷，堆出能钻进去的“崖缝洞穴”（talus cave），洞里住着汤森大耳蝠；高处的岩壁是重新放归野外的加州神鹫的家，常能看到翼展近 3 米的神鹫在 High Peaks 上空盘旋。公园离旧金山湾区约 2 小时车程，东西两侧各有入口，但园内不通车，只能靠步道相连。": "Twenty-three million years ago a volcano erupted near today's Antelope Valley, north of Los Angeles. The San Andreas Fault then split it in two, and the western half rode the Pacific Plate about 195 miles northwest. Wind and rain have carved what's left of its volcanic breccia into red-brown spires and rock walls. Boulders wedged into narrow canyons form talus caves you can walk through, home to Townsend's big-eared bats. The high cliffs are home to reintroduced California condors; you'll often see these birds, with wingspans of nearly 10 feet, circling over the High Peaks. The park is about two hours from the San Francisco Bay Area. It has entrances on both the east and west sides, but no road crosses the park—only trails connect them.",
  "2–5 月最好：山坡转绿、野花开，小溪有水，但周末和节假日人最多，早上 8 点前就可能停满。6–9 月常超过 38°C，岩石上更热，只适合清早或傍晚走短线；Bear Gulch 洞穴 5 月中到 7 月中为保护蝙蝠育幼全部关闭。10–11 月凉快人少，冬天偶有暴雨，洞里会积水临时关闭。": "February–May is best: green hills, wildflowers, and water in the creeks, but weekends and holidays are the busiest, and lots can fill before 8 a.m. June–September often tops 100°F, and the rocks are hotter still; stick to short hikes early or late in the day. Bear Gulch Cave closes completely from mid-May to mid-July to protect the bat nursery colony. October–November is cool and quieter. Winter brings occasional heavy rain, and the caves may close temporarily when they flood.",
  "东侧（Bear Gulch · 营地 · 游客中心）": "East side (Bear Gulch, campground, visitor center)",
  "西侧（Chaparral · West Pinnacles）": "West side (Chaparral, West Pinnacles)",
  "尖峰石阵游客中心（东侧，营地内）": "Pinnacles Visitor Center (east side, in the campground)",
  "园内没有酒店，唯一的过夜地方是东侧的 Pinnacles Campground（帐篷位、房车位和全年开放的帆布帐篷小屋，提前 6 个月在 Recreation.gov 订，春天周末很早订满），西侧不能过夜。住园外的话，去东侧住 Hollister（到东门约 45 分钟）或更远的 Gilroy，去西侧住 Soledad（约 25 分钟）或 Salinas、Monterey（约 1 小时–1 小时 15 分）；King City 在两侧之间，到东门约 50 分钟、西门约 45 分钟。两边都想走的，一天走一侧最省事。": "There are no hotels in the park. The only place to spend the night is Pinnacles Campground on the east side (tent sites, RV sites, and year-round tent cabins), bookable on Recreation.gov six months ahead; spring weekends fill early. You can't stay overnight on the west side. For the east side, stay in Hollister (about 45 minutes to the east entrance) or farther out in Gilroy. For the west side, stay in Soledad (about 25 minutes) or in Salinas or Monterey (about 1 hour–1 hour 15 minutes). King City sits between the two, about 50 minutes from the east entrance and 45 minutes from the west. If you want to see both sides, the simplest plan is one side per day.",
  "海峡群岛": "Channel Islands",
  "海蚀洞、岛狐与鲸鱼": "Sea caves, island foxes, and whales",
  "由南加州外海的五座岛和周围海域组成，岛上不能开车、没有商店，上岛基本只能坐船，吃喝都要自带。长期与大陆隔绝，2,000 多种动植物里有 145 种是这里独有的（比如岛狐），常被称为“北美的加拉帕戈斯”。多数人从 Ventura 港坐 Island Packers 的船去 Santa Cruz 岛或 Anacapa 岛一日游，风浪大时会停航。": "Five islands off the Southern California coast and the waters around them. There are no cars or stores on the islands, and nearly the only way out is by boat, so bring all your food and water. Long isolation from the mainland has produced 145 species found nowhere else among more than 2,000 plants and animals (the island fox, for one), earning the park the nickname “the Galápagos of North America.” Most people take an Island Packers boat from Ventura Harbor for a day trip to Santa Cruz Island or Anacapa Island. Boats don't run in rough seas.",
  "8–10 月风浪最小、海水最清，登岛和划船最稳；春季岛上变绿开花、还有灰鲸，但风大易停航；5–7 月早上常有海雾。": "August–October has the calmest seas and clearest water, the most reliable conditions for landings and kayaking. In spring the islands turn green and bloom and gray whales pass by, but wind often cancels boats. May–July mornings are often foggy.",
  "Ventura 港（大陆）": "Ventura Harbor (mainland)",
  "阿纳卡帕岛（Anacapa）": "Anacapa Island",
  "圣克鲁斯岛（Santa Cruz）": "Santa Cruz Island",
  "圣罗莎岛（Santa Rosa）": "Santa Rosa Island",
  "圣米格尔岛（San Miguel）": "San Miguel Island",
  "Ventura 港游客中心": "Ventura Harbor Visitor Center",
  "岛上没有酒店，只有简易露营地（装备要自己带上船、搬到营地，recreation.gov 最早提前 6 个月预订）。坐船当天要提前到码头签到，住 Ventura 港边最方便，Ventura 老城区餐厅多、开车约 10 分钟；部分班次从 Oxnard 的 Channel Islands Harbor 出发，订住处前看清船票。Santa Barbara 城市更有味道但房价高、到码头约 45 分钟，预算有限可以住 Camarillo 的连锁酒店。": "There are no hotels on the islands, only primitive campgrounds. You carry all your gear onto the boat and haul it to camp; reservations open on Recreation.gov up to six months ahead. You need to check in at the dock early on boat day, so staying by Ventura Harbor is easiest; downtown Ventura, with more restaurants, is about 10 minutes away. Some departures leave from Channel Islands Harbor in Oxnard, so check your boat ticket before you book a room. Santa Barbara has more character but higher prices and is about 45 minutes from the dock. On a budget, try the chain hotels in Camarillo.",
  "约书亚树": "Joshua Tree",
  "约书亚树与巨石堆": "Joshua trees and boulder piles",
  "两个沙漠在这里交汇：西北部海拔较高的莫哈韦沙漠长满了枝杈古怪的约书亚树，散落着一堆堆圆滚滚的花岗岩巨石；东南部低处是更热更干的科罗拉多沙漠，有泰迪熊仙人掌园和扇棕榈绿洲。园内没有酒店、餐厅和加油站，多数人住北边 62 号公路沿线的小镇，开车一天就能串起隐谷、骷髅岩和 Keys View；这里也是国际暗夜公园和世界知名的攀岩地，从洛杉矶开车约 2.5 小时。": "Two deserts meet here. The higher Mojave Desert in the northwest is covered in oddly branched Joshua trees and scattered piles of rounded granite boulders. The lower, hotter, drier Colorado Desert in the southeast has the Cholla Cactus Garden and fan palm oases. There are no hotels, restaurants, or gas stations in the park; most people stay in the towns along Highway 62 to the north and link Hidden Valley, Skull Rock, and Keys View in a day's drive. Joshua Tree is also an International Dark Sky Park and a world-famous climbing destination, about 2.5 hours from Los Angeles.",
  "10–4 月最舒服，雨水多的年份 2–4 月有野花和约书亚树开花；6–9 月白天常超过 38°C，只适合清晨走短步道，49 Palms 步道 6–9 月关闭；冬天夜里常到 0°C 以下，偶尔下雪。": "October–April is most comfortable. In wet years, February–April brings wildflowers and blooming Joshua trees. June–September days often top 100°F; hike only short trails at dawn. The 49 Palms Oasis Trail closes June–September. Winter nights often drop below freezing, with occasional snow.",
  "西部 · 隐谷 / Keys View": "West: Hidden Valley / Keys View",
  "中部 · 巨石阵 / 骷髅岩": "Central: Jumbo Rocks / Skull Rock",
  "北侧 · Twentynine Palms": "North: Twentynine Palms",
  "平托盆地 · 仙人掌园": "Pinto Basin: Cholla Cactus Garden",
  "南部 · Cottonwood": "South: Cottonwood",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Jumbo Rocks、Indian Cove、Black Rock、Cottonwood 等露营地（主要营地全年要在 recreation.gov 预约，最早提前 6 个月），大多没有自来水。多数人住北边 62 号公路沿线的小镇：Joshua Tree 镇离西入口最近，酒店少、整套民宿多；Yucca Valley 有连锁酒店和大超市；Twentynine Palms 靠北入口、价格最低。10 月到次年 5 月、尤其周末和春假要提前一两个月订；想住度假酒店可以住约 1 小时车程的 Palm Springs 或 Palm Desert。": "There are no hotels in the park, only campgrounds such as Jumbo Rocks, Indian Cove, Black Rock, and Cottonwood. The main campgrounds require reservations on Recreation.gov year-round (up to six months ahead), and most have no running water. Most people stay in the towns along Highway 62 to the north. Joshua Tree, closest to the west entrance, has few hotels but many vacation rentals; Yucca Valley has chain hotels and big supermarkets; Twentynine Palms, near the north entrance, is cheapest. From October through May—especially weekends and spring break—book a month or two ahead. For a resort, stay in Palm Springs or Palm Desert, about an hour away.",
  "红木": "Redwood",
  "地球上最高的树": "The tallest trees on Earth",
  "地球上最高的树——海岸红杉的大本营，由一座国家公园和 Prairie Creek、Del Norte Coast、Jedediah Smith 三座州立公园联合管理，沿 101 公路狭长分布，从南端 Orick 到北端 Crescent City 开车约 1 小时。原始林里随处是上千岁、近百米高的红杉，海边还有蕨类峡谷、金崖海滩和克拉马斯河口，草原上常见成群的罗斯福马鹿。国家公园不收门票，只有部分州立公园区域收日用费。": "The stronghold of the coast redwood, the tallest tree on Earth. One national park and three state parks—Prairie Creek, Del Norte Coast, and Jedediah Smith—are managed together in a long strip along U.S. 101, about an hour's drive from Orick in the south to Crescent City in the north. The old-growth forest is full of redwoods more than a thousand years old and nearly 330 feet tall. On the coast you'll find a fern-walled canyon, Gold Bluffs Beach, and the mouth of the Klamath River, and herds of Roosevelt elk graze the prairies. The national park charges no entrance fee; only some state park areas charge a day-use fee.",
  "全年开放；5–9 月雨少、Fern Canyon 搭起临时木桥，但海边常有雾，10–4 月是雨季。": "Open year-round. May–September is drier, and seasonal footbridges go up at Fern Canyon, but coastal fog is common. October–April is the rainy season.",
  "Orick / Bald Hills（南端）": "Orick / Bald Hills (south)",
  "Prairie Creek（草原溪）": "Prairie Creek",
  "Klamath（克拉马斯河口）": "Klamath (river mouth)",
  "Crescent City / Jedediah Smith（北端）": "Crescent City / Jedediah Smith (north)",
  "园外南侧（巨人大道）": "South of the park (Avenue of the Giants)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Elk Prairie 和 Jedediah Smith 露营地里的几间简易木屋（要自带寝具），通常提前几个月就订满。南段可以住 Orick 的 Elk Meadow Cabins，或更南边的 Trinidad、Arcata、Eureka；北段住 Crescent City 最方便，酒店多、有 Tesla 超充；Klamath 在中间，南北两头都不远。": "There are no hotels in the park, only a few basic cabins in the Elk Prairie and Jedediah Smith campgrounds (bring your own bedding), which usually book up months ahead. For the southern end, stay at Elk Meadow Cabins in Orick or farther south in Trinidad, Arcata, or Eureka. For the north, Crescent City is most convenient, with plenty of hotels and a Tesla Supercharger. Klamath is in the middle, close to both ends.",
  "拉森火山": "Lassen Volcanic",
  "四种火山与沸腾泥潭": "Four types of volcanoes and boiling mud pots",
  "加州北部的火山公园，世界上四种类型的火山（熔岩穹丘、盾状火山、火山渣锥、复合火山）在这里都能看到，拉森峰在 1914–1917 年最后一次喷发。约 48 公里长的公园公路绕过拉森峰东侧，沿途是冒泡的泥浆池、喷气孔和高山湖；东北角的 Butte Lake 还有火山渣锥和彩色的火山灰丘。": "A volcanic park in Northern California where you can see all four types of volcano found in the world: plug dome, shield, cinder cone, and composite. Lassen Peak last erupted in 1914–1917. The park highway runs about 30 miles around the east side of Lassen Peak, past bubbling mud pots, fumaroles, and alpine lakes. In the northeast corner, Butte Lake has a cinder cone and the multicolored Painted Dunes.",
  "公园公路通常 6 月全线通车、10 月底到 11 月下雪后封路；Bumpass Hell 和拉森峰步道一般 7 月雪化后才开放。": "The park highway usually opens fully in June and closes with the first snow in late October or November. The Bumpass Hell and Lassen Peak trails generally open in July, once the snow melts.",
  "西南入口区": "Southwest entrance",
  "拉森峰周边": "Lassen Peak area",
  "公路北段 / 曼萨尼塔湖": "North highway / Manzanita Lake",
  "Butte Lake（东北角）": "Butte Lake (northeast)",
  "园外北侧（Old Station / Burney）": "North of the park (Old Station / Burney)",
  "园内只有两处住宿，都只在夏秋营业：西北角 Manzanita Lake 露营地的简易小木屋（要自带床品），和东南角 Warner Valley 的 Drakesbad 客栈牧场（含三餐，常提前一年订满）。南边住西南入口外的 Mineral 最近，Chester 选择更多；北边可以住 Old Station、Shingletown，或者约 1 小时车程外的雷丁，酒店多、价格低。": "The park has just two places to stay, both open only in summer and fall: simple camping cabins at Manzanita Lake Campground in the northwest (bring your own bedding) and Drakesbad Guest Ranch in Warner Valley in the southeast (meals included; often booked a year ahead). To the south, Mineral, just outside the southwest entrance, is closest, and Chester has more choices. To the north, try Old Station or Shingletown, or Redding, about an hour away, with many hotels at lower prices.",
  "火山口湖": "Crater Lake",
  "火山口里的美国最深湖": "America's deepest lake, in a volcano",
  "约 7,700 年前马扎马火山（Mount Mazama）大喷发后塌陷，雨雪积成了深 592 米的火山口湖，是美国最深的湖，湖水异常清澈、呈深蓝色。53 公里长的环湖公路 Rim Drive 沿途有 30 多个观景点，通常 7 月中到 10 月下旬全线开通；冬季平均降雪约 13 米，只能开到 Rim Village。唯一下到湖边的 Cleetwood Cove 步道 2026–2028 年重建关闭，这期间没有湖上游船，也上不了巫师岛。": "About 7,700 years ago Mount Mazama erupted and collapsed. Rain and snow filled the caldera to form Crater Lake, 1,943 feet deep—the deepest lake in the United States—with exceptionally clear, deep-blue water. The 33-mile Rim Drive has more than 30 overlooks and is usually fully open from mid-July to late October. Winter brings an average of about 43 feet of snow, and you can drive only as far as Rim Village. The Cleetwood Cove Trail, the only route down to the water, is closed for reconstruction in 2026–2028; during that time there are no boat tours on the lake and no trips to Wizard Island.",
  "7–9 月环湖公路和步道基本全开；6 月、10 月常有路段或步道因雪未开，冬春（约 11–5 月）只能开到 Rim Village。": "July–September, Rim Drive and the trails are mostly open. In June and October, snow often keeps some road sections or trails closed. In winter and spring (about November–May) you can drive only as far as Rim Village.",
  "Rim Village / 公园总部": "Rim Village / park headquarters",
  "西环湖路": "West Rim Drive",
  "东环湖路北段": "East Rim Drive (north)",
  "东环湖路南段": "East Rim Drive (south)",
  "园内只有两处住宿：湖边的 Crater Lake Lodge（约 5 月中到 10 月中）和南入口附近的 Mazama Village 木屋（约 5 月下旬到 9 月底），都可提前 365 天预订，暑期往往几个月前就订满。园外最近的是南边的 Fort Klamath 和西边的 Union Creek、Prospect（到 Rim Village 约 40–60 分钟），北入口开放时也可以住 Diamond Lake；酒店多、价格低的是 Klamath Falls（约 1 小时 15 分）和机场所在的 Medford（约 1 小时 45 分）。": "The park has only two places to stay: Crater Lake Lodge on the rim (about mid-May to mid-October) and the Cabins at Mazama Village near the south entrance (about late May to late September). Both take reservations 365 days ahead, and summer dates often sell out months in advance. The nearest towns outside the park are Fort Klamath to the south and Union Creek and Prospect to the west (about 40–60 minutes to Rim Village); when the north entrance is open, you can also stay at Diamond Lake. For more hotels at lower prices, try Klamath Falls (about 1 hour 15 minutes) or Medford, with its airport (about 1 hour 45 minutes).",
  "雷尼尔山": "Mount Rainier",
  "冰川火山与野花草甸": "Glaciated volcano and wildflower meadows",
  "海拔 4,392 米的雷尼尔山是一座活火山，也是美国本土冰川最多的山峰。夏天南坡的 Paradise 和东北坡的 Sunrise 是两大看山区，7 月下旬到 8 月高山草甸野花最盛；Paradise 冬天也开放，可以玩雪、走雪鞋。离西雅图约 2 小时车程。": "At 14,410 feet, Mount Rainier is an active volcano and the most glaciated peak in the contiguous United States. In summer the two main viewing areas are Paradise on the south side and Sunrise on the northeast side. Subalpine wildflowers peak from late July through August. Paradise is open in winter too, for snow play and snowshoeing. The park is about two hours from Seattle.",
  "7–9 月道路全开、步道化雪，7 月下旬到 8 月野花最盛；冬季只有 Longmire 到 Paradise 的路白天开放，要带雪链。": "July–September, all roads are open and the trails are snow-free; wildflowers peak from late July through August. In winter, only the road from Longmire to Paradise is open, during daytime hours, and you must carry tire chains.",
  "Longmire（西南入口）": "Longmire (southwest entrance)",
  "Paradise（天堂区）": "Paradise",
  "Stevens Canyon / Ohanapecosh（东南）": "Stevens Canyon / Ohanapecosh (southeast)",
  "Chinook Pass（东侧 410 号公路）": "Chinook Pass (Highway 410, east side)",
  "Sunrise / White River（东北）": "Sunrise / White River (northeast)",
  "天堂游客中心（Paradise）": "Paradise Visitor Center",
  "园内只有两家酒店：Paradise 的 Paradise Inn（约 5 月中到 10 月初营业）和 Longmire 的 National Park Inn（全年营业，只有 25 间房），都要尽早订。园外最方便的是西南入口外的 Ashford，到 Paradise 约 1 小时；东南方向的 Packwood 离 Ohanapecosh 近；去 Sunrise 可以住东北方向的 Crystal Mountain 或 Enumclaw。": "The park has just two hotels: Paradise Inn at Paradise (open about mid-May to early October) and the National Park Inn at Longmire (open year-round, only 25 rooms). Book both as early as you can. The most convenient town is Ashford, outside the southwest entrance, about an hour from Paradise. Packwood, to the southeast, is close to Ohanapecosh. For Sunrise, stay northeast at Crystal Mountain or in Enumclaw.",
  "奥林匹克": "Olympic",
  "雪山、雨林与荒野海岸": "Glaciated peaks, rain forest, and wild coast",
  "一个公园里有三种完全不同的风景：飓风岭上的冰川雪峰、西侧年降水量 3 米多的温带雨林，以及立着海蚀柱、堆满漂流木的荒野海岸。园内没有横穿的公路，景点散落在环绕半岛的 101 号公路两侧，片区之间常要开一两个小时。": "Three completely different landscapes in one park: glaciated peaks along Hurricane Ridge, temperate rain forest on the west side that gets more than 10 feet of precipitation a year, and a wild coastline of sea stacks and piled driftwood. No road crosses the park. The sights are scattered along U.S. 101, which loops around the peninsula, and driving between areas often takes an hour or two.",
  "7–9 月最干爽、高山步道也通了；10–5 月多雨，飓风岭冬季一般只在周五到周日开放。": "July–September is driest, and the high trails are open. October–May is rainy; in winter, Hurricane Ridge is generally open only Friday–Sunday.",
  "飓风岭 / 天使港": "Hurricane Ridge / Port Angeles",
  "新月湖 / Sol Duc": "Lake Crescent / Sol Duc",
  "北部海岸（La Push / Rialto）": "North coast (La Push / Rialto Beach)",
  "霍河雨林": "Hoh Rain Forest",
  "Kalaloch / 红宝石海滩": "Kalaloch / Ruby Beach",
  "奥林匹克国家公园游客中心（天使港）": "Olympic National Park Visitor Center (Port Angeles)",
  "公园很大、没有横穿的公路，大多数人沿 101 号公路环线每一两晚换一个住处：北边住天使港或新月湖边的 Lake Crescent Lodge、Log Cabin Resort（Sol Duc 温泉度假村在旁边的山谷里），西边以 Forks 为据点去 La Push 海滩和霍河雨林，海边有 Kalaloch Lodge，南边住奎诺尔特湖旅馆。园内几家除 Kalaloch Lodge 外都是季节性营业，夏季要早订。": "The park is big and no road crosses it, so most people drive the U.S. 101 loop and move every night or two. In the north, stay in Port Angeles or on Lake Crescent at Lake Crescent Lodge or Log Cabin Resort (Sol Duc Hot Springs Resort is in the next valley). In the west, base yourself in Forks for La Push beaches and the Hoh Rain Forest; Kalaloch Lodge sits right on the coast. In the south, stay at Lake Quinault Lodge. Except for Kalaloch Lodge, the in-park lodges are seasonal; book early for summer.",
  "北瀑布": "North Cascades",
  "冰川雪峰与碧绿湖水": "Glaciated peaks and turquoise lakes",
  "华盛顿州北部的冰川山地，有 300 多条冰川，是阿拉斯加以外美国冰川最多的地方，锯齿状雪峰下是被冰川细粉染成碧绿色的迪亚布洛湖。园区几乎没有公路，大多数人沿 20 号公路（North Cascades Highway）自驾，在观景台和步道口停车游览，不收门票。东侧的 Rainy Pass、Washington Pass 属于国家森林，但通常和公园一起玩。": "Glacier-covered mountains in northern Washington, with more than 300 glaciers—more than anywhere in the United States outside Alaska. Below the jagged peaks, Diablo Lake is colored turquoise by fine glacial flour. There are almost no roads in the park. Most people drive Highway 20 (the North Cascades Highway) and stop at overlooks and trailheads. There's no entrance fee. Rainy Pass and Washington Pass, on the east side, are in the national forest but are usually visited along with the park.",
  "7–9 月高山步道无雪最好走，9 月底到 10 月中旬看金色落叶松；20 号公路中段冬季封闭（约 11 月底至次年 4–5 月）。": "July–September, the high trails are snow-free and easiest to hike. From late September to mid-October, the larches turn gold. The middle section of Highway 20 closes in winter (about late November to April or May).",
  "Newhalem（游客中心）": "Newhalem (visitor center)",
  "迪亚布洛湖 · 罗斯湖": "Diablo Lake / Ross Lake",
  "东侧山口（Rainy / Washington Pass）": "East-side passes (Rainy Pass / Washington Pass)",
  "北瀑布游客中心（Newhalem）": "North Cascades Visitor Center (Newhalem)",
  "园内能住的只有 Ross Lake Resort 的湖上木屋（6–10 月营业，没有车道，靠老客续订和抽签，很难订到）和环境学习中心特定日期的活动住宿；大多数人住西侧的 Marblemount 或 Concrete，到 Newhalem 约 20–40 分钟。20 号公路开通期间（约 5–11 月），东侧的 Mazama 和西部风情小镇 Winthrop 住宿更多，适合单独留一天玩东侧山口；园区内没有加油站。": "The only lodging in the park is the floating cabins at Ross Lake Resort (open June–October, no road access, mostly rebooked by returning guests or awarded by lottery, so very hard to get) and program-based stays on certain dates at the Environmental Learning Center. Most people stay west of the park in Marblemount or Concrete, about 20–40 minutes from Newhalem. While Highway 20 is open (about May–November), Mazama and the Old West–style town of Winthrop on the east side have more lodging—good for a separate day on the east-side passes. There are no gas stations in the park.",
  "黄石": "Yellowstone",
  "间歇泉、温泉与野生动物": "Geysers, hot springs, and wildlife",
  "1872 年设立的世界第一座国家公园，坐落在世界上最大的活火山之一上：全世界一半以上的间歇泉都在这里，老忠实间歇泉、大棱镜温泉和猛犸温泉阶地是招牌。黄石大峡谷和下瀑布、北美高海拔最大的黄石湖，以及拉马尔谷、海登谷里的野牛、狼和熊，同样值得专程来看。主环线约 229 公里、呈“8”字形，景点分散，建议至少留 3 天。": "Established in 1872 as the world's first national park, Yellowstone sits atop one of the largest active volcanoes on Earth. More than half the world's geysers are here; Old Faithful, Grand Prismatic Spring, and Mammoth Hot Springs Terraces are the headliners. The Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone and its Lower Falls, Yellowstone Lake (the largest high-elevation lake in North America), and the bison, wolves, and bears of Lamar Valley and Hayden Valley are just as worth the trip. The main road is a figure-eight loop of about 142 miles, and the sights are spread out; plan on at least three days.",
  "6–9 月道路和设施全开，9 月人少还能看马鹿发情；11 月到次年 4 月中旬，除北门到东北门一段外道路不通私家车，冬天只能坐雪地车进园。": "June–September, all roads and facilities are open; in September it's quieter and you can watch the elk rut. From November to mid-April, roads are closed to private vehicles except the stretch from the North Entrance to the Northeast Entrance; in winter, you can enter the interior only by snowcoach.",
  "间歇泉盆地（老忠实）": "Geyser basins (Old Faithful)",
  "诺里斯 / 麦迪逊": "Norris / Madison",
  "猛犸温泉（北门）": "Mammoth Hot Springs (North Entrance)",
  "拉马尔谷 / 东北角": "Lamar Valley / northeast",
  "黄石大峡谷": "Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone",
  "海登谷 / 黄石湖": "Hayden Valley / Yellowstone Lake",
  "峡谷村（Canyon Village）": "Canyon Village",
  "园内酒店分散在老忠实、峡谷村、湖区、猛犸温泉和 Grant Village，除猛犸温泉酒店和 Snow Lodge 外大多只在 5 月到 10 月初营业，通常提前一年左右开放预订、旺季很快订满；按路线分两三处住，能少走很多回头路。园外最方便的是西门外的 West Yellowstone（离间歇泉盆地近）和北门外的 Gardiner（全年通车）；清晨去拉马尔谷看狼可以住东北门外的 Cooke City / Silver Gate，和大提顿连着玩就住 Grant Village 或南边的 Jackson。": "In-park hotels are spread among Old Faithful, Canyon Village, the Lake area, Mammoth Hot Springs, and Grant Village. Except for Mammoth Hot Springs Hotel and Old Faithful Snow Lodge, most are open only from May to early October. Reservations usually open about a year ahead and fill quickly in peak season. Splitting your stay between two or three locations along your route saves a lot of backtracking. The most convenient gateway towns are West Yellowstone, outside the West Entrance (close to the geyser basins), and Gardiner, outside the North Entrance (open to cars year-round). For dawn wolf-watching in Lamar Valley, stay in Cooke City / Silver Gate outside the Northeast Entrance. If you're combining the trip with Grand Teton, stay at Grant Village or in Jackson to the south.",
  "大提顿": "Grand Teton",
  "拔地而起的雪峰与湖泊": "Peaks rising straight from the lakes",
  "提顿山脉没有山麓缓坡，从 Jackson Hole 谷底直接拔起 2,000 多米，主峰 Grand Teton 海拔 4,199 米，山脚下串着珍妮湖、弦湖、杰克逊湖等冰川湖。公园不大，一个环线就能看到大部分景点：西边的 Teton Park Road 贴着山脚走，东边的 191 号公路沿蛇河经过摩门街谷仓和施瓦巴赫码头。北边经洛克菲勒纪念公园路直通黄石南门，大多数人把两个公园连在一起玩。": "The Teton Range has no foothills: it rises more than 6,500 feet straight from the floor of Jackson Hole to the 13,775-foot summit of Grand Teton. Glacial lakes—Jenny, String, Jackson, and others—line the base of the mountains. The park is compact, and one loop covers most of the sights: Teton Park Road on the west hugs the foot of the range, and U.S. 191 on the east follows the Snake River past the Mormon Row barns and Schwabacher Landing. To the north, the John D. Rockefeller, Jr. Memorial Parkway leads straight to Yellowstone's South Entrance, and most people visit the two parks together.",
  "6–9 月道路、渡船和园内住宿全开，9 月底到 10 月初山杨金黄、马鹿发情；11 月到次年 4 月 Teton Park Road 北段不通车，只能滑雪或穿雪鞋。": "June–September, the roads, the Jenny Lake boat shuttle, and in-park lodging are all open. In late September and early October, the aspens turn gold and the elk rut. From November through April, the northern section of Teton Park Road is closed to cars; you can travel it only on skis or snowshoes.",
  "Moose / Moose-Wilson 路": "Moose / Moose-Wilson Road",
  "珍妮湖 / Teton Park Road": "Jenny Lake / Teton Park Road",
  "杰克逊湖 / Colter Bay": "Jackson Lake / Colter Bay",
  "191 号公路 / 蛇河沿岸": "U.S. 191 / Snake River",
  "Jackson 镇 / Teton Village（园外）": "Jackson / Teton Village (outside the park)",
  "克雷格·托马斯游客中心（Moose）": "Craig Thomas Discovery and Visitor Center (Moose)",
  "园内住宿都只在约 5 月中到 10 月初营业：杰克逊湖边的 Jackson Lake Lodge、Signal Mountain Lodge 和 Colter Bay 木屋（相对便宜），珍妮湖边的 Jenny Lake Lodge 最贵但含早晚餐，都提前约一年开放预订、旺季很快订满。园外最方便的是南边的 Jackson 镇（到珍妮湖约 40 分钟），但房价很高；想省钱或一家人租整套房子，可以翻过 Teton Pass 住爱达荷州的 Victor / Driggs，或往南住 Alpine。和黄石连着玩，可以在北边的 Colter Bay、Headwaters（Flagg Ranch）或 Buffalo Valley 住一晚，第二天一早从南门进黄石。": "All in-park lodging is open only from about mid-May to early October: Jackson Lake Lodge, Signal Mountain Lodge, and the Colter Bay cabins (relatively affordable) on Jackson Lake, and Jenny Lake Lodge, the most expensive, with breakfast and dinner included. Reservations open about a year ahead and fill quickly in peak season. The most convenient town is Jackson to the south (about 40 minutes to Jenny Lake), but rooms are very expensive. To save money, or to rent a whole house for a family, cross Teton Pass to Victor or Driggs in Idaho, or head south to Alpine. If you're continuing to Yellowstone, spend a night to the north at Colter Bay, Headwaters (Flagg Ranch), or Buffalo Valley and enter Yellowstone's South Entrance first thing in the morning.",
  "冰川": "Glacier",
  "冰川湖与向阳大道": "Glacial lakes and Going-to-the-Sun Road",
  "1910 年设立，号称“大陆之冠”（Crown of the Continent）：冰川在落基山北段刨出锯齿状的山峰、U 形谷和一串串碧绿的湖，园内还剩二十多条小冰川，正在快速消退。招牌是约 80 公里长的向阳大道（Going-to-the-Sun Road），贴着崖壁翻过大陆分水岭上的洛根山口；东侧的 Many Glacier 步道最精彩，灰熊、雪山羊和大角羊都很常见。2026 年进园不用预约，但 7 月 1 日到 9 月 7 日洛根山口私家车限停 3 小时，走高线步道这类长线要提前订班车票。": "Established in 1910 and known as the Crown of the Continent. Glaciers carved the northern Rockies here into jagged peaks, U-shaped valleys, and strings of turquoise lakes; a couple dozen small glaciers remain and are shrinking fast. The headliner is the roughly 50-mile Going-to-the-Sun Road, which clings to cliffs as it crosses the Continental Divide at Logan Pass. Many Glacier, on the east side, has the best trails, and grizzlies, mountain goats, and bighorn sheep are common. No entry reservation is required in 2026, but from July 1 to September 7, private vehicles at Logan Pass are limited to three hours of parking; for long hikes like the Highline Trail, book a shuttle ticket in advance.",
  "7 月到 9 月上旬向阳大道全线通车、高处步道的雪基本化完，是最好的季节；9 月中下旬人少，但园内酒店和游船陆续停业；10 月下旬到次年 6 月洛根山口封路，只能在西侧麦克唐纳湖一带和 2 号公路沿线活动。": "July to early September is the best season: Going-to-the-Sun Road is fully open and the snow has mostly melted from the high trails. Mid- to late September is quieter, but in-park hotels and boat tours begin shutting down. From late October to June, Logan Pass is closed, and you're limited to the Lake McDonald area on the west side and the U.S. 2 corridor.",
  "西侧 · 麦克唐纳湖": "West: Lake McDonald",
  "向阳大道 · 洛根山口": "Going-to-the-Sun Road / Logan Pass",
  "东侧 · 圣玛丽湖": "East: St. Mary Lake",
  "Many Glacier 山谷": "Many Glacier Valley",
  "双药湖 · 2 号公路": "Two Medicine / U.S. 2",
  "北岔 · 鲍曼湖": "North Fork / Bowman Lake",
  "Apgar 游客中心（西门）": "Apgar Visitor Center (West Entrance)",
  "园内酒店都只在夏季营业（2026 年大多 5 月中到 6 月上旬开门、9 月中下旬关门），每月 1 日开放下一年同月的预订，热门日期很快订满：西侧是湖边的 Lake McDonald Lodge 和 Apgar 村，东侧是 Many Glacier Hotel、Swiftcurrent Motor Inn 和 Rising Sun。园外西边的 West Glacier 离西门最近，Columbia Falls、Whitefish、Kalispell 选择多、价格低，到西门 25–50 分钟；东边只有 St. Mary、Babb 和 East Glacier Park 几个小地方，住处少、要早订。东西两侧之间开车要 1.5–2.5 小时，最好两边各住几晚。": "All in-park hotels are open only in summer (in 2026 most open between mid-May and early June and close in mid- to late September). Reservations for a given month open on the 1st of that month a year ahead, and popular dates fill fast. On the west side are Lake McDonald Lodge and Apgar Village; on the east side, Many Glacier Hotel, Swiftcurrent Motor Inn, and Rising Sun. Outside the park, West Glacier is closest to the West Entrance, while Columbia Falls, Whitefish, and Kalispell have more options at lower prices, 25–50 minutes away. On the east side there are only small places—St. Mary, Babb, and East Glacier Park—with few rooms, so book early. Driving between the east and west sides takes 1.5–2.5 hours, so it's best to spend a few nights on each side.",
  "落基山": "Rocky Mountain",
  "高山苔原与大陆分水岭": "Alpine tundra and the Continental Divide",
  "落基山脉的主脊从公园中间穿过，约三分之一的面积在林线以上。Trail Ridge Road 是美国海拔最高的连续铺装公路（最高约 3,713 米），夏秋翻过大陆分水岭，连起东边的 Estes Park 和西边的 Grand Lake；东侧 Bear Lake 路一带有一串高山湖泊，草甸上常见麋鹿，西侧河谷能看到驼鹿。2026 年 5 月 22 日到 10 月中旬白天进园要提前在 Recreation.gov 预约时段，去 Bear Lake 路还要选含 Bear Lake 路的那一种。": "The crest of the Rockies runs through the middle of the park, and about a third of it lies above tree line. Trail Ridge Road, the highest continuous paved road in the United States (topping out at about 12,180 feet), crosses the Continental Divide in summer and fall, linking Estes Park on the east with Grand Lake on the west. On the east side, the Bear Lake Road corridor has a string of alpine lakes, and elk are common in the meadows; in the river valleys on the west side you can see moose. From May 22 to mid-October 2026, daytime entry requires a timed-entry reservation on Recreation.gov; for Bear Lake Road, you need the type that includes the Bear Lake Road corridor.",
  "6 月下旬到 9 月 Trail Ridge Road 全线通车、苔原开花，7–8 月午后常有雷暴；9 月中下旬山杨变黄、麋鹿发情，最热门；Trail Ridge 约 10 月中下旬到次年 5 月底封路，冬天只能在东西两侧的低处活动。": "From late June through September, Trail Ridge Road is fully open and the tundra is in bloom; July–August often brings afternoon thunderstorms. Mid- to late September, when the aspens turn and the elk rut, is the busiest time. Trail Ridge Road closes from about mid- to late October until late May; in winter, you're limited to the lower elevations on the east and west sides.",
  "东侧 · Beaver Meadows / Horseshoe Park": "East: Beaver Meadows / Horseshoe Park",
  "Bear Lake 路（熊湖走廊）": "Bear Lake Road corridor",
  "Trail Ridge Road 高山段": "Trail Ridge Road (alpine section)",
  "西侧 · Grand Lake / Kawuneeche 河谷": "West: Grand Lake / Kawuneeche Valley",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Moraine Park、Glacier Basin、Aspenglen、Timber Creek 等露营地（在 recreation.gov 订，营地预约自带入住当天下午起的进园时段，常常一开放就订满）。大多数人住东门外的 Estes Park：酒店、木屋和餐厅最多，到 Beaver Meadows 入口约 10 分钟，6–9 月和麋鹿季的周末要提前几个月订；想横穿 Trail Ridge Road 就在西边的 Grand Lake 住一晚，再便宜些住 Granby。丹佛机场进出的第一晚、最后一晚可以住 Boulder 或丹佛。": "There are no hotels in the park, only campgrounds such as Moraine Park, Glacier Basin, Aspenglen, and Timber Creek (book on Recreation.gov; a campground reservation includes park entry from the afternoon of your arrival day, and sites often sell out as soon as they open). Most people stay in Estes Park, outside the east entrance, which has the most hotels, cabins, and restaurants, about 10 minutes from the Beaver Meadows Entrance; for June–September and elk-season weekends, book months ahead. To drive across Trail Ridge Road, spend a night in Grand Lake on the west side, or in cheaper Granby. If you're flying in and out of Denver, you can spend the first and last nights in Boulder or Denver.",
  "梅萨维德": "Mesa Verde",
  "悬崖上的古村落": "Cliff dwellings in the canyon walls",
  "科罗拉多西南角的一块大台地。古普韦布洛人（Ancestral Pueblo）在这里生活了七百多年，先住台地顶的半地穴屋和村落，最后约一百年把村子建进峡谷崖壁的岩洞里，留下悬崖宫殿等约 600 处崖居，是世界文化遗产。几处大崖居只能跟护林员导览进去（约 5–10 月，提前 14 天在 Recreation.gov 抢票），其余时间可以在台地顶环路的观景台隔着峡谷看；从入口到崖居集中的 Chapin Mesa 要开约 45 分钟山路，西侧的 Wetherill Mesa 只在夏秋开放。": "A broad mesa in the southwest corner of Colorado. Ancestral Pueblo people lived here for more than 700 years, first in pithouses and villages on the mesa tops, then, for roughly the last century, in villages built into alcoves in the canyon walls. They left about 600 cliff dwellings, including Cliff Palace, and the park is a World Heritage Site. A few of the large cliff dwellings can be entered only on ranger-led tours (about May–October; tickets go on sale on Recreation.gov 14 days ahead and go fast). The rest of the year you can view them across the canyons from overlooks on Mesa Top Loop. Chapin Mesa, where most of the cliff dwellings are, is about a 45-minute mountain drive from the entrance; Wetherill Mesa, on the west side, is open only in summer and fall.",
  "5 月初到 10 月下旬有崖居导览（2026 年 5 月 4 日–10 月 21 日），5–6 月和 9–10 月最舒服；7–8 月白天热、午后多雷雨；11 月到次年 4 月导览、Wetherill Mesa 和园内住宿都关闭，只能看台地顶环路、博物馆和云杉树屋观景台。": "Cliff dwelling tours run from early May to late October (May 4–October 21, 2026). May–June and September–October are most comfortable. July–August days are hot, with frequent afternoon thunderstorms. From November through April, the tours, Wetherill Mesa, and in-park lodging all close; you can still drive Mesa Top Loop, visit the museum, and see Spruce Tree House from the overlook.",
  "入口 · Morefield 营地": "Entrance / Morefield Campground",
  "Chapin Mesa 博物馆区": "Chapin Mesa museum area",
  "台地顶环路（Mesa Top Loop）": "Mesa Top Loop",
  "悬崖宫殿环路（Cliff Palace Loop）": "Cliff Palace Loop",
  "Wetherill Mesa（西侧台地）": "Wetherill Mesa (west)",
  "梅萨维德游客与研究中心（入口）": "Mesa Verde Visitor and Research Center (entrance)",
  "园内唯一的酒店是 Far View Lodge（2026 年 4 月 17 日–10 月 18 日营业），离崖居最近、夏天要早订；入口进来约 6.5 公里的 Morefield 营地有 267 个营位（约 4 月下旬到 10 月中旬）。多数人住西边约 15 分钟车程的 Cortez（连锁酒店、超市多）或东边的 Mancos 小镇，想住河边小木屋可以看北边的 Dolores；从杜兰戈机场进出就住 Durango（到入口约 45 分钟）。冬天园内没有住宿，只能住园外。": "The only hotel in the park is Far View Lodge (open April 17–October 18, 2026), the closest lodging to the cliff dwellings; book early for summer. Morefield Campground, about 4 miles in from the entrance, has 267 sites (about late April to mid-October). Most people stay in Cortez, about 15 minutes west, with plenty of chain hotels and supermarkets, or in the small town of Mancos to the east. For a riverside cabin, look north in Dolores. If you're flying in and out of Durango, stay in Durango (about 45 minutes to the entrance). There's no in-park lodging in winter.",
  "大沙丘": "Great Sand Dunes",
  "北美最高的沙丘": "The tallest dunes in North America",
  "科罗拉多南部圣路易斯谷的东缘，风把谷地里的沙子一路吹到桑格雷-德克里斯托山（Sangre de Cristo）脚下，堆成约 78 平方公里的沙丘区：最高的星形沙丘（Star Dune）和 Hidden Dune 从底到顶约 225 米，是北美最高的沙丘，背后就是 4,000 米级的雪山。沙丘里没有步道，可以随便爬、随便滑沙；春末融雪时，沙丘脚下的梅达诺溪（Medano Creek）漫成一片浅浅的“沙滩”，还会冲起一波波小浪。公园海拔约 2,500 米，24 小时开放、不用预约，也是国际暗夜公园，沙丘后面的国家保护区一直延伸到高山湖泊和苔原。": "On the eastern edge of the San Luis Valley in southern Colorado, wind has swept sand across the valley floor and piled it against the foot of the Sangre de Cristo Mountains, forming a dunefield of about 30 square miles. The tallest, Star Dune and Hidden Dune, rise about 740 feet from base to crest—the tallest dunes in North America—backed by snowcapped 13,000-foot peaks. There are no trails on the dunes; climb and sandboard wherever you like. In late spring, snowmelt spreads Medano Creek into a wide, shallow “beach” at the foot of the dunes, with little waves pulsing downstream. The park sits at about 8,200 feet, is open 24 hours with no reservation needed, and is an International Dark Sky Park. The national preserve behind the dunes stretches up to alpine lakes and tundra.",
  "5 月下旬到 6 月初梅达诺溪水最大、人也最多；7–8 月午后沙面能到 65°C 以上、常有雷暴，只能清早或傍晚上沙丘；9 月到 10 月上旬天气最稳、山杨变黄；3–5 月午后风大扬沙，冬天夜里常冷到零下十几度，沙丘上不时积一层薄雪。": "Medano Creek runs highest from late May to early June, which is also the busiest time. In July–August the sand surface can top 150°F in the afternoon, and thunderstorms are common; go onto the dunes only early or late in the day. September to early October has the most stable weather, and the aspens turn gold. March–May afternoons are windy, with blowing sand. Winter nights often drop to the single digits Fahrenheit or below, and a thin layer of snow sometimes covers the dunes.",
  "游客中心 · 莫斯卡山口步道": "Visitor center / Mosca Pass Trail",
  "沙丘区 · 梅达诺溪（Dunes Parking Area）": "Dunefield / Medano Creek (Dunes Parking Area)",
  "梅达诺山口四驱路 · 东侧沙丘": "Medano Pass Primitive Road / east-side dunes",
  "园外南侧 · 萨帕塔瀑布（BLM）": "South of the park: Zapata Falls (BLM)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Piñon Flats 营地（4–10 月，Recreation.gov 提前 3 个月放出，5–6 月几乎天天订满）。离沙丘最近的是入口外约 6 公里的 Great Sand Dunes Lodge（约 3 月中到 10 月）和 Oasis 的木屋、营地（4–10 月，只能打电话订），旺季要早订；酒店、超市最多的是约 45 分钟车程的 Alamosa。想住整栋民宿可以看公园南边 Zapata Falls 一带的木屋（Airbnb 上多写 Mosca），从东边过来也可以住 Fort Garland。": "There are no hotels in the park, only Piñon Flats Campground (April–October; sites open on Recreation.gov three months ahead and are booked nearly every night in May–June). The closest lodging is the Great Sand Dunes Lodge, about 4 miles outside the entrance (about mid-March to October), and the cabins and campground at the Oasis (April–October, phone reservations only); book early in peak season. Alamosa, about 45 minutes away, has the most hotels and supermarkets. For a whole-house rental, look at the cabins near Zapata Falls, south of the park (often listed on Airbnb as Mosca). Coming from the east, you can also stay in Fort Garland.",
  "甘尼森黑峡谷": "Black Canyon of the Gunnison",
  "又深又窄的黑色峡谷": "A deep, narrow, dark canyon",
  "甘尼森河用两百多万年，在约 17 亿年前形成的坚硬片麻岩里切出这道峡谷：最深处约 830 米，最窄处谷底只有约 12 米宽，有的地段一天只照到半小时左右的太阳，崖壁总显得发黑，因此得名。南缘有约 11 公里的铺装观景路和十几个观景台，能看到科罗拉多州最高的悬崖彩绘崖壁；北缘是砂石路，更偏、更安静。两缘之间没有桥，开车绕园外要 2 小时以上。": "Over more than 2 million years, the Gunnison River cut this canyon into hard gneiss formed about 1.7 billion years ago. At its deepest it's about 2,720 feet deep, and at its narrowest the canyon floor is only about 40 feet wide. Some stretches get only about half an hour of sun a day, so the walls always look dark—hence the name. The South Rim has a paved scenic drive of about 7 miles with a dozen or so overlooks, including views of the Painted Wall, the tallest cliff in Colorado. The North Rim is reached by gravel road and is more remote and quieter. There's no bridge between the rims; driving around outside the park takes more than two hours.",
  "5–6 月和 9–10 月最舒服；7–8 月白天热、午后常有雷暴；冬天南缘公路只铲雪到游客中心（其余改成滑雪、雪鞋道），北缘和谷底 East Portal 的路封闭，4 月中旬到 5 月初陆续开通。": "May–June and September–October are most comfortable. July–August days are hot, with frequent afternoon thunderstorms. In winter, South Rim Road is plowed only to the visitor center (the rest becomes a ski and snowshoe route), and the North Rim road and East Portal Road down to the river are closed; they reopen in stages from mid-April to early May.",
  "南缘 · 游客中心一带": "South Rim: visitor center area",
  "南缘观景路（游客中心以西）": "South Rim Road (west of the visitor center)",
  "East Portal（谷底河边）": "East Portal (river level)",
  "北缘": "North Rim",
  "南缘游客中心": "South Rim Visitor Center",
  "园内没有酒店，只有三个小营地：南缘营地只能在 Recreation.gov 预约（2025 年山火后 2026 年只开 25 个营位），北缘和谷底 East Portal 的营地先到先得。多数人住西边约 25 分钟车程的 Montrose，连锁酒店、超市最多，一般提前几周订就够；想住山城可以选南边约 1 小时 10 分的 Ouray，或半路上整栋民宿多的 Ridgway，从东边过来可以住约 1 小时 15 分的 Gunnison。去北缘就住 Crawford 一带，旅馆很少，要早订。": "There are no hotels in the park, only three small campgrounds. South Rim Campground is reservable only on Recreation.gov (after the 2025 wildfire, only 25 sites are open in 2026); the North Rim and East Portal campgrounds are first come, first served. Most people stay in Montrose, about 25 minutes west, which has the most chain hotels and supermarkets; booking a few weeks ahead is usually enough. For a mountain town, try Ouray, about 1 hour 10 minutes south, or Ridgway on the way, which has lots of vacation rentals. Coming from the east, you can stay in Gunnison, about 1 hour 15 minutes away. For the North Rim, stay around Crawford; lodging is scarce, so book early.",
  "死亡谷": "Death Valley",
  "北美最低、最热、最干燥": "Lowest, hottest, and driest in North America",
  "北美最低、最热、最干的地方，Badwater 盐滩低于海平面 86 米。最佳季节是 11 月到 3 月；夏天白天常超过 46°C，只适合清晨开车看景。园内加油点少、油价贵，充电只有慢充。": "The lowest, hottest, driest place in North America: Badwater Basin lies 282 feet below sea level. The best season is November–March. Summer days often top 115°F; sightseeing is only practical by car in the early morning. Gas stations in the park are few and expensive, and EV charging is slow (Level 2) only.",
  "11–3 月气温舒适；夏天酷热，只适合清晨开车看景。": "November–March is pleasant. Summer is brutally hot; sightsee by car in the early morning only.",
  "Badwater Road 沿线": "Badwater Road",
  "北部（Ubehebe）": "North (Ubehebe)",
  "西部（Panamint）": "West (Panamint)",
  "园内住宿集中在 Furnace Creek（The Inn、The Ranch）和 Stovepipe Wells，西边还有 Panamint Springs；预算有限可以住园外的 Beatty 或 Pahrump（内华达），但每天要多开一两个小时。夏天园内酒店不贵但非常热。": "In-park lodging is concentrated at Furnace Creek (The Inn and The Ranch) and Stovepipe Wells, with Panamint Springs farther west. On a budget, stay outside the park in Beatty or Pahrump (Nevada), but expect an extra hour or two of driving each day. In summer the in-park hotels are inexpensive but extremely hot.",
  "锡安": "Zion",
  "红色峡谷与天使降临": "Red canyons and Angels Landing",
  "在红色砂岩峡谷底部，抬头看 600 多米高的岩壁。招牌是天使降临（需要许可证）和窄缝（在维珍河里逆流徒步）。主峡谷大部分时间只能坐免费班车，停车是最大难题。": "Stand on the floor of a red sandstone canyon and look up at walls more than 2,000 feet high. The headliners are Angels Landing (permit required) and The Narrows (hiking upstream in the Virgin River). Most of the year, the main canyon is reachable only by free shuttle, and parking is the biggest challenge.",
  "春秋最舒服；夏天炎热、7–9 月有山洪，窄缝 6–10 月水温合适。": "Spring and fall are most comfortable. Summer is hot, and flash floods are a risk July–September. Water temperatures in The Narrows are best June–October.",
  "锡安峡谷（班车区）": "Zion Canyon (shuttle area)",
  "南入口 / Springdale": "South Entrance / Springdale",
  "东侧（隧道以东）": "East side (beyond the tunnel)",
  "Kolob 峡谷": "Kolob Canyons",
  "锡安峡谷游客中心": "Zion Canyon Visitor Center",
  "园内只有 Zion Lodge 一家酒店，很难订；大多数人住南门外的 Springdale，走路或坐镇上的免费班车就能到游客中心。更便宜的在 Hurricane、St. George；要顺路去布莱斯或大峡谷北缘的话，东边的 Kanab 也方便。": "Zion Lodge is the only hotel in the park and is hard to book. Most people stay in Springdale, outside the South Entrance, and walk or take the town's free shuttle to the visitor center. Hurricane and St. George are cheaper. If you're continuing to Bryce Canyon or the Grand Canyon's North Rim, Kanab to the east is also convenient.",
  "布莱斯峡谷": "Bryce Canyon",
  "岩柱林立的圆形剧场": "Amphitheaters full of hoodoos",
  "其实不是峡谷，而是高原边缘被侵蚀出的一连串“圆形剧场”，里面站满了叫 hoodoo 的石柱，密度世界第一。海拔 2,400–2,800 米，夏天凉快、冬天积雪；也是国际暗夜公园，星空极好。": "Not actually a canyon, but a series of “amphitheaters” eroded into the edge of a plateau and packed with rock spires called hoodoos—the highest concentration in the world. At 8,000–9,100 feet, it's cool in summer and snowy in winter. It's also an International Dark Sky Park with superb stargazing.",
  "高海拔夏天也凉快；冬天常有雪，雪中石林很美。": "The high elevation keeps summers cool. Winter often brings snow, and the hoodoos are beautiful under it.",
  "布莱斯圆形剧场": "Bryce Amphitheater",
  "南段景观道": "Southern Scenic Drive",
  "12 号公路": "Highway 12",
  "布莱斯峡谷游客中心": "Bryce Canyon Visitor Center",
  "园内只有 The Lodge at Bryce Canyon；门口的 Bryce Canyon City（Ruby's Inn 一带）选择最多，离日出点约 10 分钟车程。东边的 Tropic、北边的 Panguitch 价格更低。": "The Lodge at Bryce Canyon is the only in-park hotel. Bryce Canyon City, just outside (around Ruby's Inn), has the most choices, about 10 minutes from Sunrise Point. Tropic to the east and Panguitch to the north are cheaper.",
  "大峡谷": "Grand Canyon",
  "二十亿年的地层": "Two billion years of rock",
  "科罗拉多河切出的约 1.6 公里深的大峡谷，从南缘看出去是近 20 亿年的岩层，日出日落时颜色变化最大。南缘全年开放、设施齐全；北缘只在夏秋开放，2025 年山火烧毁了北缘的 Grand Canyon Lodge，2026 年北缘没有住宿、饮用水和加油。": "The Colorado River carved this canyon about a mile deep; from the South Rim you look across rock layers spanning nearly 2 billion years, with the colors shifting most at sunrise and sunset. The South Rim is open year-round with full services. The North Rim is open only in summer and fall; the 2025 wildfire destroyed the North Rim's Grand Canyon Lodge, and in 2026 the North Rim has no lodging, drinking water, or gas.",
  "春秋最舒服；夏天南缘不算太热，但峡谷里非常热。": "Spring and fall are most comfortable. Summer isn't too hot on the South Rim, but it's extremely hot inside the canyon.",
  "南缘村（游客中心）": "Grand Canyon Village (visitor center)",
  "Hermit Road（西段）": "Hermit Road (west)",
  "Desert View Drive（东段）": "Desert View Drive (east)",
  "大峡谷村（南缘）": "Grand Canyon Village (South Rim)",
  "南缘村里有 El Tovar、Bright Angel、Maswik 等几家园内酒店，加上 Yavapai Lodge，要提早订；园外最近的是南门外的 Tusayan（约 10 分钟），再远是 Williams 和 Flagstaff（约 1–1.5 小时）。去东边沙漠观景塔方向，可以住 Cameron。2026 年 8 月底山洪后南缘缺水，园内酒店暂停过夜接待，NPS 预计感恩节前后恢复供水，之后分阶段重开。": "Grand Canyon Village on the South Rim has several in-park hotels—El Tovar, Bright Angel, Maswik—plus Yavapai Lodge; book early. The closest town is Tusayan, just outside the south entrance (about 10 minutes); farther out are Williams and Flagstaff (about 1–1.5 hours). If you're heading east toward the Desert View Watchtower, you can stay in Cameron. After flash flooding in late August 2026, the South Rim has a water shortage and in-park hotels have suspended overnight stays; the NPS expects water service to be restored around Thanksgiving, with a phased reopening after that.",
  "大盆地": "Great Basin",
  "古狐尾松、大理石溶洞与满天银河": "Ancient bristlecones, marble caves, and the Milky Way",
  "大盆地是北美最大的内流区，荒漠谷地和一道道南北走向的山脉相间，公园守着其中的 Snake 山脉：从海拔约 1,600 米的鼠尾草荒漠，一路升到 3,982 米的惠勒峰（Wheeler Peak）。山脚的 Lehman Caves 是内华达最长的洞穴，大理石里长满钟乳石、石笋和少见的洞穴盾；山顶附近的狐尾松林里有活了几千年的大盆地狐尾松，是地球上最长寿的树之一。这里地处偏远、空气干燥，是美国本土星空最暗的地方之一。": "The Great Basin is the largest area of interior drainage in North America, where desert valleys alternate with north–south mountain ranges. The park protects one of them, the Snake Range, which climbs from sagebrush desert at about 5,250 feet to 13,063-foot Wheeler Peak. At its foot, Lehman Caves is the longest cave in Nevada, its marble decorated with stalactites, stalagmites, and rare cave shields. In the groves near the summit, Great Basin bristlecone pines have lived for thousands of years, among the oldest trees on Earth. The park is remote and the air is dry, making it one of the darkest places in the contiguous United States.",
  "6–9 月最好：惠勒峰景观道全线通车（通常阵亡将士纪念日前后通到顶、11 月初第一场大雪后关上段），高山湖、狐尾松步道雪化了，夏天每周有护林员观星活动；7–8 月午后常有雷暴。9 月中下旬山杨变黄，9 月新月前后有天文节。冬天只有山下一段景观道、Lehman Caves 和最低的营地开放，适合穿雪鞋。": "June–September is best: Wheeler Peak Scenic Drive is fully open (it usually opens to the top around Memorial Day and the upper section closes after the first heavy snow in early November), the snow is gone from the alpine lake and bristlecone trails, and rangers lead astronomy programs every week in summer. July–August afternoons often bring thunderstorms. The aspens turn in mid- to late September, and the astronomy festival is held around the September new moon. In winter, only the lower part of the scenic drive, Lehman Caves, and the lowest campground are open—good for snowshoeing.",
  "Lehman Caves 游客中心一带": "Lehman Caves Visitor Center area",
  "惠勒峰景观道（高山湖 · 狐尾松 · 惠勒峰）": "Wheeler Peak Scenic Drive (alpine lakes, bristlecones, Wheeler Peak)",
  "南部（Lexington Arch）": "South (Lexington Arch)",
  "Baker 小镇": "Baker",
  "园内没有酒店，只有五个营地（都要在 Recreation.gov 预订，营地里没有饮用水），夏天要早订。最近的住处在园外 8 公里的小镇 Baker：Stargazer Inn、Whispering Elms 汽车旅馆都只有几间房，州界上的 Border Inn（约 15 分钟）全年营业；房间少，夏天和天文节前后很早订满。再找不到就住约 1 小时 15 分外的 Ely（内华达这一带最大的镇，酒店、超市都有），或者犹他一侧约 1 小时 40 分的 Delta。附近只有 Baker 和 Border Inn 两个加油站，路上很长一段没有补给，在 Ely 或 Delta 加满再来。": "There are no hotels in the park, only five campgrounds (all reservable on Recreation.gov, none with drinking water); book early for summer. The nearest lodging is in Baker, about 5 miles outside the park: the Stargazer Inn and Whispering Elms Motel have only a handful of rooms, and the Border Inn on the state line (about 15 minutes) is open year-round. With so few rooms, summer and astronomy-festival dates fill early. Otherwise, stay in Ely, about 1 hour 15 minutes away (the largest town in this part of Nevada, with hotels and supermarkets), or in Delta, Utah, about 1 hour 40 minutes away. Baker and the Border Inn have the only gas stations nearby, and there are long stretches with no services, so fill up in Ely or Delta.",
  "羚羊峡谷": "Antelope Canyon",
  "纳瓦霍部落公园（Navajo Nation Parks & Recreation）": "Navajo Nation Parks & Recreation",
  "光束洒落的狭缝峡谷": "Slot canyons lit by light beams",
  "纳瓦霍保留地上的砂岩狭缝峡谷，千万年的山洪和风沙把岩壁冲刷成流动的波纹，晴天正午阳光从窄缝射下，在谷底形成光束。陆路只能跟纳瓦霍授权的导览团进：上羚羊峡谷谷底平坦、光束最有名，下羚羊峡谷要上下几段钢梯、更窄更弯；订不到还可以去人少的羚羊峡谷 X 和水洞峡谷。峡谷注入鲍威尔湖的那一段也能从水上进：从 Antelope Point 划皮划艇进去，或坐码头的游船，归格伦峡谷国家休闲区管，不用订纳瓦霍的导览团。各家导览都按亚利桑那时间（不实行夏令时）发团。": "Sandstone slot canyons on the Navajo Nation, where ages of flash floods and blowing sand have scoured the walls into flowing waves. On sunny days around noon, sunlight shoots down through the narrow openings and forms beams on the canyon floor. By land you can enter only with an authorized Navajo tour. Upper Antelope Canyon has a flat floor and the most famous light beams; Lower Antelope Canyon involves several sets of steel stairs and is narrower and twistier. If those are booked, try the quieter Antelope Canyon X or Waterholes Canyon. The stretch where the canyon meets Lake Powell can also be reached by water—kayak in from Antelope Point or take a boat tour from the marina. That part is managed by Glen Canyon National Recreation Area and doesn't require a Navajo tour. All tour companies run on Arizona time (no daylight saving time).",
  "全年都能跟团进（感恩节、圣诞节、元旦等纳瓦霍节日关闭）；上羚羊的光束约 3 月底到 10 月初出现、6–7 月最明显，7–9 月雨季有山洪风险时会临时取消导览。": "Tours run year-round (closed on Navajo holidays, including Thanksgiving, Christmas, and New Year's Day). The light beams in Upper Antelope appear from about late March to early October and are strongest in June–July. During the July–September monsoon, tours may be canceled when there's a flash-flood risk.",
  "其他狭缝峡谷": "Other slot canyons",
  "鲍威尔湖 · 水上部分": "Lake Powell (by water)",
  "羚羊峡谷部落公园入口（98 号公路）": "Antelope Canyon Navajo Tribal Park entrance (Highway 98)",
  "羚羊峡谷里没有住宿，几乎所有人都住西边约 5 公里的佩吉（Page）：连锁酒店、汽车旅馆和餐厅都在 Lake Powell Blvd 一带，有几家上羚羊导览公司直接从镇上发团，3–10 月旺季和节假日要提前一两个月订。想住整套房子可以看佩吉西北的 Greenehaven，或犹他州一侧的 Big Water（犹他实行夏令时，夏天比佩吉快 1 小时，赶导览时间要按亚利桑那时间算）。": "There's no lodging at Antelope Canyon; nearly everyone stays in Page, about 3 miles west. Chain hotels, motels, and restaurants line Lake Powell Boulevard, and several Upper Antelope tour companies depart right from town. For peak season (March–October) and holidays, book a month or two ahead. For a whole-house rental, look at Greenehaven, northwest of Page, or Big Water on the Utah side. (Utah observes daylight saving time, so in summer it's an hour ahead of Page—schedule tours in Arizona time.)",
  "马蹄湾": "Horseshoe Bend",
  "格伦峡谷国家休闲区（NPS）· 停车场由佩吉市管理": "Glen Canyon National Recreation Area (NPS) · parking lot run by the City of Page",
  "科罗拉多河马蹄形河湾": "A horseshoe bend in the Colorado River",
  "科罗拉多河在佩吉以南绕着一座砂岩孤峰转了约 270 度，从约 300 米高的崖边往下看，河水像一只绿色的马蹄。观景台属于格伦峡谷国家休闲区，停车场归佩吉市管、按车收费，从停车场走约 1.2 公里硬化路面就到。附近的格伦峡谷大坝、Carl Hayden 游客中心和鲍威尔湖 Wahweap 观景点，加起来半天就能看完。": "South of Page, the Colorado River wraps about 270 degrees around a sandstone butte. From the cliff edge about 1,000 feet above, the river looks like a green horseshoe. The overlook is in Glen Canyon National Recreation Area; the parking lot is run by the City of Page and charges per vehicle. From the lot, a hardened path of about 0.7 mile leads to the rim. Nearby Glen Canyon Dam, the Carl Hayden Visitor Center, and the Wahweap Overlook on Lake Powell can all be seen in half a day.",
  "全年开放；春秋最舒服，夏天崖顶几乎没有遮阴、正午很热，日落时人最多。": "Open year-round. Spring and fall are most comfortable. In summer there's almost no shade on the rim and midday is very hot. Sunset is the most crowded time.",
  "格伦峡谷大坝": "Glen Canyon Dam",
  "鲍威尔湖 Wahweap": "Lake Powell: Wahweap",
  "科罗拉多河 · Lees Ferry": "Colorado River: Lees Ferry",
  "马蹄湾在佩吉镇以南约 10 分钟车程，住佩吉最方便，酒店、餐厅和超市都多，和羚羊峡谷连着玩也住这里；想住在湖边可以订格伦峡谷国家休闲区里 Wahweap 湾的 Lake Powell Resort。接着往大峡谷北缘或 White Pocket 方向走的话，可以住约 45 分钟外 Marble Canyon 一带的几家老旅馆；旺季佩吉周末常满，最好提前一两个月订。": "Horseshoe Bend is about 10 minutes south of Page. Staying in Page is easiest, with plenty of hotels, restaurants, and supermarkets, and it's also the base for Antelope Canyon. To stay on the lake, book Lake Powell Resort on Wahweap Bay in Glen Canyon National Recreation Area. If you're continuing toward the Grand Canyon's North Rim or White Pocket, try the handful of old lodges around Marble Canyon, about 45 minutes away. Page is often full on peak-season weekends, so book a month or two ahead.",
  "纪念碑谷": "Monument Valley",
  "西部片里的红色孤峰": "The red buttes of the Western",
  "横跨亚利桑那和犹他两州的纳瓦霍部落公园，平坦的荒漠上立着一两百米到三百米高的红色孤峰和方山，左右手（Mittens）和 Merrick Butte 是无数西部片和广告里的画面。游客中心的观景台就能看到最经典的全景，约 27 公里的土路环线可以自己开车下到谷底；环线以外的区域只能跟纳瓦霍向导去。纳瓦霍保留地实行夏令时，夏天比亚利桑那其他地方（包括佩吉）快 1 小时。": "A Navajo Tribal Park straddling Arizona and Utah, where red buttes and mesas rise roughly 300 to 1,000 feet from the flat desert. The Mittens and Merrick Butte have appeared in countless Westerns and commercials. The visitor center overlook has the classic panorama, and you can drive yourself down to the valley floor on a dirt loop of about 17 miles. Areas off the loop are open only with a Navajo guide. The Navajo Nation observes daylight saving time, so in summer it's an hour ahead of the rest of Arizona, including Page.",
  "春秋最舒服；夏天白天热、7–9 月午后常有雷暴，冬天偶尔下雪，红岩配白雪很漂亮；3 月底和 9 月中旬前后几天，日落时西手套岩的影子会投到东手套岩上。": "Spring and fall are most comfortable. Summer days are hot, and afternoon thunderstorms are common July–September. Winter brings occasional snow, which looks striking on the red rock. For a few days around late March and mid-September, the West Mitten's shadow falls on the East Mitten at sunset.",
  "游客中心 · The View": "Visitor center / The View",
  "谷地自驾环线": "Valley Drive",
  "向导团限定区域": "Guided-tour-only areas",
  "163 号公路（园外）": "Highway 163 (outside the park)",
  "纪念碑谷游客中心": "Monument Valley Visitor Center",
  "园内唯一的酒店是游客中心旁的 The View Hotel，每间房都正对左右手岩，看日出不用出门，房间少、旺季要提前几个月订；西边约 15 分钟的 Goulding's Lodge 有酒店、小木屋、营地、餐厅和加油站。订不到可以住南边亚利桑那的 Kayenta（约 35 分钟）或北边犹他的 Mexican Hat（约 35 分钟）、Bluff（约 1 小时）；也可以住纳瓦霍家庭经营的传统泥屋（hogan）和小木屋。": "The only hotel in the park is The View Hotel next to the visitor center. Every room faces the Mittens, so you can watch sunrise without leaving your room; it's small, so book months ahead for peak season. Goulding's Lodge, about 15 minutes west, has a hotel, cabins, a campground, a restaurant, and a gas station. If both are full, stay south in Kayenta, Arizona (about 35 minutes), or north in Mexican Hat (about 35 minutes) or Bluff (about an hour), Utah. You can also stay in traditional hogans and cabins run by Navajo families.",
  "波浪谷": "The Wave",
  "美国土地管理局（BLM）· 朱红悬崖国家保护区": "Bureau of Land Management (BLM) · Vermilion Cliffs National Monument",
  "抽签才能去的砂岩波浪": "Sandstone waves, by lottery only",
  "亚利桑那和犹他交界、美国土地管理局（BLM）管理的朱红悬崖国家保护区里，一片被风化成层层波纹的砂岩，条纹像凝固的海浪。每天只放 64 个名额，只能靠提前 4 个月的网上抽签或出发前两天的手机现场抽签拿到许可证，往返约 10 公里、没有路标。没抽中也有得玩：同一个步道口出发的 Wire Pass 狭缝峡谷、89 号公路边的蘑菇石不用抽签，开四驱或跟团还能去白口袋（White Pocket）。": "On the Arizona–Utah border, in Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, managed by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM), weathering has turned a patch of sandstone into layered ripples whose stripes look like frozen ocean waves. Only 64 people a day are allowed in. The only ways to get a permit are an online lottery four months ahead or a mobile daily lottery two days before your hike. The hike is about 6 miles round trip and unmarked. If you don't win, there's still plenty to do: the Wire Pass slot canyon, which starts from the same trailhead, and the Toadstool Hoodoos along U.S. 89 need no lottery, and with a 4WD vehicle or a guided tour you can reach White Pocket.",
  "春秋最合适；5–9 月白天酷热、几乎没有遮阴，出过中暑死亡事故，7–9 月雨季山洪多、土路可能被冲断，冬天砂岩可能结冰。": "Spring and fall are best. May–September days are brutally hot with almost no shade, and heatstroke deaths have occurred. The July–September monsoon brings frequent flash floods that can wash out the dirt roads. In winter the sandstone may ice over.",
  "狼丘北区（The Wave）": "Coyote Buttes North (The Wave)",
  "89 号公路沿线": "U.S. 89 corridor",
  "帕里亚高原（White Pocket）": "Paria Plateau (White Pocket)",
  "Paria 游客站（89 号公路）": "Paria Contact Station (U.S. 89)",
  "附近没有酒店，最常见的是住西边的 Kanab（到 Wire Pass 步道口约 1 小时 10 分，最后约 13 公里是土路），BLM 游客中心和每日抽签的安全说明也在镇上；东边的佩吉（约 1 小时）和两者之间的 Big Water 也行。去 White Pocket 或南边的 Coyote Buttes South，可以住 89A 号公路边 Marble Canyon 一带的老旅馆。雨后 House Rock Valley Road 可能过不去，行程里留一天机动。": "There are no hotels nearby. Most people stay in Kanab to the west (about 1 hour 10 minutes to the Wire Pass Trailhead; the last 8 miles or so are dirt road). The BLM visitor center and the daily lottery's safety briefing are in town too. Page to the east (about an hour) and Big Water in between also work. For White Pocket or Coyote Buttes South, try the old lodges around Marble Canyon on Highway 89A. After rain, House Rock Valley Road may be impassable, so leave a spare day in your itinerary.",
  "拱门": "Arches",
  "两千多座天然石拱": "More than 2,000 natural stone arches",
  "园内登记在册的天然砂岩拱门超过 2,000 座，密度世界第一，还有平衡石、公园大道这样的石柱和岩墙。一条约 28 公里长的主路从入口通到北端的魔鬼花园，大部分景点下车走几分钟到一两个小时就能看到；招牌精致拱门要徒步往返约 4.8 公里，日落时最好看。2026 年进园不用预约时段，但 3–10 月白天入口常排队一小时以上。": "More than 2,000 documented natural sandstone arches—the highest concentration in the world—plus rock pillars and fins like Balanced Rock and Park Avenue. A main road of about 18 miles runs from the entrance to Devils Garden at the north end, and most sights are a few minutes' to an hour or two's walk from the car. The signature Delicate Arch is a hike of about 3 miles round trip and looks best at sunset. No timed-entry reservation is required in 2026, but March–October daytime lines at the entrance often run more than an hour.",
  "3–5 月和 9–10 月最舒服；6–8 月白天常超过 38°C，徒步要赶清晨或傍晚；冬天人少，偶尔下雪，步道可能结冰。": "March–May and September–October are most comfortable. June–August days often top 100°F; hike at dawn or in the evening. Winter is quiet, with occasional snow, and trails may be icy.",
  "入口 · 公园大道": "Entrance / Park Avenue",
  "平衡石 · 窗户区": "Balanced Rock / Windows Section",
  "精致拱门 · 全景点": "Delicate Arch / Panorama Point",
  "火焰炉 · 魔鬼花园（北段）": "Fiery Furnace / Devils Garden (north)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有北端的 Devils Garden 露营地（3–10 月的营位在 recreation.gov 提前 6 个月开放、很快订满，11–2 月先到先得）。绝大多数人住南边约 10 分钟车程的 Moab 镇，酒店、民宿和餐厅都多，但 3–10 月旺季房价高、周末常满，最好提前几个月订；想住整套房子可以看镇南的 Spanish Valley，订不到时往北住 Green River（约 1 小时）。和峡谷地连着玩，在 Moab 住两三晚最省事。": "There are no hotels in the park, only Devils Garden Campground at the north end (sites for March–October open on Recreation.gov six months ahead and fill fast; November–February is first come, first served). The vast majority of visitors stay in Moab, about 10 minutes south, which has plenty of hotels, vacation rentals, and restaurants. Prices are high and weekends often sell out in peak season (March–October), so book months ahead. For a whole-house rental, look at Spanish Valley, south of town; if Moab is full, head north to Green River (about an hour). If you're also visiting Canyonlands, two or three nights in Moab is the simplest plan.",
  "峡谷地": "Canyonlands",
  "河流切出的峡谷迷宫": "A maze of river-cut canyons",
  "科罗拉多河和格林河在这里交汇，把高原切成一层层台地和深谷，是犹他州最大的国家公园。两条河把公园分成几个互不相通的园区：离 Moab 最近的天空之岛（Island in the Sky）是一块高出四周 300 多米的台地，梅萨拱门日出、大观景点和格林河观景点都在这里；南边的针尖区（The Needles）以红白条纹的石柱群和徒步为主，从 Moab 开车约 1.5 小时；西边的迷宫区只有四驱车能进，马蹄峡谷的大画廊岩画也在西侧。园区之间没有公路相连，一天一般只玩一个区。": "The Colorado and Green Rivers meet here, carving the plateau into tiers of mesas and deep canyons. It's the largest national park in Utah. The rivers split the park into districts with no roads between them. Island in the Sky, closest to Moab, is a mesa rising more than 1,000 feet above its surroundings, home to sunrise at Mesa Arch, Grand View Point, and Green River Overlook. The Needles, to the south, is known for red-and-white-banded spires and hiking, about 1.5 hours' drive from Moab. The Maze, to the west, is accessible only by 4WD vehicle, and Horseshoe Canyon, with the Great Gallery rock art, is also on the west side. With no roads linking the districts, most people visit one district per day.",
  "4–5 月和 9–10 月最舒服；夏天台地上常超过 35°C、峡谷里更热；冬天人少，偶尔下雪，针尖区游客中心约 12 月到次年 2 月中旬关闭。": "April–May and September–October are most comfortable. Summer often tops 95°F on the mesas and is hotter still in the canyons. Winter is quiet, with occasional snow; the Needles Visitor Center closes from about December to mid-February.",
  "天空之岛 · 死马点": "Island in the Sky / Dead Horse Point",
  "针尖区 · 211 号公路": "The Needles / Highway 211",
  "马蹄峡谷（西侧）": "Horseshoe Canyon (west)",
  "园内没有酒店：天空之岛的 Willow Flat 露营地只有 12 个先到先得的营位，针尖区露营地的 B 区可以在 recreation.gov 提前 6 个月订。玩天空之岛一般住 Moab（开车约 40–50 分钟），想住得更近可以订死马点州立公园里的蒙古包（提前 4 个月开放，很抢手）；去针尖区可以住园区门口的 Needles Outpost 帐篷营地（约 3–11 月营业）或东南边的 Monticello（约 1 小时）。去马蹄峡谷住 Green River 最近。": "There are no hotels in the park. Willow Flat Campground in Island in the Sky has just 12 first-come, first-served sites; Loop B of the Needles Campground can be reserved on Recreation.gov six months ahead. For Island in the Sky, most people stay in Moab (about 40–50 minutes' drive); to stay closer, book a yurt in Dead Horse Point State Park (reservations open four months ahead and go fast). For the Needles, stay at the Needles Outpost tent camp at the district entrance (open about March–November) or in Monticello to the southeast (about an hour). For Horseshoe Canyon, Green River is closest.",
  "圆顶礁": "Capitol Reef",
  "地壳褶皱与拓荒果园": "Folded rock and pioneer orchards",
  "公园沿着一道约 160 公里长的地壳褶皱——水袋褶皱（Waterpocket Fold）展开：白色的纳瓦霍砂岩圆顶像国会大厦的穹顶，连绵的崖壁像挡住去路的暗礁，“Capitol Reef”由此得名。游览中心是 24 号公路边的弗鲁塔（Fruita）：摩门拓荒者留下的果园夏秋可以自己摘果子，吉福德之家卖现烤的水果派，附近有岩画、希克曼天然桥和景观道；北边的大教堂谷、南边的 Burr Trail 都要开很长的土路，人很少。": "The park follows a wrinkle in the Earth's crust about 100 miles long: the Waterpocket Fold. White Navajo Sandstone domes resemble the Capitol dome, and the long line of cliffs blocked travel like a reef—hence the name Capitol Reef. The hub is Fruita, along Highway 24. In summer and fall you can pick fruit in the orchards left by Mormon pioneers, and the Gifford House sells freshly baked pies. Nearby are petroglyphs, Hickman Natural Bridge, and the Scenic Drive. Cathedral Valley to the north and the Burr Trail to the south both involve long dirt roads and see few visitors.",
  "4–6 月和 9–10 月最舒服，6–10 月果园陆续有水果可摘；7–9 月午后常有雷暴和山洪，窄峡谷和土路会临时封闭；冬天偶尔下雪，主要道路照常通车。": "April–June and September–October are most comfortable, and different fruits are ready to pick in the orchards from June through October. July–September afternoons often bring thunderstorms and flash floods, and narrow canyons and dirt roads may close temporarily. Winter brings occasional snow, but the main roads stay open.",
  "弗鲁塔 · 24 号公路": "Fruita / Highway 24",
  "景观道 · 峡谷步道": "Scenic Drive / canyon trails",
  "24 号公路西段观景点": "Highway 24 west overlooks",
  "大教堂谷（北区）": "Cathedral Valley (north)",
  "Burr Trail（南区）": "Burr Trail (south)",
  "园外东侧（妖精谷）": "East of the park (Goblin Valley)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Fruita 露营地（71 个营位，在 recreation.gov 提前 6 个月订，3 月中到 10 月几乎天天订满）。最方便的是西边约 15 分钟车程的 Torrey 小镇，汽车旅馆、餐厅和加油站都在 24 号公路边，旺季要提前订；想住整套木屋可以看旁边的 Teasdale。从东边来、或者要去妖精谷和马蹄峡谷，可以住 Hanksville（约 50 分钟）；沿 12 号公路从布莱斯过来，也可以在 Boulder 小镇住一晚。": "There are no hotels in the park, only Fruita Campground (71 sites, reservable on Recreation.gov six months ahead and booked nearly every night from mid-March through October). The most convenient town is Torrey, about 15 minutes west, with motels, restaurants, and gas along Highway 24; book ahead in peak season. For a whole-cabin rental, look at nearby Teasdale. If you're coming from the east or heading to Goblin Valley or Horseshoe Canyon, stay in Hanksville (about 50 minutes). Coming from Bryce on Highway 12, you can also spend a night in the town of Boulder.",
  "白沙": "White Sands",
  "世界最大的石膏沙丘": "The world's largest gypsum dunefield",
  "世界上最大的石膏沙丘区（约 710 平方公里）在新墨西哥州南部的图拉罗萨盆地，白沙公园保护了其中的一大部分：雪一样白的沙丘一直铺到圣安德烈斯山脚，2019 年由国家纪念地升格为国家公园。园里只有一条约 13 公里的沙丘大道，开到尽头就是纯白的沙丘中心，可以徒步、滑沙、看日落。公园被白沙导弹靶场包围，导弹试验时沙丘大道和 70 号公路会临时封闭几个小时。": "The world's largest gypsum dunefield, about 275 square miles, lies in the Tularosa Basin of southern New Mexico, and White Sands protects a large part of it. Snow-white dunes stretch to the foot of the San Andres Mountains. It was upgraded from a national monument to a national park in 2019. The only road, Dunes Drive, runs about 8 miles to the pure-white Heart of the Sands, where you can hike, sled the dunes, and watch the sunset. The park is surrounded by White Sands Missile Range; during missile tests, Dunes Drive and U.S. 70 close temporarily for a few hours.",
  "10–11 月和 2–3 月最舒服；6–8 月白天常到 35–38°C，只适合清早和傍晚活动，7–8 月午后多雷暴；3–5 月风大、常有沙尘暴；冬天白天十几度，夜里会到冰点以下。": "October–November and February–March are most comfortable. June–August days often reach 95–100°F, so plan activities for early morning and evening; July–August afternoons bring frequent thunderstorms. March–May is windy, with frequent dust storms. Winter days are in the 50s°F, and nights drop below freezing.",
  "游客中心 · 入口": "Visitor center / entrance",
  "沙丘大道沿线": "Dunes Drive",
  "沙丘中心（Heart of the Sands）": "Heart of the Sands",
  "卢塞罗湖（导弹靶场内）": "Lake Lucero (on the missile range)",
  "园内没有住宿和营地（野营区 2026 年仍关闭）。最近的是约 20 分钟车程的 Alamogordo，连锁酒店集中在 White Sands Blvd 南段，一般提前几天到几周订就行，9 月热气球节那个周末要早订；Las Cruces 酒店最多，从埃尔帕索机场过来顺路，到公园约 55 分钟。夏天想住凉快些，可以住萨克拉门托山上海拔约 2,600 米的 Cloudcroft，木屋多，到公园约 45 分钟。": "There's no lodging or campground in the park (the backcountry camping area remains closed in 2026). The closest town is Alamogordo, about 20 minutes away; chain hotels cluster on the south end of White Sands Boulevard, and booking a few days to a few weeks ahead is usually enough—except for the September balloon festival weekend, when you should book early. Las Cruces has the most hotels and is on the way from the El Paso airport, about 55 minutes from the park. For somewhere cooler in summer, stay in Cloudcroft, up in the Sacramento Mountains at about 8,500 feet, with lots of cabins, about 45 minutes from the park.",
  "卡尔斯巴德洞窟": "Carlsbad Caverns",
  "地下洞厅与蝙蝠群": "Vast caverns and bat flights",
  "地面上是约 2.6 亿年前海底礁石抬升成的瓜达卢佩山脊，地下藏着 119 个以上的洞穴，是含硫酸的地下水溶蚀石灰岩形成的。主角卡尔斯巴德洞窟可以从天然入口一路走下约 230 米，也可以坐电梯直达 Big Room——北美按体积最大的单个洞厅；4–10 月每天傍晚还能在洞口看几十万只蝙蝠飞出觅食。1995 年列入世界遗产。": "Above ground are the Guadalupe Mountains, an ancient reef from a sea about 260 million years ago, later uplifted. Beneath them lie more than 119 caves, dissolved out of the limestone by sulfuric acid–rich groundwater. At Carlsbad Cavern, the main attraction, you can walk about 750 feet down from the Natural Entrance or ride the elevator straight to the Big Room, the largest single cave chamber by volume in North America. From April through October, you can also watch hundreds of thousands of bats fly out of the cave mouth each evening to feed. The park became a World Heritage Site in 1995.",
  "洞里常年约 13°C，一年四季都能去；想看蝙蝠出洞要 4–10 月，8–9 月最多；夏天地面常到 32–40°C，8–9 月多午后雷雨，冬天偶尔下雪结冰。": "The cave stays about 56°F year-round, so you can visit any season. Bat flights happen April–October, with the most bats in August–September. Summer days on the surface often reach 90–104°F, August–September brings frequent afternoon thunderstorms, and winter has occasional snow and ice.",
  "游客中心 · 蝙蝠剧场": "Visitor center / Bat Flight Amphitheater",
  "卡尔斯巴德洞窟（地下）": "Carlsbad Cavern (underground)",
  "Walnut Canyon · 进园公路": "Walnut Canyon / entrance road",
  "Slaughter Canyon（西南角）": "Slaughter Canyon (southwest)",
  "园内没有住宿和露营地，只能凭免费许可证在背包野营区过夜。最近的是公园大门外的 White's City，只有一家老旅馆和 RV 营地，上山到游客中心约 15 分钟；多数人住约 35 分钟车程的 Carlsbad，连锁酒店多，但常被油田工人订走，平日也不便宜，最好提前几周订。从埃尔帕索飞进飞出的，第一晚或最后一晚可以住埃尔帕索机场附近（到洞窟约 2.5 小时），路上正好经过瓜达卢佩山国家公园。": "There's no lodging or campground in the park; the only overnight option is backcountry camping with a free permit. The closest place is White's City, just outside the park entrance, with one old hotel and an RV park, about 15 minutes up to the visitor center. Most people stay in Carlsbad, about 35 minutes away. It has plenty of chain hotels, but they're often booked by oil field workers and aren't cheap even on weekdays, so book a few weeks ahead. If you're flying in and out of El Paso, you can spend the first or last night near the El Paso airport (about 2.5 hours from the caverns); the drive passes right by Guadalupe Mountains National Park.",
  "石化林": "Petrified Forest",
  "彩绘沙漠与化石木": "Painted Desert and petrified wood",
  "这里保存着世界上最集中、颜色最艳的化石木之一：2 亿多年前三叠纪的大树被河水冲倒、掩埋，二氧化硅慢慢取代木质，变成五颜六色的石头。北段是红、粉、紫色条纹的彩绘沙漠和一段 66 号公路旧址，中段有古普韦布洛人的村落和岩画，南段是成片的化石木。一条约 45 公里的公园路从 I-40 的 311 号出口通到 180 号公路，多数人从一头进、另一头出，半天到一天就能看完；公园 8:00–17:00 开放，带走任何一块化石木都违法。": "One of the world's largest and most colorful concentrations of petrified wood. More than 200 million years ago, in the Triassic, great trees were toppled and buried by rivers, and silica slowly replaced the wood, turning it into multicolored stone. The north end has the Painted Desert, striped red, pink, and purple, and a stretch of old Route 66; the middle has Ancestral Pueblo village sites and petroglyphs; the south end has fields of petrified logs. A park road of about 28 miles runs from I-40 Exit 311 to U.S. 180. Most people enter at one end and leave at the other, taking half a day to a full day. The park is open 8 a.m.–5 p.m. Taking any petrified wood is illegal.",
  "春秋最舒服；6 月中旬到 9 月是季风雨季，7 月起午后常有雷暴和山洪，但雨后荒地颜色最鲜艳；冬天冷、偶尔下雪，路面结冰时会推迟开园。": "Spring and fall are most comfortable. Mid-June through September is monsoon season; from July on, afternoon thunderstorms and flash floods are common, but the badlands' colors are richest after rain. Winter is cold with occasional snow, and the park may open late when roads are icy.",
  "彩绘沙漠（北段）": "Painted Desert (north)",
  "66 号公路 · 普埃科河": "Route 66 / Puerco River",
  "蓝台地 · 圆锥丘": "Blue Mesa / The Tepees",
  "玛瑙桥 · 水晶森林": "Agate Bridge / Crystal Forest",
  "彩虹森林（南入口）": "Rainbow Forest (south entrance)",
  "彩绘沙漠游客中心（北入口，I-40 311 号出口）": "Painted Desert Visitor Center (north entrance, I-40 Exit 311)",
  "园内没有酒店和营地（只能背包进荒野区过夜，当天在游客中心领免费许可证）。最近的是西边约 30 分钟车程的 Holbrook，66 号公路沿线的老汽车旅馆多，招牌是能住进水泥“帐篷”的 Wigwam Motel；再往西约 1 小时的 Winslow 有修复的老铁路酒店 La Posada；从新墨西哥过来可以住 Gallup（到北入口约 1 小时 15 分，夏天比亚利桑那快 1 小时）。凤凰城或弗拉格斯塔夫机场进出、或者接着去大峡谷，就住 Flagstaff（约 2 小时）。一般不难订，提前几周就够。": "There are no hotels or campgrounds in the park (backpackers can camp in the wilderness area with a free permit picked up at the visitor center the same day). The closest town is Holbrook, about 30 minutes west, with lots of old motels along Route 66; the standout is the Wigwam Motel, where you sleep in a concrete “teepee.” About an hour farther west, Winslow has La Posada, a restored railroad hotel. Coming from New Mexico, you can stay in Gallup (about 1 hour 15 minutes to the north entrance; in summer it's an hour ahead of Arizona). If you're flying in or out of Phoenix or Flagstaff, or continuing to the Grand Canyon, stay in Flagstaff (about two hours). Rooms usually aren't hard to get; a few weeks ahead is enough.",
  "巨人柱": "Saguaro",
  "索诺兰沙漠的巨人柱仙人掌森林": "A saguaro forest in the Sonoran Desert",
  "巨人柱仙人掌（saguaro）只长在索诺兰沙漠，能活一两百年、高 12 米以上，五六十岁以后才长出第一根“手臂”，是美国西部最有代表性的剪影。公园分成图森市两边的两个园区：西区（Tucson Mountain District）海拔低，巨人柱最密，夕阳下的仙人掌森林和 Signal Hill 的古代岩画最有名；东区（Rincon Mountain District）有一条 13 公里的铺装环线穿过老仙人掌林，背后的林孔山从沙漠一直升到 2,600 多米的松林“天空之岛”。": "Saguaro cacti grow only in the Sonoran Desert. They can live 150 years or more and grow over 40 feet tall, and they don't sprout their first “arm” until they're 50 or 60 years old—the classic silhouette of the American West. The park has two districts on either side of Tucson. The western Tucson Mountain District is lower and has the densest saguaros, best known for cactus forest at sunset and ancient petroglyphs at Signal Hill. The eastern Rincon Mountain District has an 8-mile paved loop through an old saguaro forest, and behind it the Rincon Mountains climb from desert to a pine-forested “sky island” above 8,500 feet.",
  "10 月到次年 4 月白天 18–30°C，最舒服，也是护林员活动最多的时候；巨人柱 5 月底到 7 月开花，但白天常到 38–43°C，只能清早或傍晚活动；6 月中到 9 月是季风雨季，午后雷暴常引发山洪、冲坏西区的砂石路。": "October–April, days run about 65–85°F—the most comfortable time and when the most ranger programs are offered. Saguaros bloom from late May through July, but days often reach 100–110°F; go out only early or late. Mid-June through September is monsoon season, when afternoon thunderstorms often cause flash floods that damage the gravel roads in the west district.",
  "西区 · 图森山（Tucson Mountain District）": "West: Tucson Mountain District",
  "东区 · 林孔山（Rincon Mountain District）": "East: Rincon Mountain District",
  "Sabino Canyon（图森东北，园外）": "Sabino Canyon (northeast Tucson, outside the park)",
  "图森市中心（东西两区之间）": "Downtown Tucson (between the districts)",
  "园内没有酒店和车能开进去的营地（只有要走进山里的背包营地），大家都住图森：只去一边的话，西区住图森山脚的度假村或 Gilbert Ray 县营地，东区住城东 Tanque Verde / Broadway 一带；两边都去、想吃得方便，住市中心或大学一带最省事，到两个园区都约 25–35 分钟。10 月到次年 4 月是旺季，2 月初的宝石矿物展期间全城酒店最贵、最难订。": "There are no hotels or drive-in campgrounds in the park (only backcountry campgrounds you hike to), so everyone stays in Tucson. If you're visiting only one district, stay at a resort in the Tucson Mountains or at Gilbert Ray Campground (run by the county) for the west, or around Tanque Verde / Broadway on the east side of town for the east. To visit both and have easy dining, staying downtown or near the university is simplest, about 25–35 minutes to either district. October–April is peak season; during the gem and mineral show in early February, hotels across the city are at their most expensive and hardest to book.",
  "奇里卡瓦": "Chiricahua",
  "火山灰凝成的石柱森林": "Rock spires carved from volcanic ash",
  "亚利桑那东南角的奇里卡瓦山是索诺兰、奇瓦瓦两片沙漠之间的一座“天空之岛”。约 2,700 万年前附近 Turkey Creek 火山大爆发，厚厚的火山灰熔结成流纹岩，后来裂开、风化成几千根石柱和摇摇欲坠的平衡石，早年的牧场主叫它“石林”（Wonderland of Rocks）。8 英里的观景路从橡树林谷底一直开到山顶的 Massai Point，几条步道从山顶下到石柱中间。这里也是奇里卡瓦阿帕奇人的故乡，谷底的 Faraway Ranch 讲早期移民的故事。1924 年设为国家纪念地，2026 年 10 月 20 日升为美国第 64 座国家公园（NPS 官网、步道指南和 Recreation.gov 暂时还写旧名 Chiricahua National Monument）。": "In the southeast corner of Arizona, the Chiricahua Mountains rise as a “sky island” between the Sonoran and Chihuahuan deserts. About 27 million years ago the nearby Turkey Creek volcano erupted, and thick layers of ash fused into rhyolite. The rock later cracked and weathered into thousands of spires and precariously balanced rocks; early ranchers called it the “Wonderland of Rocks.” An 8-mile scenic drive climbs from oak woodland on the canyon floor to Massai Point at the top, and several trails drop from there down among the spires. This is also the homeland of the Chiricahua Apache, and Faraway Ranch on the canyon floor tells the story of early settlers. Designated a national monument in 1924, it became the 64th U.S. national park on October 20, 2026 (for now, the NPS website, trail guides, and Recreation.gov still use the old name, Chiricahua National Monument).",
  "海拔约 1,600–2,200 米，比图森凉快不少。3 月最挤（亚利桑那的冬季候鸟和春假），10 月、12 月学校放假也多，10 月到次年 4 月的周末停车难；夏天人最少，但 6 月中到 9 月底是季风季，午后常有雷暴、山洪和闪电。11 月到次年 4 月随时可能下雪，一场几英寸到一英尺，山顶的路可能结冰。4–6 月最干，常有禁火令。": "At about 5,200–7,200 feet, it's much cooler than Tucson. March is the busiest month (Arizona's snowbirds plus spring break), school breaks bring crowds in October and December too, and parking is tight on weekends from October through April. Summer is the quietest season, but mid-June through late September is monsoon season, with frequent afternoon thunderstorms, flash floods, and lightning. Snow can fall anytime from November through April, from a few inches to a foot at a time, and the road to the top may ice over. April–June is the driest stretch, and fire restrictions are common.",
  "谷底 · 游客中心 · Faraway Ranch": "Canyon floor: visitor center / Faraway Ranch",
  "山顶 · Massai Point · Echo Canyon 石林": "Summit: Massai Point / Echo Canyon spires",
  "Fort Bowie 国家历史遗址（北边约 50 分钟，园外）": "Fort Bowie National Historic Site (about 50 minutes north, outside the park)",
  "园里没有旅馆，只有一个 Bonita Canyon 营地（20 多个营位，Recreation.gov 提前 6 个月预约，3–4 月、10 月和节假日很快订满；车长 29 英尺以内，没有淋浴和电）。最近的住处在西北的 Willcox（约 50 分钟），I-10 边上有连锁汽车旅馆、超市和加油站，最方便；东边山那头的 Portal 是看鸟的人住的小村子，有几家山庄和出租小屋，但到公园要走 Pinery Canyon 土路翻山（建议高底盘车），铺装路要绕 Willcox 或 Douglas；南边的老矿镇 Bisbee 约 2 小时，住老房子改的民宿、逛街吃饭最有意思，适合和图森、Tombstone 连着玩。园内和附近没有加油站，Sunizona（27 英里）和 Willcox（37 英里）是最后的补给点。": "There's no lodging in the park, only Bonita Canyon Campground (20-some sites, reservable on Recreation.gov six months ahead; it fills fast in March–April, October, and on holidays. Vehicles are limited to 29 feet, and there are no showers or electric hookups). The nearest beds are in Willcox, about 50 minutes northwest, where chain motels, a grocery store, and gas stations along I-10 make it the most convenient base. Portal, over the mountains to the east, is a small village popular with birders, with a few lodges and rental cabins, but getting to the park from there means crossing the range on the dirt Pinery Canyon Road (high-clearance vehicle recommended); the paved route goes around via Willcox or Douglas. Bisbee, an old mining town to the south, is about two hours away. It's the most fun place to stay, in B&Bs in old houses with good shops and restaurants, and it pairs well with Tucson and Tombstone. There's no gas in or near the park; Sunizona (27 miles) and Willcox (37 miles) are the last places to fill up.",
  "瓜达卢佩山": "Guadalupe Mountains",
  "得州最高峰与远古海底礁石": "Texas's highest peak and an ancient reef",
  "瓜达卢佩山是约 2.6 亿年前二叠纪海底的一段巨大礁石（Capitan 礁），被抬升后成了从奇瓦瓦沙漠里拔地而起的石灰岩山脉，南端的 El Capitan 绝壁是西得州公路上最醒目的地标。旁边的瓜达卢佩峰海拔 2,667 米，是得州最高点；山里的 McKittrick 峡谷有溪水和枫树，10 月底到 11 月初满谷红叶。公园几乎没有穿过山里的公路，大部分要靠走：东边的 Pine Springs、McKittrick 峡谷，西边的白色石膏沙丘，北边的 Dog Canyon 各从不同的路进去。": "The Guadalupe Mountains are part of a huge reef (the Capitan Reef) from a Permian sea about 260 million years ago, uplifted into a limestone range that rises abruptly from the Chihuahuan Desert. El Capitan, the sheer cliff at the south end, is the most striking landmark on any West Texas highway. Neighboring Guadalupe Peak, at 8,751 feet, is the highest point in Texas. McKittrick Canyon has a stream and maples that turn the canyon red in late October and early November. Almost no roads cross the mountains, and most of the park is reached on foot: Pine Springs and McKittrick Canyon on the east, the white gypsum dunes on the west, and Dog Canyon on the north each have their own access roads.",
  "春秋最适合爬山，10 月底到 11 月初是 McKittrick 峡谷的红叶季，也是一年里人最多的时候，周末停车场和营地常满；夏天白天常到 32–38°C，午后多雷暴，山顶易遭雷击；一年四季都常刮大风（阵风可达 100 公里/时左右），冬春最猛；冬天偶尔下小雪，一般一天就化。": "Spring and fall are best for hiking. Late October to early November is fall color season in McKittrick Canyon and the busiest time of year; the parking lots and campgrounds often fill on weekends. Summer days often reach 90–100°F, with frequent afternoon thunderstorms, and summits are exposed to lightning. Strong winds blow year-round (gusts can reach about 60 mph), strongest in winter and spring. Winter brings occasional light snow that usually melts within a day.",
  "Pine Springs · 瓜达卢佩峰": "Pine Springs / Guadalupe Peak",
  "McKittrick 峡谷": "McKittrick Canyon",
  "62/180 号公路观景点": "U.S. 62/180 overlooks",
  "Salt Basin 沙丘（西侧）": "Salt Basin Dunes (west)",
  "Dog Canyon（北侧）": "Dog Canyon (north)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Pine Springs 和 Dog Canyon 两个只有厕所和饮用水的简易营地（全部要在 Recreation.gov 预约，春秋周末很快订满）。不露营的话，最近的是东北约 35 英里（约 45 分钟）的 White's City，只有一家老旅馆；多数人住约 1 小时车程的 Carlsbad，正好和卡尔斯巴德洞窟一起玩；从南边来可以住约 1 小时的 Van Horn（I-10 边的小镇），从埃尔帕索来单程约 2 小时。园内和附近都没有加油站和餐馆，进山前加满油、带好吃的。": "There are no hotels in the park, only two basic campgrounds, Pine Springs and Dog Canyon, with just restrooms and drinking water (all sites must be reserved on Recreation.gov; spring and fall weekends fill fast). If you're not camping, the closest lodging is White's City, about 35 miles (about 45 minutes) northeast, with a single old hotel. Most people stay in Carlsbad, about an hour away, and combine the trip with Carlsbad Caverns. Coming from the south, you can stay in Van Horn, a small town on I-10 about an hour away; from El Paso it's about two hours each way. There are no gas stations or restaurants in or near the park, so fill up and bring food before you arrive.",
  "大弯": "Big Bend",
  "格兰德河大拐弯、沙漠与天空岛": "The Rio Grande's big bend, desert, and sky island",
  "格兰德河在得州西南角拐了一个大弯，公园沿着这段美墨界河延伸约 190 公里，面积约 3,240 平方公里。园里三种地貌叠在一起：占公园大部分的奇瓦瓦沙漠、中间拔地而起的奇索斯山（美国唯一一座整个在国家公园里的山脉，山上是松树、橡树林），和河上切出的圣埃伦娜、Boquillas 等石灰岩大峡谷。这里离大城市很远，也是美国本土光污染最少的国家公园之一（国际暗夜公园）；周五到周一还能从园里的口岸坐小船过河，去墨西哥小村 Boquillas 吃顿午饭。": "The Rio Grande makes a big bend in the far southwest corner of Texas, and the park follows about 118 miles of this border river between the U.S. and Mexico, covering about 1,250 square miles. Three landscapes overlap: the Chihuahuan Desert, which makes up most of the park; the Chisos Mountains rising in the middle (the only mountain range in the U.S. contained entirely within a national park, with pine and oak woodland on top); and limestone canyons cut by the river, such as Santa Elena and Boquillas. Far from any big city, it's one of the national parks with the least light pollution in the contiguous U.S. (an International Dark Sky Park). Friday–Monday, you can also take a rowboat across the river at the park's port of entry to have lunch in the small Mexican village of Boquillas.",
  "10 月到次年 4 月是旺季，3 月春假和感恩节、圣诞节前后最挤，营地和山上的小屋天天满；2–4 月沙漠开花。5–9 月极热，河边下午常到 40°C 以上（5–6 月最热），只适合清早活动或上奇索斯山（盆地海拔约 1,650 米，凉快约 10°C）；7–9 月是雨季，午后雷暴常引发山洪、冲断土路。冬天偶有寒潮，山上会结冰、下雪。": "October–April is peak season. Spring break in March and the weeks around Thanksgiving and Christmas are the most crowded, with campgrounds and the lodge full every night. The desert blooms February–April. May–September is extremely hot: afternoons along the river often top 104°F (May–June is hottest), so be active only in the early morning or head up into the Chisos Mountains (the Basin sits at about 5,400 feet and is about 18°F cooler). July–September is the rainy season, when afternoon thunderstorms often cause flash floods that wash out dirt roads. Winter brings occasional cold snaps, with ice and snow in the mountains.",
  "奇索斯山 · 盆地（Chisos Basin）": "Chisos Mountains / Chisos Basin",
  "Ross Maxwell 观景道 · 圣埃伦娜峡谷（西南部）": "Ross Maxwell Scenic Drive / Santa Elena Canyon (southwest)",
  "格兰德河村 · Boquillas（东部）": "Rio Grande Village / Boquillas (east)",
  "Panther Junction · 北部": "Panther Junction / north",
  "园外：Terlingua · 河路 FM 170": "Outside the park: Terlingua / River Road (FM 170)",
  "Panther Junction 游客中心（公园总部）": "Panther Junction Visitor Center (park headquarters)",
  "园内只有奇索斯山小屋（Chisos Mountains Lodge）一家，在海拔约 1,650 米的盆地里，72 间房，11–4 月要提前半年以上订（石头小木屋要提前一两年）；2026 年小屋的餐厅关着，只有餐车和小超市。园外住得最多的是西门外的 Terlingua / Study Butte：汽车旅馆、土坯小屋、帐篷和房车营地都有，到 Panther Junction 约 40 分钟、到圣埃伦娜峡谷约 1 小时；北边的 Marathon 小镇（老牌 Gage 酒店）到 Panther Junction 约 1 小时 10 分钟；Alpine 连锁酒店多、便宜些，但单程要开约 1 小时 45 分钟。园里只有 Panther Junction 和格兰德河村两处加油站，园外最近的在 Study Butte 和 Marathon，进园前加满。": "The only lodging in the park is Chisos Mountains Lodge, in the Basin at about 5,400 feet, with 72 rooms; for November–April, book more than six months ahead (a year or two ahead for the stone cottages). In 2026 the lodge restaurant is closed, leaving only a food truck and a small store. Most people stay outside the west entrance in Terlingua / Study Butte, which has motels, adobe casitas, tents, and RV parks, about 40 minutes from Panther Junction and about an hour from Santa Elena Canyon. Marathon, a small town to the north with the historic Gage Hotel, is about 1 hour 10 minutes from Panther Junction. Alpine has more chain hotels and is cheaper, but it's about 1 hour 45 minutes each way. The only gas stations in the park are at Panther Junction and Rio Grande Village, and the nearest outside are in Study Butte and Marathon; fill up before you enter.",
  "恶地": "Badlands",
  "大草原上被雨水切开的彩色岩壁": "Rain-carved, multicolored walls on the prairie",
  "大平原中间突然裂开一道几十公里长的“恶地之墙”（Badlands Wall）：几千万年沉积下来的泥岩、火山灰被雨水切成尖塔、沟壑和一层层红黄白相间的条纹，每年还在以大约 2.5 厘米的速度往后退。岩层里埋着大量古哺乳动物化石；墙下和墙北是美国面积最大的混合草原保护区之一，野牛、大角羊、草原犬鼠和叉角羚都常见。2026 年 7 月公园宣布获得国际暗夜公园认证，夏夜能看到清晰的银河。": "In the middle of the Great Plains, the Badlands Wall suddenly breaks open for many miles. Tens of millions of years of mudstone and volcanic ash have been carved by rain into spires, gullies, and bands of red, yellow, and white, and the wall is still retreating by about an inch a year. The rock layers hold a wealth of ancient mammal fossils. Below and north of the wall lies one of the largest protected mixed-grass prairies in the U.S., where bison, bighorn sheep, prairie dogs, and pronghorn are common. In July 2026 the park announced its certification as an International Dark Sky Park; on summer nights the Milky Way is clearly visible.",
  "5–6 月和 9 月到 10 月上旬最舒服；7–8 月白天常到 35°C 以上、午后多雷暴，徒步要赶早；冬季寒冷多风雪，Loop Road 偶尔因冰雪临时封路，园内酒店和餐厅 10 月中到次年 4 月中关门。": "May–June and September to early October are most comfortable. July–August days often top 95°F with frequent afternoon thunderstorms; hike early. Winter is cold, windy, and snowy, Loop Road occasionally closes temporarily for ice and snow, and the in-park lodge and restaurant close from mid-October to mid-April.",
  "Cedar Pass（游客中心 · Door / Notch 步道）": "Cedar Pass (visitor center, Door and Notch trails)",
  "Badlands Loop Road 观景点": "Badlands Loop Road overlooks",
  "Sage Creek 荒野区（看野牛）": "Sage Creek Wilderness (bison)",
  "南园区（Stronghold · White River）": "South Unit (Stronghold, White River)",
  "园外：Wall 镇 · I-90 沿线": "Outside the park: Wall / I-90",
  "园内只有 Cedar Pass Lodge（4 月中到 10 月中营业，小木屋数量少，旺季要早订）和旁边的 Cedar Pass 营地，住这里看日出日落、参加晚上的星空讲解最方便。其次是北边 I-90 出口的 Wall 镇，汽车旅馆多、价格适中，到 Pinnacles 入口约 15 分钟；东南角的 Interior 小村只有几家旅馆。从拉皮德城当天往返单程约 1 小时 15 分，适合和黑山、拉什莫尔山一起玩的人把拉皮德城当大本营。": "The only in-park options are Cedar Pass Lodge (open mid-April to mid-October; there are few cabins, so book early for peak season) and the adjacent Cedar Pass Campground—the most convenient base for sunrise, sunset, and evening night-sky programs. Next best is the town of Wall, at the I-90 exit to the north, with plenty of moderately priced motels, about 15 minutes from the Pinnacles Entrance. The small village of Interior in the southeast has only a few motels. A day trip from Rapid City is about 1 hour 15 minutes each way; if you're also visiting the Black Hills and Mount Rushmore, Rapid City makes a good base.",
  "风洞": "Wind Cave",
  "地下的方解石“蜂窝”，地上的野牛草原": "Calcite “honeycomb” below, bison prairie above",
  "1903 年设立，是美国最早的国家公园之一，也是世界上第一座为保护洞穴设立的国家公园。地底已测绘出 160 多英里（约 260 公里）的通道，是世界上最长的洞穴之一，洞壁上满是薄片交错、像蜂窝一样的方解石“箱格”（boxwork），全世界已知的箱格大部分都在这里；进洞只能跟护林员导览。地面上是黑山南缘的混合草原和黄松林，野牛、马鹿、叉角羚和成片的草原犬鼠城就在公路边。": "Established in 1903, Wind Cave is one of the oldest national parks in the U.S. and the first in the world created to protect a cave. More than 160 miles of passages have been mapped, making it one of the longest caves in the world. Its walls are covered in boxwork, thin intersecting blades of calcite that look like honeycomb; most of the world's known boxwork is here. You can enter the cave only on ranger-led tours. Above ground, the mixed-grass prairie and ponderosa pine forest of the southern Black Hills put bison, elk, pronghorn, and sprawling prairie dog towns right beside the road.",
  "5–9 月洞穴导览班次最多，天然入口导览只在 5 月到 9 月开，烛光导览和野洞探险只在夏天；9–10 月马鹿发情求偶、黄昏能听到鸣叫；冬天洞里照样 12°C 左右，导览每天只有两三场，地面偶尔因暴风雪临时封路。北边卡斯特州立公园的 Needles 公路冬季不通车。": "May–September has the most cave tours. The Natural Entrance Tour runs only May–September, and the Candlelight and Wild Cave tours only in summer. In September–October the elk rut, and you can hear them bugling at dusk. In winter the cave is still about 54°F, but there are only two or three tours a day, and blizzards occasionally close roads temporarily. The Needles Highway in Custer State Park, to the north, is closed to cars in winter.",
  "游客中心 · 洞穴导览": "Visitor center / cave tours",
  "南部草原（US-385 · Bison Flats）": "South prairie (U.S. 385, Bison Flats)",
  "北部（Rankin Ridge · NPS 5/6 砂石路）": "North (Rankin Ridge, NPS 5/6 gravel roads)",
  "园外：卡斯特州立公园": "Outside the park: Custer State Park",
  "园外：拉什莫尔山 · 疯马": "Outside the park: Mount Rushmore / Crazy Horse",
  "园内只有 Elk Mountain 营地，没有酒店。住南边约 15 分钟的 Hot Springs 离洞最近；想顺路玩卡斯特州立公园、拉什莫尔山和疯马，住北边约 30 分钟的 Custer 镇或州立公园里的几家度假木屋（State Game Lodge、Sylvan Lake Lodge 等，一般 5–10 月营业）更方便，Keystone、Hill City 离拉什莫尔山近；拉皮德城到游客中心约 1 小时，旅馆、超市最多。每年 8 月上中旬 Sturgis 摩托车集会（2026 年 8 月 7–16 日，2027 年 8 月 6–15 日）期间整个黑山的房价暴涨，要很早订。": "The only in-park option is Elk Mountain Campground; there's no hotel. Hot Springs, about 15 minutes south, is closest to the cave. If you're also visiting Custer State Park, Mount Rushmore, and Crazy Horse, it's easier to stay in the town of Custer, about 30 minutes north, or at one of the resort lodges in the state park (State Game Lodge, Sylvan Lake Lodge, and others, generally open May–October); Keystone and Hill City are close to Mount Rushmore. Rapid City, about an hour from the visitor center, has the most hotels and supermarkets. During the Sturgis Motorcycle Rally in early to mid-August (August 7–16, 2026; August 6–15, 2027), room prices across the Black Hills soar, so book very early.",
  "西奥多·罗斯福": "Theodore Roosevelt",
  "北达科他恶地里的野马和野牛": "Wild horses and bison in the North Dakota badlands",
  "小密苏里河切开北达科他西部的草原，留下一片层层叠叠的恶地：灰色的膨润土、黑色的褐煤层和烧红的“熔渣岩”一层压一层。1880 年代年轻的西奥多·罗斯福在这里打猎、经营牧场，后来当上总统、成了美国保护自然的推手。公园分成三块：Medora 镇边的 South Unit 有 58 公里的景观环路，野牛、野马和草原犬鼠沿路就能看到；往北约 110 公里的 North Unit 更陡峭、更安静，有大角羊；两者之间的 Elkhorn Ranch 是罗斯福的牧场旧址。": "The Little Missouri River cut through the prairie of western North Dakota, leaving layered badlands: gray bentonite, black lignite seams, and red “scoria” baked by burning coal, stacked one on another. In the 1880s a young Theodore Roosevelt hunted and ranched here; he later became president and a driving force behind conservation in America. The park has three units. The South Unit, next to the town of Medora, has a 36-mile scenic loop where bison, wild horses, and prairie dogs are visible from the road. The North Unit, about 70 miles north, is more rugged and quieter, with bighorn sheep. Between them is the Elkhorn Ranch, the site of Roosevelt's ranch.",
  "全年开放、24 小时都能进。6 月草最绿、野花多、小野马刚出生；7–8 月白天常到 30°C 以上、午后多雷暴，也是 Medora 音乐剧的季节；9 月凉爽、人少，下旬河边的三叶杨变黄，麋鹿开始发情鸣叫。冬天常在 -20°C 以下，下雪结冰时景观路会部分封闭。注意 North Unit 用中部时间，比 South Unit 和 Medora 早一小时。": "Open year-round, 24 hours a day. June is greenest, with wildflowers and newborn foals. July–August days often top 85°F with frequent afternoon thunderstorms; it's also the season of the Medora Musical. September is cool and quiet; in late September the cottonwoods along the river turn yellow and the elk begin to bugle. Winter often drops below −4°F, and sections of the scenic drive close when there's snow and ice. Note that the North Unit is on Central Time, an hour ahead of the South Unit and Medora.",
  "South Unit · 景观环路（Medora）": "South Unit: Scenic Loop Drive (Medora)",
  "彩绘峡谷（I-94 旁）": "Painted Canyon (off I-94)",
  "石化林（South Unit 西侧，砂石路进）": "Petrified Forest (western South Unit, by gravel road)",
  "Elkhorn Ranch 园区（罗斯福牧场旧址）": "Elkhorn Ranch Unit (Roosevelt's ranch site)",
  "North Unit（Watford City 以南）": "North Unit (south of Watford City)",
  "Medora 小镇（园外）": "Medora (outside the park)",
  "South Unit 游客中心（Medora）": "South Unit Visitor Center (Medora)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 Cottonwood（South Unit）和 Juniper（North Unit）两个营地，2026 年 5 月起都要在 Recreation.gov 预订。多数人住 South Unit 门口的 Medora：镇上的酒店、汽车旅馆大多由西奥多·罗斯福 Medora 基金会经营，6 月初到 9 月中音乐剧季最难订；冬天只有 Rough Riders Hotel 和 Hotel 1883 两家开；订不到就住东边约 25 分钟的 Belfield 或 45 分钟的 Dickinson（连锁酒店最多）。去 North Unit 住 Watford City，到入口约 20 分钟；从 Medora 当天来回 North Unit 单程约 1 小时 15 分。Elkhorn Ranch 附近没有住处。": "There are no hotels in the park, only two campgrounds, Cottonwood (South Unit) and Juniper (North Unit); from May 2026 both require reservations on Recreation.gov. Most people stay in Medora, at the South Unit entrance. Most of its hotels and motels are run by the Theodore Roosevelt Medora Foundation and are hardest to book during the musical season, early June to mid-September. In winter only two are open, the Rough Riders Hotel and Hotel 1883. If Medora is full, stay in Belfield, about 25 minutes east, or Dickinson, about 45 minutes, which has the most chain hotels. For the North Unit, stay in Watford City, about 20 minutes from the entrance; a day trip to the North Unit from Medora is about 1 hour 15 minutes each way. There's no lodging near the Elkhorn Ranch.",
  "凯霍加谷": "Cuyahoga Valley",
  "克利夫兰和阿克伦之间的运河、瀑布和砂岩崖": "Canal history, waterfalls, and sandstone ledges between Cleveland and Akron",
  "夹在克利夫兰和阿克伦两座城市之间、沿凯霍加河约 35 公里长的一条河谷，是美国离大城市最近的国家公园之一。19 世纪这里是俄亥俄–伊利运河（Ohio & Erie Canal）的主干，当年拉船的纤道现在是约 32 公里平坦的 Towpath 步道，可以骑车、走路，再坐观光火车回来；河谷两侧的小溪切出 Brandywine 等几十条瀑布，Virginia Kendall 一带还有长满青苔的砂岩崖壁 The Ledges。凯霍加河 1969 年因为污染严重着过火，后来成了美国治理环境的标志，如今河谷里有河狸、苍鹭和白头海雕。": "This river valley runs about 22 miles along the Cuyahoga River between Cleveland and Akron, making it one of the closest national parks to a major city. In the 1800s the main line of the Ohio & Erie Canal ran through here, and the old towpath where canal boats were hauled is now the Towpath Trail, about 20 flat miles for biking or walking, with a scenic train to ride back. Streams on both sides of the valley have cut dozens of waterfalls, Brandywine Falls among them, and the Virginia Kendall area has The Ledges, mossy sandstone cliffs. The Cuyahoga River was so polluted that it caught fire in 1969, and it went on to become a symbol of America's environmental cleanup. Today the valley has beavers, herons, and bald eagles.",
  "10 月中旬红叶最好，也是一年里最挤的时候，天气好的周末 Brandywine 瀑布停车场 10 点前就满。春天（4–5 月）瀑布水量大、林下野花多；夏天可以骑车走 Towpath、坐火车，6–8 月有“Explorer”火车接骑车的人。冬天公园照开，Kendall Hills 一带能滑雪橇、越野滑雪，瀑布偶尔结冰。": "Fall color peaks in mid-October, which is also the busiest time of year; on nice weekends the Brandywine Falls lot fills before 10 a.m. In spring (April–May) the waterfalls run high and wildflowers cover the forest floor. Summer is for biking the Towpath and riding the train, and June–August the Explorer train picks up cyclists. The park stays open in winter, with sledding and cross-country skiing around Kendall Hills, and the falls sometimes freeze.",
  "Boston · Peninsula（游客中心 · 火车站）": "Boston / Peninsula (visitor center, train stations)",
  "Brandywine 瀑布一带": "Brandywine Falls area",
  "南段：Everett · Beaver Marsh（Ira）": "South: Everett / Beaver Marsh (Ira)",
  "北段：Canal Exploration Center · Rockside": "North: Canal Exploration Center / Rockside",
  "园内住处很少：Brandywine 瀑布旁边的 Inn at Brandywine Falls 是一家老房子民宿，Boston 一带的 Stanford House 是公园的老农舍、整栋出租给团体。大多数人住园外：北头 I-77 和 Rockside Road 一带的 Independence 连锁酒店最多，离火车 Rockside 站近；东边的 Hudson 小镇安静、有餐馆；南头住阿克伦（Akron）或 Cuyahoga Falls，离 Beaver Marsh、Everett 一带近。从克利夫兰市区开过来约 30 分钟，当天来回也很常见。": "There are few places to stay in the park: The Inn at Brandywine Falls is a B&B in an old house next to the falls, and the Stanford House, an old farmhouse near Boston, is rented out whole to groups. Most people stay outside the park. Independence, at the north end around I-77 and Rockside Road, has the most chain hotels and is close to the train's Rockside station. Hudson, to the east, is a quiet town with restaurants. At the south end, stay in Akron or Cuyahoga Falls, close to Beaver Marsh and the Everett area. Downtown Cleveland is about 30 minutes away, so day trips are common too.",
  "印第安纳沙丘": "Indiana Dunes",
  "密歇根湖南岸的沙丘、沼泽和湖滩": "Dunes, wetlands, and beaches on Lake Michigan's southern shore",
  "芝加哥东南约 1 小时，密歇根湖南岸约 24 公里长的一条湖岸带：一边是能游泳的细沙湖滩和几十米高的沙丘，背后是一圈圈不同年代的老沙丘上长出来的橡树林、黑橡树稀树草原、沼泽和泥炭藓沼。20 世纪初芝加哥大学的 Henry Cowles 就是在这里研究沙丘上的植物怎么一步步演替，开创了美国的生态学；这里也是美国生物多样性最高的国家公园之一。公园和钢厂、电厂、小镇交错在一起，2019 年才从国家湖滨升为国家公园；中间的印第安纳沙丘州立公园是州里的，另收门票。": "About an hour southeast of Chicago, the park stretches about 15 miles along the southern shore of Lake Michigan. On one side are fine-sand swimming beaches and dunes rising well over 100 feet; behind them, ridge after ridge of older dunes support oak woods, black oak savanna, marshes, and bogs. In the early 1900s Henry Cowles of the University of Chicago studied how plants gradually take over the dunes here, work that helped found the science of ecology in America, and the park is one of the most biodiverse in the national park system. It's woven in among steel mills, power plants, and small towns, and it was redesignated from a national lakeshore to a national park only in 2019. Indiana Dunes State Park, in the middle, is run by the state and charges its own entrance fee.",
  "6–8 月是湖滩季，周末 West Beach 等大停车场常满，湖水 7–8 月才暖；离岸流和大浪的日子很危险，看海滩的旗子。9–10 月人少、秋叶好，沙丘上走起来不晒。冬天湖边结冰、风大，沙丘可以越野滑雪；春天（4–5 月）是看候鸟的季节，Great Marsh 一带鸟最多。": "June–August is beach season. Big lots like West Beach often fill on weekends, and the lake doesn't warm up until July–August. Rip currents and high waves make some days dangerous, so check the beach flags. September–October is quieter, with fall color and cooler dune hikes. In winter the shore ices up and the wind is strong, but you can cross-country ski the dunes. Spring (April–May) is bird migration season, best around the Great Marsh.",
  "西区：West Beach · Miller Woods · Portage Lakefront": "West: West Beach / Miller Woods / Portage Lakefront",
  "中区：游客中心 · Cowles Bog · Chellberg 农场": "Central: visitor center / Cowles Bog / Chellberg Farm",
  "印第安纳沙丘州立公园（州里的，另收费）": "Indiana Dunes State Park (state-run, separate fee)",
  "东区：Beverly Shores · Great Marsh · Mount Baldy": "East: Beverly Shores / Great Marsh / Mount Baldy",
  "印第安纳沙丘游客中心（Porter）": "Indiana Dunes Visitor Center (Porter)",
  "园内只有 Dunewood 营地（66 个营位，Recreation.gov 预订）。最方便的是住游客中心旁边的 Chesterton / Porter（连锁酒店、餐馆，到 West Beach、Mount Baldy 都在 20–25 分钟内）或东头的 Michigan City（湖边酒店、赌场酒店、大型奥特莱斯，离 Mount Baldy 最近）。Beverly Shores、Dune Acres 一带的湖边小镇有不少整套度假屋，夏天要提前几个月订。从芝加哥当天来回也很常见：开车约 1 小时，或者坐 South Shore Line 通勤火车到 Dune Park、Beverly Shores 站。": "The only place to stay in the park is Dunewood Campground (66 sites, reservable on Recreation.gov). The most convenient bases are Chesterton/Porter, next to the visitor center (chain hotels and restaurants, 20–25 minutes to both West Beach and Mount Baldy), and Michigan City at the east end (lakeside hotels, casino hotels, and a big outlet mall; closest to Mount Baldy). The lakeside towns of Beverly Shores and Dune Acres have plenty of whole-house vacation rentals; book several months ahead for summer. Day trips from Chicago are common too: it's about an hour's drive, or take the South Shore Line commuter train to Dune Park or Beverly Shores station.",
  "圣路易斯拱门": "Gateway Arch",
  "密西西比河边 192 米高的不锈钢拱门": "A 630-foot stainless steel arch on the Mississippi",
  "美国面积最小的国家公园（约 0.8 平方公里），在圣路易斯市中心的密西西比河边。主角是芬兰裔建筑师埃罗·沙里宁（Eero Saarinen）设计的大拱门：不锈钢外皮，高、宽都是 630 英尺（约 192 米），1965 年建成，是美国最高的人造纪念碑，纪念托马斯·杰斐逊和 19 世纪美国的西进扩张。坐拱门里面的小电车上到顶端，从小窗户往下看密西西比河和整座城；拱门底下是免费的博物馆，讲从原住民到路易斯安那购地、刘易斯与克拉克、拓荒者的西部故事。几个街区外的老法院（Old Courthouse）是 1847 年德雷德·斯科特（Dred Scott）争取自由的诉讼开始的地方。2018 年由“杰斐逊国家扩张纪念地”改名升为国家公园。": "The smallest national park in the country (about 190 acres), on the Mississippi riverfront in downtown St. Louis. The centerpiece is the Gateway Arch, designed by Finnish American architect Eero Saarinen: clad in stainless steel, 630 feet tall and 630 feet wide, and completed in 1965. It's the tallest human-made monument in the U.S., honoring Thomas Jefferson and the nation's westward expansion in the 19th century. A small tram inside the Arch carries you to the top, where narrow windows look down on the Mississippi and the whole city. Beneath the Arch, a free museum tells the story of the West, from Native peoples to the Louisiana Purchase, Lewis and Clark, and the pioneers. A few blocks away, the Old Courthouse is where Dred Scott's suit for freedom began in 1847. The site, formerly Jefferson National Expansion Memorial, was renamed and became a national park in 2018.",
  "全年都能去，室内为主。4–5 月、9–10 月最舒服；6–8 月又热又湿，电车票常提前卖光，暑假周末最挤；7 月 4 日前后 Fair Saint Louis 在拱门草地上办，人山人海。冬天冷、风大，但人少、电车好订。密西西比河涨水时河边的 Leonor K. Sullivan 大道和游船码头会被淹、游船停航。": "Good year-round, since most of it is indoors. April–May and September–October are the most comfortable. June–August is hot and humid, tram tickets often sell out in advance, and summer weekends are the busiest. Around July 4, Fair Saint Louis takes over the Arch grounds and draws huge crowds. Winter is cold and windy, but it's quiet and tram tickets are easy to get. When the Mississippi floods, Leonor K. Sullivan Boulevard and the riverboat landing go underwater and the cruises stop.",
  "拱门和地下博物馆": "The Arch and underground museum",
  "老法院 · 市中心": "Old Courthouse / downtown",
  "河滨（游船码头 · Eads 大桥）": "Riverfront (riverboat landing / Eads Bridge)",
  "拱门游客中心（4th Street 入口）": "Gateway Arch Visitor Center (4th Street entrance)",
  "就住圣路易斯市中心：拱门西边隔一条街的 Hyatt Regency St. Louis at the Arch 等几家酒店走路几分钟到游客中心，房间能看到拱门的要另外选；北边河边的老仓库区 Laclede's Landing、西边市中心 Washington Avenue 一带有更多酒店和整套公寓。市中心晚上部分街区比较冷清，住得离拱门近、走大路比较安心。公园没有自己的停车场，开车来停附近的收费停车楼（比如 Stadium East 停车楼）或河边老码头的收费停车场。从机场（STL）坐 MetroLink 轻轨到 8th & Pine 或 Laclede's Landing 站约 30 分钟，不用开车。": "Stay downtown. The Hyatt Regency St. Louis at the Arch and a few other hotels one block west of the Arch are a few minutes' walk from the visitor center; if you want an Arch view, book a room that has one. Laclede's Landing, the old riverside warehouse district to the north, and the Washington Avenue area downtown to the west have more hotels and apartment rentals. Some downtown blocks are quiet at night, so staying close to the Arch and sticking to main streets is the more comfortable choice. The park has no parking lot of its own; if you drive, use a nearby paid garage (such as the Stadium East Garage) or the paid lots on the old riverfront landing. From the airport (STL), MetroLink light rail reaches 8th & Pine or Laclede's Landing station in about 30 minutes, so you don't need a car.",
  "皇家岛": "Isle Royale",
  "苏必利尔湖上的狼、驼鹿和荒野岛": "Wolves, moose, and wilderness on Lake Superior",
  "苏必利尔湖西北部的一座长约 72 公里的荒岛和周围 400 多个小岛，离加拿大比离密歇根本土还近。岛上不通车、没有公路，只有约 265 公里步道和 36 处只能走路、划船到的营地，是全美游客最少的国家公园之一，也是少有的游客平均停留好几天的公园：很多人从西头的 Windigo 背包走到东头的 Rock Harbor。岛上的狼和驼鹿从 1958 年起一直有人在研究，是世界上持续最久的捕食者和猎物研究。只能坐渡轮、水上飞机或自己的船来，每年只开 4 月 16 日到 10 月 31 日。": "A wilderness island about 45 miles long in northwestern Lake Superior, plus more than 400 smaller islands around it, closer to Canada than to mainland Michigan. There are no cars or roads, only about 165 miles of trails and 36 campgrounds you can reach only on foot or by boat. It's one of the least-visited national parks in the country and one of the few where visitors stay several days on average: many backpack the length of the island from Windigo at the west end to Rock Harbor at the east. Researchers have studied the island's wolves and moose since 1958, the longest-running predator-prey study in the world. You can get here only by ferry, seaplane, or private boat, and the park is open only April 16–October 31.",
  "公园 4 月 16 日到 10 月 31 日开放，11 月到次年 4 月中整座岛关闭。渡轮、水上飞机大约 5 月中到 9 月底才有，Rock Harbor Lodge、游客中心、商店只在 6 月上旬到 9 月中旬营业。7–8 月最暖、班次最多，但 6 月到 7 月初黑蝇、蚊子多；8 月底到 9 月蚊虫少、人少，9 月下旬开始有红叶，班次也越来越少。湖上常年冷，夏天也要带抓绒和雨衣。": "The park is open April 16–October 31; from November to mid-April the whole island closes. Ferries and seaplanes run only from about mid-May to late September, and Rock Harbor Lodge, the visitor centers, and the store are open only from early June to mid-September. July–August is the warmest, with the most departures, but black flies and mosquitoes are bad from June to early July. Late August–September brings fewer bugs and fewer people; fall color starts in late September, as departures dwindle. The lake is cold all year, so bring fleece and rain gear even in summer.",
  "东头：Rock Harbor（Copper Harbor、Houghton 坐船）": "East end: Rock Harbor (boats from Copper Harbor and Houghton)",
  "西头：Windigo（Grand Portage 坐船）": "West end: Windigo (boats from Grand Portage)",
  "岛中间（背包穿越）": "Interior (backpacking)",
  "密歇根本土：Houghton · Copper Harbor": "Michigan mainland: Houghton / Copper Harbor",
  "明尼苏达本土：Grand Portage": "Minnesota mainland: Grand Portage",
  "Houghton（公园总部和游客中心）": "Houghton (park headquarters and visitor center)",
  "岛上只有东头的 Rock Harbor Lodge（60 间湖景房和 20 栋带小厨房的小木屋，2026 年 6 月 5 日到 9 月 11 日最后一晚）和西头 Windigo 的 2 间简易小木屋，提前 366 天开订、夏天很快订满；其余都是先到先得的营地（6 人以下免费、要在岛上领许可）。当天来回的住码头附近：去 Rock Harbor 的住 Copper Harbor（小镇上几家汽车旅馆，大多只在夏天开），或者 Houghton / Hancock（大学城，连锁酒店多，到 Copper Harbor 码头约 1 小时）；坐水上飞机的住 Houghton 最近。去 Windigo 的住 Grand Portage 的 Grand Portage Lodge & Casino，或者往南约 1 小时的 Grand Marais（明尼苏达北岸的度假小镇，小木屋、民宿多）。": "On the island, the only lodging is Rock Harbor Lodge at the east end (60 lakeview rooms and 20 cottages with kitchenettes; in 2026, open June 5, with September 11 as the last night) and two rustic camper cabins at Windigo on the west end. Reservations open 366 days ahead, and summer fills fast. Everything else is first-come, first-served campgrounds (free for groups of six or fewer, with a permit you pick up on the island). For a day trip, stay near your dock. For Rock Harbor, stay in Copper Harbor (a few motels in town, most open only in summer) or in Houghton/Hancock (a college town with plenty of chain hotels, about an hour from the Copper Harbor dock); for the seaplane, Houghton is closest. For Windigo, stay at Grand Portage Lodge & Casino in Grand Portage, or in Grand Marais, about an hour south, a resort town on Minnesota's North Shore with lots of cabins and B&Bs.",
  "航海家": "Voyageurs",
  "明尼苏达北部的湖、岛和北极光": "Lakes, islands, and northern lights in northern Minnesota",
  "明尼苏达北部和加拿大安大略交界处的一片湖区：Rainy、Kabetogama、Namakan、Sand Point 四个大湖和 500 多个岛，水面约占公园四成，中间的 Kabetogama 半岛不通公路。名字来自 18 世纪划着桦皮大独木舟在这条水路上运皮毛的法裔加拿大船夫（voyageurs）。岸边是 20 多亿年前的古老岩石和北方针叶林，湖里有白头海雕、潜鸟，林子里有狼和黑熊。夏天坐护林员游船去湖中间 1913 年建成的 Kettle Falls 酒店，或者租船屋在湖上住几天；冬天湖面冻实，可以开车上冰上公路。2020 年被评为国际暗夜公园，常能看到北极光。": "A lake country on the border between northern Minnesota and Ontario: four big lakes (Rainy, Kabetogama, Namakan, and Sand Point) and more than 500 islands. Water covers about 40 percent of the park, and no road crosses the Kabetogama Peninsula in the middle. The name comes from the voyageurs, the French Canadian canoemen who paddled big birchbark canoes along this water route carrying furs in the 1700s. The shores are rock more than 2 billion years old, under boreal forest; bald eagles and loons live on the lakes, and wolves and black bears in the woods. In summer, take a ranger-led boat tour to the Kettle Falls Hotel, built in 1913 in the middle of the lakes, or rent a houseboat and live on the water for a few days. In winter the lakes freeze solid and you can drive out on ice roads. Voyageurs became an International Dark Sky Park in 2020, and the northern lights are often visible.",
  "6 月中到 9 月底护林员游船、游客中心全开，7–8 月最暖、游船最多，但 6 月到 7 月蚊子、鹿虻多；9 月人少、开始变色，月底游船就停了。5 月初湖上可能还有冰，10 月以后只剩 Rainy Lake 游客中心短时间开放。冬天（大约 1–3 月）可以开冰上公路、雪地摩托、越野滑雪，夜里最冷到零下 30 多摄氏度。北极光一年四季都可能有，秋冬夜长最容易看到。": "From mid-June to late September the ranger-led boat tours and visitor centers are fully running. July–August is the warmest, with the most tours, but mosquitoes and deer flies are thick in June and July. September is quieter, the leaves start to turn, and the tours end late in the month. In early May there may still be ice on the lakes; after October, only the Rainy Lake Visitor Center stays open, with limited hours. In winter (roughly January–March) you can drive the ice roads, snowmobile, and cross-country ski; the coldest nights drop below –22°F. The northern lights can appear any time of year but are easiest to see on the long nights of fall and winter.",
  "Rainy Lake（International Falls 一侧）": "Rainy Lake (International Falls side)",
  "Kettle Falls（坐船）": "Kettle Falls (by boat)",
  "园内只有坐船才到得了的 Kettle Falls 酒店（1910–1913 年建的老客房，另有带厨房的度假屋，住客可以订酒店的船从 Ash River 游客中心接送）和许多只能划船、开船去的营地。多数人住园外：西边的 International Falls（连锁酒店最多，到 Rainy Lake 游客中心约 20 分钟），或者 Kabetogama、Ash River 湖边的家庭度假村（小木屋，大多带船出租，5 月到 10 月营业）；南边的 Crane Lake 也有几家。想住湖上的可以在 Rainy Lake、Ash River、Crane Lake 的公司租船屋，夏天周末很早订满。三个片区之间开车要 30–60 分钟，按要坐的游船选住处。": "The only lodging in the park is the Kettle Falls Hotel, reachable only by boat (historic rooms built 1910–1913, plus villas with kitchens; guests can book the hotel's boat shuttle from the Ash River Visitor Center), along with lots of campsites you can reach only by canoe or boat. Most people stay outside the park: in International Falls to the west (the most chain hotels, about 20 minutes from the Rainy Lake Visitor Center), or at the family-run resorts on Kabetogama Lake and Ash River (cabins, most with boat rentals, open May to October). Crane Lake, to the south, has a few as well. To stay on the water, rent a houseboat from outfitters on Rainy Lake, Ash River, or Crane Lake; summer weekends book up early. The three areas are 30–60 minutes apart by car, so choose where to stay based on which boat tour you're taking.",
  "大烟山": "Great Smoky Mountains",
  "云雾缭绕的阿巴拉契亚老山与山谷农庄": "Misty old Appalachian ridges and valley farmsteads",
  "横跨田纳西和北卡两州、约 2,100 平方公里的阿巴拉契亚山地，是美国游客最多的国家公园（2025 年约 1,150 万人次）。山上终年湿润，植物蒸腾出的水汽让一层层山脊总罩着蓝色的雾，“大烟山”因此得名；这里是全世界蝾螈种类最多的地方之一，林子里有约 1,900 头黑熊。除了瀑布和老林步道，Cades Cove、Cataloochee 等山谷里还保留着 19 世纪移民留下的木屋、教堂和磨坊。公园不收门票，但 2023 年起停车超过 15 分钟要买停车证（Parking Tag）。": "About 800 square miles of Appalachian mountains straddling Tennessee and North Carolina, and the most visited national park in the U.S. (about 11.5 million visits in 2025). The mountains stay damp year-round, and vapor given off by the forest wraps the layered ridges in a blue haze—the “smoke” in the name. It's one of the world's centers of salamander diversity, and the forests hold about 1,900 black bears. Beyond waterfalls and old-growth trails, valleys like Cades Cove and Cataloochee preserve the cabins, churches, and mills of 19th-century settlers. There's no entrance fee, but since 2023 you need a parking tag to park for more than 15 minutes.",
  "4–5 月野花遍地、瀑布水量大；6 月高处杜鹃开花，夏天低处闷热潮湿、午后常有雷阵雨，山顶凉快；10 月中旬到 11 月初红叶从高处往低处走，是一年最挤的时候，周末进出 Gatlinburg 要排长队。12–3 月人少，但 Kuwohi 路、Roaring Fork 等支路关闭，Newfound Gap 公路遇冰雪会临时封。": "April–May brings wildflowers everywhere and full waterfalls. In June, rhododendrons bloom at high elevations. Summer is hot and humid down low, with frequent afternoon thunderstorms, but cool on the peaks. Fall color moves from the high country down from mid-October to early November—the most crowded time of year, with long lines into and out of Gatlinburg on weekends. December–March is quiet, but Kuwohi Road, Roaring Fork, and other side roads are closed, and Newfound Gap Road closes temporarily for ice and snow.",
  "Sugarlands · Roaring Fork（Gatlinburg 入口）": "Sugarlands / Roaring Fork (Gatlinburg entrance)",
  "Newfound Gap 公路 · 主脊（Kuwohi）": "Newfound Gap Road / main crest (Kuwohi)",
  "Little River 路 · Elkmont": "Little River Road / Elkmont",
  "Cades Cove（Townsend 一侧）": "Cades Cove (Townsend side)",
  "Oconaluftee（北卡 Cherokee 入口）": "Oconaluftee (Cherokee, N.C., entrance)",
  "Cataloochee 谷（东北角）": "Cataloochee Valley (northeast)",
  "园外：Gatlinburg · Pigeon Forge": "Outside the park: Gatlinburg / Pigeon Forge",
  "园外：蓝岭公路（北卡段）": "Outside the park: Blue Ridge Parkway (North Carolina)",
  "Sugarlands 游客中心（Gatlinburg 入口）": "Sugarlands Visitor Center (Gatlinburg entrance)",
  "园内只有走路上山才能到的 LeConte Lodge（要提前一年抢），其余都住园外。田纳西一侧的 Gatlinburg 紧挨 Sugarlands 入口，酒店、餐馆最多，但秋季和夏季周末镇上堵车厉害；Pigeon Forge 便宜一些、离公园再远 20–30 分钟；想去 Cades Cove 住 Townsend 最近，安静。Wears Valley 和 Gatlinburg 周围山坡上有大量带热水浴缸的整栋小木屋，适合一家人。北卡一侧住 Cherokee（Oconaluftee 入口外）或 Bryson City（Deep Creek 旁），看 Cataloochee 的麋鹿住 Maggie Valley。两侧之间走 Newfound Gap 公路翻山约 1 小时 15 分钟，排行程时尽量一侧连着玩。": "The only in-park lodging is LeConte Lodge, reachable only on foot (book a year ahead); everyone else stays outside the park. On the Tennessee side, Gatlinburg sits right at the Sugarlands entrance and has the most hotels and restaurants, but traffic in town is heavy on fall and summer weekends. Pigeon Forge is a bit cheaper and 20–30 minutes farther from the park. For Cades Cove, quiet Townsend is closest. Wears Valley and the hillsides around Gatlinburg have lots of whole-cabin rentals with hot tubs, good for families. On the North Carolina side, stay in Cherokee (outside the Oconaluftee entrance) or Bryson City (next to Deep Creek); for the Cataloochee elk, stay in Maggie Valley. Crossing between the two sides over Newfound Gap Road takes about 1 hour 15 minutes, so try to group each side's sights together.",
  "仙纳度": "Shenandoah",
  "蓝岭山脊上的天际线公路": "Skyline Drive along the Blue Ridge",
  "公园沿着弗吉尼亚北部的蓝岭（Blue Ridge）山脊延伸约 170 公里，离华盛顿特区只有 1.5–2 小时车程。整条山脊只有一条路：天际线公路（Skyline Drive），限速 35 英里/时，路边 70 多个观景台，西边俯瞰仙纳度河谷、东边是弗吉尼亚丘陵；阿巴拉契亚步道（Appalachian Trail）有约 160 公里和它并行。园里大多是短步道：上 Stony Man、Hawksbill 看日落，下到峡谷里看瀑布，在 Big Meadows 草甸上看鹿；最有名的是园界东侧要攀爬花岗岩巨石的 Old Rag。10 月中下旬满山红叶，是一年里最挤的时候。": "The park runs about 105 miles along the crest of the Blue Ridge in northern Virginia, just 1.5–2 hours from Washington, D.C. There's only one road along the ridge: Skyline Drive, with a 35 mph speed limit and more than 70 overlooks, looking west over the Shenandoah Valley and east over the Virginia Piedmont. The Appalachian Trail parallels it for about 100 miles. Most trails are short: climb Stony Man or Hawksbill for sunset, drop into a hollow to see a waterfall, or watch deer in Big Meadows. The best known is Old Rag, on the park's eastern edge, with its granite boulder scramble. Mid- to late October brings peak fall color and the biggest crowds of the year.",
  "4–6 月瀑布水量大、山花开（5 月野杜鹃、6 月山月桂）；7–8 月山上比河谷凉快约 5°C，但常有雾和午后雷雨；10 月中下旬是红叶高峰，周末天际线公路和热门步道口都很挤。园里的酒店、餐厅、营地大多 3–4 月开、11 月关，冬天只有公路和步道；天际线公路没有固定的冬季封路，但下雪结冰时会临时分段封闭，雪后可能好几天才重开。": "April–June brings full waterfalls and mountain blooms (wild azaleas in May, mountain laurel in June). July–August is about 10°F cooler on the ridge than in the valley, though fog and afternoon thunderstorms are common. Fall color peaks in mid- to late October, when Skyline Drive and popular trailheads are packed on weekends. Most in-park lodges, restaurants, and campgrounds open in March or April and close in November; in winter only the road and trails remain. Skyline Drive has no fixed winter closure, but sections close temporarily for snow and ice and may stay closed for days after a storm.",
  "北区（Front Royal 入口–Thornton Gap，0–31.5 英里）": "North District (Front Royal Entrance–Thornton Gap, Miles 0–31.5)",
  "中区（Thornton Gap–Swift Run Gap，31.5–65.5 英里）": "Central District (Thornton Gap–Swift Run Gap, Miles 31.5–65.5)",
  "南区（Swift Run Gap–Rockfish Gap，65.5–105 英里）": "South District (Swift Run Gap–Rockfish Gap, Miles 65.5–105)",
  "园界东侧 · Old Rag（不通天际线公路）": "Eastern edge: Old Rag (no access from Skyline Drive)",
  "园外：Luray 小镇（西侧河谷）": "Outside the park: Luray (valley to the west)",
  "Luray 小镇（Thornton Gap 入口西侧）": "Luray (west of the Thornton Gap Entrance)",
  "园内住宿都在天际线公路中段，由 Delaware North 经营：Skyland（41.7 英里，公路最高处，看日落最好）、Big Meadows Lodge（51 英里，旁边就是游客中心、草甸和加油站）和 Lewis Mountain 小木屋（57.5 英里），大约 3–5 月开到 11 月，10 月红叶季的周末很早订满。园外最方便的是西边河谷里的 Luray（到 Thornton Gap 入口约 15 分钟），周边 Page 县有大量带热水浴缸的山间小木屋；从华盛顿来、先玩北段的可以住 Front Royal；南段住 Charlottesville 或 Waynesboro，Harrisonburg 连锁酒店多、便宜。园里只有 Big Meadows 一处加油站，充电桩只在 Skyland，进山前加满、充满。": "All in-park lodging is in the central section of Skyline Drive and run by Delaware North: Skyland (Mile 41.7, the highest point on the drive, with the best sunsets), Big Meadows Lodge (Mile 51, next to the visitor center, the meadow, and a gas station), and Lewis Mountain Cabins (Mile 57.5). They open roughly March–May and stay open until November; October weekends during fall color book up very early. The most convenient town is Luray, in the valley to the west (about 15 minutes to the Thornton Gap Entrance), and surrounding Page County has lots of mountain cabins with hot tubs. Coming from Washington and starting in the north, stay in Front Royal. For the south, stay in Charlottesville or Waynesboro; Harrisonburg has lots of cheaper chain hotels. Big Meadows has the only gas station in the park and Skyland the only EV chargers, so fill up and charge before you head up.",
  "新河峡谷": "New River Gorge",
  "钢拱大桥、砂岩崖壁和美东最野的激流": "A steel arch bridge, sandstone cliffs, and the East's wildest whitewater",
  "2020 年底升格为国家公园（全称 New River Gorge National Park and Preserve），是美国最新的国家公园之一。公园沿新河延伸约 85 公里，河水在阿巴拉契亚高原上切出平均深约 300 米的峡谷；峡谷北端横跨着 1977 年建成的新河峡谷大桥，桥面离河面约 267 米，曾是世界上跨度最大的单跨钢拱桥。崖顶的砂岩峭壁是美东最有名的攀岩地，谷底的下游河段是 III–V 级的激流漂流；林子里还散落着 Thurmond、Kaymoor、Nuttallburg 这些百年前的煤矿小镇遗址。": "Upgraded to a national park at the end of 2020 (the full name is New River Gorge National Park and Preserve), it's one of the newest national parks in the U.S. The park follows the New River for about 53 miles, where it has cut a gorge averaging about 1,000 feet deep into the Appalachian Plateau. At the north end, the New River Gorge Bridge, completed in 1977, carries traffic 876 feet above the river; it was once the world's longest single-span steel arch bridge. The sandstone cliffs along the rim are the East's most famous climbing area, and the lower river runs Class III–V rapids. Scattered through the woods are the remains of century-old coal towns like Thurmond, Kaymoor, and Nuttallburg.",
  "5 月中下旬紫色杜鹃花开、6–8 月漂流季最热闹，10 月中旬红叶最盛，10 月第三个周六的桥日（Bridge Day）能走上大桥；但秋叶季周末步道口很难停车。冬天公园照常开放，游客中心大多关闭，偶尔冰雪会让峡谷里的小路难开。": "Purple rhododendrons bloom in mid- to late May, rafting season is busiest June–August, and fall color peaks in mid-October. On Bridge Day, the third Saturday in October, you can walk out on the bridge. Trailhead parking is very hard to find on fall-color weekends. The park stays open in winter, though most visitor centers close, and ice and snow occasionally make the small roads into the gorge hard to drive.",
  "大桥一带（Canyon Rim · Fayette Station）": "Bridge area (Canyon Rim, Fayette Station)",
  "北岸：Endless Wall · Nuttallburg": "North side: Endless Wall / Nuttallburg",
  "南岸：Fayetteville · Long Point · Kaymoor": "South side: Fayetteville / Long Point / Kaymoor",
  "峡谷下游河段（漂流）": "Lower Gorge (whitewater)",
  "中段：Thurmond 小镇": "Middle: Thurmond",
  "Grandview（Beckley 附近）": "Grandview (near Beckley)",
  "南段：Sandstone 瀑布 · Hinton": "South: Sandstone Falls / Hinton",
  "园外：Babcock 州立公园": "Outside the park: Babcock State Park",
  "Canyon Rim 游客中心（大桥北端）": "Canyon Rim Visitor Center (north end of the bridge)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有 8 处免费、先到先得、没有自来水的小营地（多在河边）。大多数人住大桥南边的 Fayetteville（走路就有餐馆，到 Canyon Rim、Long Point、Kaymoor 都在 10 分钟内）或旁边的 Oak Hill；大桥北边的 Adventures on the Gorge、Minden 的 ACE Adventure Resort 是漂流公司的度假村，有小木屋和营地，订漂流时一起订最方便。去 Grandview、Sandstone 瀑布住南边约 30 分钟的 Beckley（连锁酒店最多）或 Hinton 更顺路。桥日（10 月第三个周六）和红叶季的周末，Fayetteville 一带要提前几个月订。": "There are no hotels in the park, only eight small, free, first-come, first-served campgrounds without running water (mostly along the river). Most people stay in Fayetteville, just south of the bridge (restaurants within walking distance, and Canyon Rim, Long Point, and Kaymoor all within 10 minutes), or neighboring Oak Hill. Adventures on the Gorge, north of the bridge, and ACE Adventure Resort in Minden are rafting company resorts with cabins and campgrounds; booking lodging along with your rafting trip is easiest. For Grandview and Sandstone Falls, Beckley, about 30 minutes south (with the most chain hotels), or Hinton is more convenient. For Bridge Day (the third Saturday in October) and fall-color weekends, book the Fayetteville area months ahead.",
  "猛犸洞": "Mammoth Cave",
  "世界上最长的洞穴系统": "The world's longest cave system",
  "肯塔基中部的石灰岩丘陵底下，是世界上已知最长的洞穴系统：已经测绘的通道超过 430 英里（约 690 公里），而且还在不断发现新的。洞里分好几层，上层是又宽又干的大通道和巨大的洞厅，19 世纪的硝石矿遗迹、游客用烟熏在洞顶的签名都还在；东南边 Frozen Niagara 一带才有钟乳石、石笋和石瀑布。进洞都要买导览票（全年都有），大多是护林员带队，从 30 分钟的自助短线到 6 小时爬行钻洞的 Wild Cave 都有。地面上是 Green 河谷和丘陵森林，有 80 多英里步道；1981 年列为世界遗产，2021 年获国际暗夜公园认证。": "Beneath the limestone hills of central Kentucky lies the longest known cave system in the world: more than 430 miles of passages have been mapped, and more are still being found. The cave has several levels. The upper levels have wide, dry passages and huge rooms, where 19th-century saltpeter mining works and the names early visitors smoked onto the ceiling are still visible; stalactites, stalagmites, and flowstone are found only to the southeast, around Frozen Niagara. Every visit into the cave needs a tour ticket (tours run year-round), and most tours are ranger-led, from a 30-minute self-guided route to the six-hour Wild Cave crawl. Above ground are the Green River valley and wooded hills, with more than 80 miles of trails. Mammoth Cave became a World Heritage Site in 1981 and an International Dark Sky Park in 2021.",
  "洞里常年约 12°C（50 多华氏度），一年四季都能看。6–8 月和春秋学校假期最挤，导览票常提前几周卖光；夏天地面闷热潮湿、多雷阵雨、蜱虫多。10 月下旬红叶。冬天导览场次、线路都少很多（2026 年 11 月中到 2027 年 2 月每天只有四五条线），园内两个大营地 12 月到 2 月关闭。": "The cave stays around 54°F year-round, so you can visit in any season. June–August and spring and fall school breaks are the busiest, and tour tickets often sell out weeks ahead; summer above ground is hot and humid, with frequent thunderstorms and lots of ticks. Fall color arrives in late October. In winter there are far fewer tours and routes (from mid-November 2026 to February 2027, only four or five routes a day), and the park's two large campgrounds close December–February.",
  "游客中心 · 历史入口": "Visitor center / Historic Entrance",
  "Frozen Niagara · New Entrance 一带（坐车去）": "Frozen Niagara / New Entrance area (by bus)",
  "Flint Ridge · Great Onyx 洞": "Flint Ridge / Great Onyx Cave",
  "南侧：Cedar Sink · Sand Cave · Sloans Crossing": "South: Cedar Sink / Sand Cave / Sloans Crossing",
  "Green 河（划船 · 渡口）": "Green River (paddling / ferries)",
  "猛犸洞游客中心": "Mammoth Cave Visitor Center",
  "园内只有游客中心旁边的 The Lodge at Mammoth Cave（Sunset Terrace 客房、Historic Cottages、Family Cabins 全年开，便宜的 Woodland Cottages 一般 4 月到 10 月底），走路就到游客中心和历史入口，早上的导览最方便。园外最多人住东边 I-65 旁的 Cave City（53 号出口，到游客中心约 20 分钟）：连锁汽车旅馆、餐馆、加油站都在这里；南边的 Park City（48 号出口）更小更安静。Bowling Green 离游客中心约 45 分钟，酒店和超市最多。园里的 Mammoth Cave Campground 3 月到 11 月开（Recreation.gov 预订），西侧的 Houchin Ferry 小营地全年开。Green 河北岸的营地和 Brownsville 一带要坐 Green River 渡轮过河，渡轮因为水位低或涨水常停（2026 年 9 月起因水位低停运），停了就要绕路约 45 分钟。": "The only lodging in the park is The Lodge at Mammoth Cave, next to the visitor center (Sunset Terrace rooms, Historic Cottages, and Family Cabins are open year-round; the less expensive Woodland Cottages are usually open April through late October). It's a short walk to the visitor center and the Historic Entrance, the easiest setup for morning tours. Outside the park, most people stay in Cave City, on I-65 to the east (Exit 53, about 20 minutes from the visitor center), where chain motels, restaurants, and gas stations are concentrated. Park City to the south (Exit 48) is smaller and quieter. Bowling Green is about 45 minutes from the visitor center and has the most hotels and grocery stores. In the park, Mammoth Cave Campground is open March–November (reserve on Recreation.gov), and the small Houchin Ferry Campground on the west side is open year-round. To reach the campgrounds on the north bank of the Green River and the Brownsville area, you cross on the Green River Ferry, which often stops running when the water is too low or too high (it's been out of service since September 2026 because of low water); when it's down, the detour adds about 45 minutes.",
  "康加里": "Congaree",
  "美国最高的阔叶老林和柏树沼泽": "The tallest old-growth hardwood forest in the U.S., and cypress swamps",
  "南卡首府哥伦比亚东南约 30 分钟，Congaree 河和 Cedar Creek 的泛滥平原上保留着美国东南部面积最大的一片原始河漫滩阔叶林：没被砍过的火炬松、橡树、山核桃长到四五十米高，NPS 称这里是美国最高的落叶阔叶林；低洼处是膝根（cypress knees）密布的落羽杉、紫树沼泽。一年大约十次洪水把林子淹上，带来养分，也让这片地一直没被开发。大多数人走游客中心出发的约 4 公里高架木栈道，再往里走 Weston Lake 步道，或者跟导览公司在 Cedar Creek 上划独木舟；每年 5 月中旬还有同步闪光的萤火虫，要抽签才能进。": "About 30 minutes southeast of Columbia, South Carolina's capital, the floodplain of the Congaree River and Cedar Creek holds the largest remaining tract of old-growth bottomland hardwood forest in the Southeast. Never-logged loblolly pines, oaks, and hickories grow 130–160 feet tall, and the NPS calls it the tallest deciduous forest in the country. In the low spots are bald cypress and tupelo swamps bristling with cypress knees. Floods wash through the forest about 10 times a year, bringing nutrients and helping keep the land from ever being developed. Most visitors walk the elevated Boardwalk Loop, about 2.5 miles, from the visitor center, then continue on the Weston Lake Loop Trail, or paddle Cedar Creek with a guide company. Each year in mid-May, synchronous fireflies flash in unison here, and you have to win a lottery to see them.",
  "春秋最舒服：3–4 月树刚发芽、蚊子还少，10–11 月凉爽，11 月落羽杉变成铁锈红。5 月中旬是同步萤火虫季（要抽签）。6–9 月又热又闷，蚊子非常多（游客中心门口有个“蚊子指数表”），午后常有雷雨。一年约十次洪水会淹掉低处的步道和一部分木栈道，冬春最常见，出发前看公告。": "Spring and fall are the most comfortable. In March–April the trees are just leafing out and mosquitoes are still few, October–November is cool, and in November the bald cypresses turn rusty red. Mid-May is synchronous firefly season (lottery required). June–September is hot and muggy, with heavy mosquitoes (the visitor center has a “mosquito meter” out front) and frequent afternoon thunderstorms. About 10 floods a year cover low-lying trails and parts of the boardwalk, most often in winter and spring; check park alerts before you go.",
  "Harry Hampton 游客中心 · 木栈道": "Harry Hampton Visitor Center / Boardwalk",
  "Cedar Creek（South Cedar Creek 码头 · 划船）": "Cedar Creek (South Cedar Creek landing / paddling)",
  "东区：Bates Ferry（US-601）": "East: Bates Ferry (US 601)",
  "园内没有旅馆，只有两个要预订、没有自来水的帐篷营地（Longleaf 能开车到停车场，Bluff 要背东西走约 1.6 公里）。多数人住西北约 30 分钟车程的哥伦比亚（Columbia）：市中心、大学一带和 I-77 沿线连锁酒店、餐馆最多，也有不少整套民宿；从园里开回市区路上几乎没有加油站和餐馆，进园前加满油、买好吃的。从机场来最方便的是哥伦比亚机场（CAE，到公园约 35 分钟）；从夏洛特（约 1 小时 45 分钟）或查尔斯顿（约 1 小时 45 分钟）开车过来也行。附近没有出租车和网约车，必须自己开车。": "There's no lodging in the park, only two tent campgrounds that require reservations and have no running water (you can drive to the Longleaf parking lot; Bluff is about a 1-mile hike in with your gear). Most people stay in Columbia, about 30 minutes northwest: downtown, the university area, and the I-77 corridor have the most chain hotels and restaurants, plus plenty of vacation rentals. There are almost no gas stations or restaurants on the drive between the park and the city, so fill up and pick up food before you head in. The most convenient airport is Columbia Metropolitan (CAE, about 35 minutes from the park); driving from Charlotte (about 1 hour 45 minutes) or Charleston (about 1 hour 45 minutes) works too. There are no taxis or rideshares nearby, so you need your own car.",
  "温泉": "Hot Springs",
  "老城里的浴场街和 62°C 的泉水": "A historic bathhouse row and 143°F springs in the middle of town",
  "美国最特别的国家公园之一：它就在阿肯色州温泉市的老城中心。Hot Springs Mountain 山脚冒出 40 多处温泉，水温约 62°C（143°F），是约 4,000 年前落下的雨水渗进地下、被加热后再冒出来的。1832 年联邦政府就把这里划为保留地，比黄石还早 40 年；1921 年升为国家公园。主街 Central Avenue 旁的“浴场街”（Bathhouse Row）一排八座 1890–1920 年代的浴场，是当年全美最火的疗养胜地：现在 Fordyce 是游客中心和博物馆，Buckstaff 还照百年前的老规矩泡澡，Quapaw 改成了温泉池水疗馆，Superior 是用温泉水酿啤酒的啤酒厂。浴场背后的山上是约 42 公里步道和两条观景山路。": "One of the most unusual national parks in the country, set in the historic downtown of Hot Springs, Arkansas. More than 40 hot springs flow from the base of Hot Springs Mountain at about 143°F. The water fell as rain about 4,000 years ago, seeped deep underground, and was heated before rising back to the surface. The federal government set the area aside as a reservation in 1832, 40 years before Yellowstone, and it became a national park in 1921. Bathhouse Row, along Central Avenue, the main street, is a line of eight bathhouses built from the 1890s to the 1920s, when this was the most popular spa resort in America. Today the Fordyce is the visitor center and museum, the Buckstaff still offers baths the traditional way, as it has for a century, the Quapaw has become a spa with thermal pools, and the Superior is a brewery that makes beer with spring water. On the mountains behind the bathhouses are about 26 miles of trails and two scenic mountain drives.",
  "温泉一年四季都一样热，泡澡冬天最舒服。春天（3–5 月）山上的山茱萸、紫荆开花，10 月下旬到 11 月上旬红叶；6–8 月又热又湿，午后常有雷雨，体感温度超过 38°C 时户外讲解取消。城里节庆多，周末住宿更贵。": "The springs are just as hot year-round, and a soak is best in winter. In spring (March–May) dogwoods and redbuds bloom on the mountains, and fall color comes in late October to early November. June–August is hot and humid, with frequent afternoon thunderstorms; outdoor ranger programs are canceled when the heat index tops 100°F. The town has lots of festivals, and lodging costs more on weekends.",
  "浴场街（Bathhouse Row · Central Avenue）": "Bathhouse Row / Central Avenue",
  "Fordyce 浴场游客中心": "Fordyce Bathhouse Visitor Center",
  "公园就在城里，住处很多。想走路逛浴场街的住老城：浴场街北头的 Arlington Resort Hotel（1924 年的老酒店，正对浴场街）或者浴场街里 Hale 浴场改的 Hotel Hale（只有 9 间房，房间浴缸放的就是温泉水）。连锁酒店集中在城南 Central Avenue 往 Lake Hamilton 的一路上，停车方便、便宜；Lake Hamilton、Lake Ouachita 湖边有很多整套湖景民宿。园内唯一的营地 Gulpha Gorge 在城东，40 个带水电和排污的房车营位，全部要在 Recreation.gov 预订。": "The park is in town, so there are plenty of places to stay. To walk to Bathhouse Row, stay downtown: the Arlington Resort Hotel, a historic 1924 hotel facing the north end of the row, or Hotel Hale, in the converted Hale Bathhouse on the row itself (only nine rooms, with thermal water in the tubs). Chain hotels line Central Avenue south of town toward Lake Hamilton, with easy parking and lower prices, and Lake Hamilton and Lake Ouachita have many whole-house lakeview rentals. The park's only campground, Gulpha Gorge, is on the east side of town, with 40 RV sites with water, electric, and sewer hookups; all must be reserved on Recreation.gov.",
  "阿卡迪亚": "Acadia",
  "缅因海岸的粉色花岗岩与日出": "Pink granite and sunrise on the Maine coast",
  "冰川把缅因海岸的粉色花岗岩磨成圆顶山和峡湾，海浪又在山脚凿出崖壁、海蚀洞和卵石滩。公园大部分在荒漠山岛（Mount Desert Island）上：东侧的 Park Loop Road 沿海岸串起沙滩、雷鸣洞和水獭崖，再绕到乔丹池和卡迪拉克山顶，秋冬早上这里常是美国最早看到日出的地方之一；岛上还有洛克菲勒家族修的 70 多公里马车道和石桥，不许开车，只能走路、骑车、骑马。西侧人少，有 Bass Harbor 灯塔和潮池；隔海的 Schoodic 半岛更安静。": "Glaciers ground Maine's pink granite into rounded mountains and a fjord, and the surf has cut cliffs, sea caves, and cobble beaches at their base. Most of the park is on Mount Desert Island. On the east side, Park Loop Road follows the coast past Sand Beach, Thunder Hole, and Otter Cliff, then loops around to Jordan Pond and the summit of Cadillac Mountain—in fall and winter often one of the first places in the U.S. to see the sunrise. The island also has more than 45 miles of carriage roads and stone bridges built by the Rockefeller family, closed to cars and open only to walkers, cyclists, and horseback riders. The west side is quieter, with Bass Harbor Head Light and tide pools, and the Schoodic Peninsula across the bay is quieter still.",
  "6–10 月最好：7–8 月最暖、人最多，停车场一早就满；9 月到 10 月中天气清爽，10 月上中旬是红叶季，周末又挤起来。Park Loop Road 和卡迪拉克山顶路 4 月 15 日到 12 月 1 日开，冬天只有一小段和 Schoodic 环线通车；Island Explorer 免费班车大约 5 月下旬到 10 月中旬。5 月下旬到 10 月下旬开车上卡迪拉克山顶要提前在 Recreation.gov 订分时段车证。": "June–October is best. July–August is warmest and busiest, and parking lots fill early in the morning. September to mid-October is crisp and clear; fall color peaks in early to mid-October, and weekends get crowded again. Park Loop Road and Cadillac Summit Road are open April 15–December 1; in winter only a short section and the Schoodic Loop are open to cars. The free Island Explorer shuttle runs from about late May to mid-October. From late May to late October, driving to the summit of Cadillac Mountain requires a timed vehicle reservation from Recreation.gov.",
  "荒漠山岛东侧（Park Loop Road · 卡迪拉克山 · 乔丹池 · 巴尔港）": "Mount Desert Island, east (Park Loop Road, Cadillac Mountain, Jordan Pond, Bar Harbor)",
  "荒漠山岛西侧（Bass Harbor · Echo Lake · Southwest Harbor）": "Mount Desert Island, west (Bass Harbor, Echo Lake, Southwest Harbor)",
  "Schoodic 半岛（隔海，开车约 1 小时）": "Schoodic Peninsula (across the bay, about an hour's drive)",
  "Hulls Cove 游客中心（巴尔港北边）": "Hulls Cove Visitor Center (north of Bar Harbor)",
  "园内只有营地（Blackwoods、Seawall、Schoodic Woods，提前在 Recreation.gov 订），没有酒店。大多数人住巴尔港（Bar Harbor）：酒店、民宿、餐馆最多，到 Hulls Cove 游客中心约 5 分钟、到 Sand Beach 约 15 分钟，Island Explorer 班车也从镇中心发车；7–8 月和 10 月红叶季很早订满、价格高。想安静一点住西侧的 Southwest Harbor 或 Northeast Harbor（到 Bass Harbor 灯塔 10–15 分钟）；想便宜住岛外的 Trenton（约 20 分钟）或 Ellsworth（约 35 分钟）。去 Schoodic 半岛的那天可以住 Winter Harbor 一带。": "The park has only campgrounds (Blackwoods, Seawall, and Schoodic Woods; reserve ahead on Recreation.gov) and no hotels. Most people stay in Bar Harbor, which has the most hotels, inns, and restaurants, about 5 minutes from Hulls Cove Visitor Center and 15 minutes from Sand Beach; the Island Explorer also departs from the town center. July–August and October's fall-color season book up very early, at high prices. For somewhere quieter, stay on the west side in Southwest Harbor or Northeast Harbor (10–15 minutes to Bass Harbor Head Light). To save money, stay off the island in Trenton (about 20 minutes) or Ellsworth (about 35 minutes). On your Schoodic Peninsula day, you can stay around Winter Harbor.",
  "大沼泽地": "Everglades",
  "草河、鳄鱼与红树林": "River of grass, alligators, and mangroves",
  "大沼泽地其实是一条极宽极浅的“草河”：雨季的水从奥基乔比湖一带漫过锯齿草原，每天只往南流几百米，最后经红树林流进佛罗里达湾和墨西哥湾。公园约 6,100 平方公里，是美国本土最大的亚热带荒野，也是世界遗产和国际重要湿地；短吻鳄、美洲鳄、海牛、成群的涉禽和濒危的佛罗里达豹都住在这里，南佛罗里达是世界上唯一短吻鳄和美洲鳄同处一地的地方。公园三个入口互不相通：迈阿密西边 Tamiami Trail 上的 Shark Valley，Homestead 一侧一路开到海边 Flamingo 的主园路，和西北角 Everglades City 的万岛群。": "The Everglades is really an extremely wide, shallow “river of grass.” Rainy-season water spreads from the Lake Okeechobee area across sawgrass prairie, moving south only a few hundred yards a day, and finally flows through mangroves into Florida Bay and the Gulf of Mexico. At about 2,350 square miles, the park is the largest subtropical wilderness in the contiguous U.S., a World Heritage Site, and a Wetland of International Importance. American alligators, American crocodiles, manatees, flocks of wading birds, and the endangered Florida panther all live here; South Florida is the only place in the world where alligators and crocodiles live side by side. The park's three entrances don't connect: Shark Valley on the Tamiami Trail west of Miami; the Main Park Road from the Homestead side all the way to Flamingo on the coast; and the Ten Thousand Islands at Everglades City in the northwest.",
  "12 月到次年 4 月是旱季：凉快、少雨、蚊子少，水退到少数水塘边，鳄鱼和涉禽最集中，也是游客最多的时候，Shark Valley 停车场旺季上午 10 点前就满。5–11 月是雨季：湿热，几乎天天午后雷阵雨，蚊子极多（Flamingo 一带夏天尤其厉害），护林员活动也少；6–11 月是飓风季，8–10 月最要留意天气预报。": "December–April is the dry season: cool, with little rain and few mosquitoes. As the water recedes to a few ponds, alligators and wading birds concentrate there. It's also the busiest season, and the Shark Valley lot fills before 10 a.m. in peak months. May–November is the wet season: hot and humid, with afternoon thunderstorms almost daily, intense mosquitoes (especially around Flamingo in summer), and fewer ranger programs. June–November is hurricane season; watch the forecast closely August–October.",
  "Homestead 主入口 · Royal Palm": "Homestead main entrance / Royal Palm",
  "主园路（Pa-hay-okee 到 West Lake）": "Main Park Road (Pa-hay-okee to West Lake)",
  "Flamingo · 佛罗里达湾": "Flamingo / Florida Bay",
  "Gulf Coast · Everglades City（万岛群）": "Gulf Coast / Everglades City (Ten Thousand Islands)",
  "园外：Tamiami Trail · Big Cypress": "Outside the park: Tamiami Trail / Big Cypress",
  "园外：Homestead · Florida City": "Outside the park: Homestead / Florida City",
  "Ernest F. Coe 游客中心（Homestead 主入口）": "Ernest F. Coe Visitor Center (Homestead main entrance)",
  "园内能住的只有海边的 Flamingo：2023 年新建的 Flamingo Lodge（24 间集装箱改造的套房和单间）、环保帐篷、船屋和营地，离 Homestead 主入口还要开约 1 小时，冬季早订，夏天蚊子极多。去 Royal Palm、Flamingo 一侧多数人住 Florida City / Homestead：连锁汽车旅馆集中在收费公路出口，到 Ernest F. Coe 游客中心约 15 分钟，也顺路去比斯坎和佛罗里达群岛（到 Key Largo 约 30 分钟）。Shark Valley 一侧没有住宿，从迈阿密西郊开过去约 40 分钟；去 Gulf Coast 住 Everglades City 的小旅馆，或者西北约 45 分钟的那不勒斯（Naples）。三个入口之间都要绕到园外：Homestead 到 Shark Valley 约 1 小时，Shark Valley 到 Everglades City 约 1 小时。园内没有给汽车加油的地方，进去前在 Florida City 加满。": "The only in-park lodging is at Flamingo on the coast: the Flamingo Lodge, built in 2023 (24 suites and rooms made from converted shipping containers), plus eco-tents, houseboats, and a campground. It's still about an hour's drive from the Homestead main entrance; book early for winter, and expect intense mosquitoes in summer. For Royal Palm and the Flamingo side, most people stay in Florida City / Homestead, where chain motels cluster at the turnpike exits, about 15 minutes from Ernest F. Coe Visitor Center and on the way to Biscayne and the Florida Keys (about 30 minutes to Key Largo). There's no lodging on the Shark Valley side; it's about 40 minutes from Miami's western suburbs. For the Gulf Coast, stay at a small inn in Everglades City or in Naples, about 45 minutes northwest. Getting between entrances means driving around outside the park: Homestead to Shark Valley is about an hour, and Shark Valley to Everglades City is about an hour. There's no gas for cars in the park, so fill up in Florida City first.",
  "比斯坎": "Biscayne",
  "迈阿密门口的海上公园：礁岛、珊瑚礁与高脚屋": "A marine park at Miami's doorstep: keys, coral reefs, and stilt houses",
  "公园就在迈阿密市中心南边，约 95% 是水面：浅浅的比斯坎湾、佛罗里达礁岛群最北端的一串礁岛，和外侧的珊瑚礁。陆上只有 Homestead 东边 Convoy Point 的游客中心和一段海堤步道，真正的看点都要坐船：Boca Chita 岛上 1938 年建的装饰灯塔、Elliott Key 的热带硬木林、湾里的 Stiltsville 高脚屋，还有礁盘上的沉船和珊瑚。不开自己的船的话，就跟公园合作的 Biscayne National Park Institute 出海浮潜、划船或上岛。": "The park lies just south of downtown Miami and is about 95% water: shallow Biscayne Bay, a string of keys at the northern tip of the Florida Keys, and the coral reef beyond. On land there's only the visitor center at Convoy Point, east of Homestead, and a short jetty trail. The real highlights require a boat: the ornamental lighthouse built in 1938 on Boca Chita Key, the tropical hardwood forest on Elliott Key, the Stiltsville stilt houses in the bay, and shipwrecks and coral on the reef. If you don't have your own boat, go snorkeling, paddling, or island-hopping with the park's partner, the Biscayne National Park Institute.",
  "12–4 月是旱季，凉爽、蚊子少，最舒服，但冷锋过境时风大，船团可能取消；5–9 月风小水清，浮潜最好，只是湿热、午后常有雷雨；6–11 月是飓风季。岛上夏秋蚊子很凶（尤其 Elliott Key）。": "December–April is the dry season—cool, with few mosquitoes, and the most comfortable time—but cold fronts bring wind that can cancel boat tours. May–September has calmer winds and clearer water, the best snorkeling, but it's hot and humid with frequent afternoon thunderstorms. June–November is hurricane season. Mosquitoes on the islands are fierce in summer and fall (especially on Elliott Key).",
  "Convoy Point（陆上 · 游客中心）": "Convoy Point (mainland, visitor center)",
  "外侧礁岛与珊瑚礁（坐船，Convoy Point 出发）": "Outer keys and coral reef (by boat from Convoy Point)",
  "北湾 · Boca Chita · Stiltsville（坐船，Coconut Grove 出发）": "North bay: Boca Chita / Stiltsville (by boat from Coconut Grove)",
  "Homestead 一带（园外）": "Homestead area (outside the park)",
  "Dante Fascell 游客中心（Convoy Point）": "Dante Fascell Visitor Center (Convoy Point)",
  "园内没有开车能到的住处：Boca Chita 和 Elliott Key 两个岛上的营地只能自己开船去，先到先得。坐 Convoy Point 出发的船团住 Homestead / Florida City 最方便（约 15–20 分钟），这里也是去大沼泽地主入口的门户，汽车旅馆多、比迈阿密便宜；坐 Coconut Grove（Dinner Key）出发的 Boca Chita、Stiltsville 船团就住 Coconut Grove 或迈阿密市区，走路或几分钟车程就到码头。接着往礁岛群走的可以住 Key Largo，到 Convoy Point 约 50 分钟。": "There's no lodging in the park you can drive to. The campgrounds on Boca Chita Key and Elliott Key are reachable only by private boat and are first come, first served. For boat tours from Convoy Point, Homestead / Florida City is most convenient (about 15–20 minutes); it's also the gateway to the Everglades main entrance, with plenty of motels cheaper than Miami. For the Boca Chita and Stiltsville tours from Coconut Grove (Dinner Key), stay in Coconut Grove or Miami, a walk or a few minutes' drive from the marina. If you're continuing into the Keys, you can stay in Key Largo, about 50 minutes from Convoy Point.",
  "干龟": "Dry Tortugas",
  "海中央的六角形砖砌要塞": "A six-sided brick fort in the open sea",
  "Key West 以西约 110 公里，七个小沙岛和四周的珊瑚礁，公园 99% 是海。主角是 Garden Key 上的杰斐逊堡（Fort Jefferson）：1846 年开建、用了 1,600 多万块砖，是美洲最大的砖砌建筑，修了快 30 年也没完工；南北战争后当过军事监狱，因林肯遇刺案被判刑的 Samuel Mudd 医生就关在这里。要塞外的护城河墙边就能浮潜，1 月底到 7 月初成群的乌燕鸥在旁边的 Bush Key 筑巢。只能从 Key West 坐渡轮或水上飞机来，绝大多数人当天来回。": "About 70 miles west of Key West, seven small sandy islands and the surrounding coral reefs; the park is 99% water. The centerpiece is Fort Jefferson on Garden Key. Construction began in 1846, and it took more than 16 million bricks, making it the largest brick masonry structure in the Americas; after nearly 30 years of work it was never finished. After the Civil War it served as a military prison, where Dr. Samuel Mudd, convicted in the Lincoln assassination, was held. You can snorkel right along the moat wall outside the fort, and from late January to early July, sooty terns nest by the thousands on neighboring Bush Key. The only ways in are by ferry or seaplane from Key West, and most people make it a day trip.",
  "4–6 月海面相对平静、水清，春季（3–5 月）候鸟迁徙是观鸟高峰；12–3 月冷锋多，风大浪高，渡轮更颠、偶尔停航；6–11 月是飓风季，夏天湿热，有热带风暴时停航。渡轮全年每天开，冬春旺季和节假日常提前几周订满。": "April–June seas are relatively calm and the water is clear; spring (March–May) migration is peak bird-watching season. December–March brings frequent cold fronts with high winds and waves, so the ferry ride is rougher and occasionally canceled. June–November is hurricane season; summer is hot and humid, and trips are canceled for tropical storms. The ferry runs daily year-round, and in the winter-spring peak season and on holidays it often sells out weeks in advance.",
  "干龟群岛（坐渡轮 · 水上飞机）": "Dry Tortugas (by ferry or seaplane)",
  "海外公路（迈阿密开往 Key West 的路上）": "Overseas Highway (on the drive from Miami to Key West)",
  "Key West Bight 渡轮码头（Yankee Freedom 出发处）": "Key West Bight Ferry Terminal (Yankee Freedom departures)",
  "公园里唯一能过夜的是 Garden Key 上的原始营地（8 个营位加一片空地，要坐渡轮带上全部的水和装备，渡轮的露营票提前 6 个月放、很快卖完），其余的人都住 Key West 当天来回。渡轮 7:00 就要报到，住 Key West 老城最方便，走路 10–15 分钟到码头，但房价是全佛州最贵的一档，冬季和周末更贵；新城、Stock Island 的连锁酒店便宜些，开车到码头 10–15 分钟，市政停车楼 $40/天。往回 40 分钟的 Big Pine Key 一带有带厨房的整套房子；从迈阿密开车过来约 3.5–4 小时，可以在 Key Largo 或 Marathon 住一晚分两段开。": "The only overnight option in the park is the primitive campground on Garden Key (eight sites plus an overflow area). You bring all your water and gear on the ferry; ferry camping tickets are released six months ahead and sell out fast. Everyone else stays in Key West and does a day trip. Ferry check-in is at 7 a.m., so Old Town Key West is most convenient, a 10–15-minute walk to the terminal, but prices are among the highest in Florida, higher still in winter and on weekends. Chain hotels in New Town and on Stock Island are cheaper, a 10–15-minute drive to the terminal; the city parking garage is $40 a day. Around Big Pine Key, 40 minutes back up the highway, you'll find whole houses with kitchens. The drive from Miami takes about 3.5–4 hours; you can break it up with a night in Key Largo or Marathon.",
  "维尔京群岛": "Virgin Islands",
  "加勒比海的白沙湾、珊瑚礁和甘蔗种植园遗址": "White-sand bays, coral reefs, and sugar plantation ruins in the Caribbean",
  "美属维尔京群岛的圣约翰岛约六成是国家公园，另有约 2,300 公顷的海域：从山脊的干燥热带林一直到海湾里的珊瑚礁、海草床。北岸一串白沙湾一个接一个，Trunk Bay 常被评为世界上最美的海滩之一，Maho Bay 的海草床里常能看到绿海龟。林子里散落着丹麦殖民时代的甘蔗种植园和糖厂遗址，讲述着奴隶制和 1733 年奴隶起义的历史；Reef Bay 山谷里还有泰诺人留下的岩刻。1956 年 Laurance Rockefeller 把买下的土地捐给国家才建了公园。要从圣托马斯岛坐约 20 分钟的渡轮过来，岛上靠左开车。": "About 60 percent of St. John in the U.S. Virgin Islands is national park, along with about 5,700 acres of surrounding waters, from dry tropical forest on the ridges down to coral reefs and seagrass beds in the bays. A string of white-sand bays lines the north shore, one after another; Trunk Bay is often ranked among the world's most beautiful beaches, and green sea turtles are often seen in the seagrass at Maho Bay. Scattered through the forest are the ruins of sugar plantations and mills from the Danish colonial era, which tell the history of slavery and the slave revolt of 1733; the Reef Bay valley also has petroglyphs left by the Taíno. The park exists because in 1956 Laurance Rockefeller donated land he had bought to the nation. You reach St. John by a roughly 20-minute ferry ride from St. Thomas, and on the island you drive on the left.",
  "全年 25–32°C 左右。12 月到 4 月是旱季和旺季，风浪小、最舒服，但房价最高，渡轮、海滩人多；冬天偶尔有从北边来的大浪（“Christmas winds”），北岸海滩下水要小心。6–11 月是飓风季，8–10 月最容易有热带风暴，雨多、闷热，很多餐馆和度假屋 9 月前后歇业，但人少、便宜。夏天常有撒哈拉沙尘让天空发灰。": "Temperatures stay around 77–90°F year-round. December–April is the dry season and high season, with calm seas and the most comfortable weather, but also the highest rates and the busiest ferries and beaches. In winter, big swells occasionally roll in from the north (the “Christmas winds”), so take care getting into the water at north shore beaches. June–November is hurricane season, with tropical storms most likely August–October; it's rainy and muggy, and many restaurants and rentals close around September, but it's quieter and cheaper. In summer, Saharan dust often turns the sky hazy.",
  "Cruz Bay（码头 · 游客中心）": "Cruz Bay (ferry dock / visitor center)",
  "北岸海湾（North Shore Road）": "North shore bays (North Shore Road)",
  "中部山脊 · Reef Bay": "Central ridge / Reef Bay",
  "东南：Salt Pond · Ram Head": "Southeast: Salt Pond / Ram Head",
  "圣托马斯岛（园外）": "St. Thomas (outside the park)",
  "Cruz Bay（游客中心 · 客轮码头）": "Cruz Bay (visitor center / passenger ferry dock)",
  "园内能住的只有北岸的 Cinnamon Bay 海滩营地：带床和风扇的生态帐篷、水泥小屋和自带帐篷的营位，没有空调，提前 11 个月开订、最少住 2 晚（圣诞、新年、复活节等周最少 7 晚）。其余的住 Cruz Bay（码头边的小镇，酒店、度假屋、餐馆都在这里，坐客轮最方便），或者东边更安静的 Coral Bay（度假屋为主，餐馆少）。圣约翰岛整体房价高，旺季要提前很久订；想省钱可以住圣托马斯岛东头的 Red Hook 一带，每天坐客轮过去（单程约 20 分钟），但在岛上要另外租车或坐出租车。": "The only place to stay in the park is Cinnamon Bay Campground on the north shore: eco-tents with beds and fans, concrete cottages, and bare sites for your own tent, none with air conditioning. Reservations open 11 months ahead, with a two-night minimum (seven nights over the weeks of Christmas, New Year's, Easter, and other holidays). Otherwise, stay in Cruz Bay (the town by the ferry dock, with hotels, vacation rentals, and restaurants, and the easiest place for the passenger ferry) or in quieter Coral Bay to the east (mostly vacation rentals, few restaurants). Lodging on St. John is expensive across the board, so book far ahead for high season. To save money, stay around Red Hook on the east end of St. Thomas and take the passenger ferry over each day (about 20 minutes each way), but you'll need to rent a car or take taxis on St. John.",
  "德纳里": "Denali",
  "北美最高峰与苔原": "North America's highest peak and tundra",
  "北美最高峰麦金利山（6,190 米；2015–2025 年官方名称是德纳里峰）所在地，更是看野生动物的地方：灰熊、驼鹿、驯鹿、大角羊和狼。夏季私家车只能开到 Mile 15，再往里坐巴士；冬季大部分区域关闭，但能看极光、参观雪橇犬。": "Home to Mount McKinley, North America's highest peak (20,310 feet; officially named Denali from 2015 to 2025), and above all a place to see wildlife: grizzlies, moose, caribou, Dall sheep, and wolves. In summer, private vehicles can drive only to Mile 15; beyond that you ride a bus. In winter most of the park is closed, but you can see the northern lights and visit the sled dogs.",
  "6–8 月巴士运营、野生动物最多；9 月有秋色，冬季看极光。": "June–August, the buses are running and wildlife is most abundant. September brings fall color; winter is for the northern lights.",
  "入口区": "Entrance area",
  "公园路（Mile 13–15）": "Park Road (Miles 13–15)",
  "园外南侧（3 号公路）": "South of the park (Parks Highway)",
  "园内几乎没有普通酒店，住宿集中在入口外的 Nenana Canyon（酒店、餐厅、漂流公司都在这一带）和北边约 15 分钟的 Healy；夏季旺季房价高、要早订。南边的 Cantwell、Talkeetna 适合顺路过夜。": "There are almost no conventional hotels in the park. Lodging is concentrated in Nenana Canyon just outside the entrance (where the hotels, restaurants, and rafting companies are) and in Healy, about 15 minutes north. Summer prices are high, so book early. Cantwell and Talkeetna, to the south, are good overnight stops along the way.",
  "基奈峡湾": "Kenai Fjords",
  "潮水冰川与峡湾游船": "Tidewater glaciers and fjord cruises",
  "哈丁冰原覆盖了公园一半以上的面积，近 40 条冰川从冰原流下，有的一直流进海里，在峡湾尽头崩落。公园大部分只能坐船或小飞机进去，开车能到的只有 Seward 附近的 Exit Glacier；夏天从 Seward 出发的游船能开到潮水冰川前，一路常碰到座头鲸、虎鲸、海獭和海鹦。": "The Harding Icefield covers more than half the park, and nearly 40 glaciers flow from it, some all the way to the sea, where they calve at the heads of the fjords. Most of the park is reachable only by boat or small plane; the only part you can drive to is Exit Glacier near Seward. In summer, boat tours from Seward reach the face of tidewater glaciers, often passing humpback whales, orcas, sea otters, and puffins along the way.",
  "6–8 月游船班次最多、Exit Glacier 的路和步道都通；5 月和 9 月人少但天气多变；10 月底到次年 5 月中 Exit Glacier 路不通汽车，去冰川的游船也停航。": "June–August has the most boat tours, and the Exit Glacier road and trails are open. May and September are quieter, but the weather is changeable. From late October to mid-May, the Exit Glacier road is closed to cars and glacier cruises don't run.",
  "Seward 小镇": "Seward",
  "峡湾 · 复活湾（坐船）": "The fjords / Resurrection Bay (by boat)",
  "Seward 公路（安克雷奇来的路上）": "Seward Highway (on the way from Anchorage)",
  "基奈峡湾国家公园游客中心（Seward）": "Kenai Fjords National Park Visitor Center (Seward)",
  "园内没有开车能到的住宿，大家都住 Seward：港口一带酒店、民宿最多，走路就到游船码头，到 Exit Glacier 约 20 分钟；夏季房价高，7 月 4 日前后和周末很早订满。想便宜安静可以住北边约 35 分钟的 Moose Pass 或 1 小时的 Cooper Landing；从安克雷奇当天来回单程要开约 2.5 小时，也可以坐阿拉斯加铁路的火车。": "There's no lodging in the park you can drive to, so everyone stays in Seward. The harbor area has the most hotels and B&Bs, within walking distance of the tour boat docks and about 20 minutes from Exit Glacier. Summer prices are high, and dates around July 4 and weekends book up very early. For somewhere cheaper and quieter, stay in Moose Pass, about 35 minutes north, or Cooper Landing, about an hour away. A day trip from Anchorage is about 2.5 hours' drive each way, or you can take the Alaska Railroad.",
  "兰格尔–圣伊莱亚斯": "Wrangell–St. Elias",
  "美国最大的国家公园": "The largest national park in the U.S.",
  "美国面积最大的国家公园，约 5.3 万平方公里，比瑞士还大，美国 16 座最高峰里有 9 座在这里。只有两条砂石路通进来：南边的 McCarthy Road 通往 1938 年关闭的 Kennecott 铜矿镇和 Root 冰川，北边的 Nabesna Road 穿过火山和苔原；更深的地方只能坐小飞机。": "The largest national park in the U.S., at about 20,500 square miles—bigger than Switzerland—and home to 9 of the 16 highest peaks in the country. Only two gravel roads lead in: McCarthy Road in the south, to Kennecott, a copper mining town that closed in 1938, and the Root Glacier; and Nabesna Road in the north, through volcanic country and tundra. The deeper backcountry is reachable only by small plane.",
  "6–8 月 McCarthy 一带的接驳车、导览和住宿都开，路况最好；9 月上旬秋色好、人少，但店铺和导览陆续关门；冬季大部分设施关闭，McCarthy Road 只做基本养护。": "June–August, the shuttles, tours, and lodging around McCarthy are all open and the road is in its best shape. Early September has good fall color and fewer people, but shops and tours start closing. In winter most facilities close, and McCarthy Road gets only basic maintenance.",
  "Copper Center · 游客中心": "Copper Center / visitor center",
  "Nabesna Road（北侧）": "Nabesna Road (north)",
  "Richardson 公路 · Worthington 冰川": "Richardson Highway / Worthington Glacier",
  "兰格尔–圣伊莱亚斯游客中心（Copper Center）": "Wrangell–St. Elias Visitor Center (Copper Center)",
  "园内住宿集中在 McCarthy 和 Kennecott，只在夏季营业、房间少，要早订；路尽头步行桥的西岸有营地和小木屋。去 McCarthy 前一晚可以住 Copper Center 或 Glennallen（全年有旅馆、加油站和超市），第二天一早出发，到路尽头约 4–4.5 小时；多数租车公司不允许开砂石路，订车前先问清楚。": "Lodging in the park is concentrated in McCarthy and Kennecott; it's open only in summer and has few rooms, so book early. On the west side of the footbridge at the end of the road there are campgrounds and cabins. The night before driving to McCarthy, stay in Copper Center or Glennallen (hotels, gas, and groceries year-round) and leave early the next morning; the drive to the end of the road takes about 4–4.5 hours. Most rental car companies don't allow driving on gravel roads, so ask before you book.",
  "冰川湾": "Glacier Bay",
  "潮水冰川与座头鲸的海湾": "A bay of tidewater glaciers and humpback whales",
  "250 多年前整个海湾还被一条大冰川填满，一直伸到湾口的 Icy Strait；之后冰川退了约 100 公里，留下一条长长的峡湾，湾底的 Margerie、Grand Pacific 等潮水冰川还在往海里崩落，夏天湾里有座头鲸、海獭、海豹，岸上有熊和山羊。这里是 Huna 特林吉特人（Xunaa Lingít）世代的家园。多数人是坐邮轮在湾里看一天；自己来要先飞到 Gustavus（从朱诺没有公路），住在湾口的 Bartlett Cove 或 Gustavus 小镇，再坐每天一班的游船进湾。": "Just over 250 years ago, a single great glacier filled the entire bay, reaching all the way to Icy Strait at its mouth. The ice has since retreated about 65 miles, leaving a long fjord. At its head, tidewater glaciers such as Margerie and Grand Pacific still calve into the sea. In summer the bay has humpback whales, sea otters, and seals, and bears and mountain goats roam the shore. This is the ancestral homeland of the Huna Tlingit (Xunaa Lingít). Most visitors see the bay in a day from a cruise ship. On your own, fly to Gustavus first (there's no road from Juneau), stay at Bartlett Cove or in Gustavus, and take the once-daily boat tour up the bay.",
  "5 月下旬到 9 月上旬 Glacier Bay Lodge、游客中心和进湾的游船都开（2026 年是 5 月 22 日到 9 月 7 日），7 月人最多；座头鲸 6 月中以后多起来，7–8 月最多。4–6 月雨相对少，9–10 月雨最多；冬季几乎所有服务都关，只有小飞机进出。": "From late May to early September, Glacier Bay Lodge, the visitor center, and the boat tour up the bay are all running (May 22–September 7 in 2026); July is the busiest month. Humpback whales become more numerous after mid-June, peaking July–August. April–June is relatively dry, September–October the wettest. In winter almost all services close, and access is by small plane only.",
  "Bartlett Cove（公园总部）": "Bartlett Cove (park headquarters)",
  "冰川湾里（坐船 · 坐飞机）": "Glacier Bay (by boat or plane)",
  "Gustavus 小镇 · Icy Strait": "Gustavus / Icy Strait",
  "冰川湾游客中心（Bartlett Cove 的 Glacier Bay Lodge 二楼）": "Glacier Bay Visitor Center (second floor of Glacier Bay Lodge, Bartlett Cove)",
  "园内只有 Bartlett Cove 的 Glacier Bay Lodge（2026 年 5 月 21 日到 9 月 8 日营业），游客中心在酒店二楼，进湾的游船就在门口码头上船；其余住处都在约 16 公里外的 Gustavus 小镇，有民宿、小木屋和几家包三餐的度假屋，夏季要早订。从朱诺没有公路：Alaska Airlines 夏季每天一班喷气机（2026 年 6 月 6 日到 8 月 30 日，约 30 分钟），Alaska Seaplanes 的小飞机全年每天都飞，州营渡轮夏季大约每周两班。Gustavus 只有一家小租车行，多数人靠酒店接驳车、出租车和自行车。不少人是坐邮轮在湾里看一天，不上岸过夜；Bartlett Cove 还有一个免费、不能预约的步行进入式帐篷营地。": "The only lodging in the park is Glacier Bay Lodge at Bartlett Cove (open May 21–September 8, 2026). The visitor center is on the lodge's second floor, and the boat tour up the bay boards at the dock out front. Everything else is in Gustavus, about 10 miles away, which has B&Bs, cabins, and a few inns that include all meals; book early for summer. There's no road from Juneau: Alaska Airlines runs one jet flight a day in summer (June 6–August 30, 2026, about 30 minutes), Alaska Seaplanes flies small planes daily year-round, and the state ferry runs about twice a week in summer. Gustavus has just one small car rental, and most people get around by lodge shuttle, taxi, and bicycle. Many visitors see the bay in a day from a cruise ship and never stay ashore. Bartlett Cove also has a free walk-in tent campground that can't be reserved.",
  "北极之门": "Gates of the Arctic",
  "没有路也没有步道的北极荒野": "Arctic wilderness with no roads or trails",
  "美国最北、面积第二大的国家公园，整个在北极圈以北：布鲁克斯山脉中部 3.4 万平方公里的荒野里没有一条公路、一条步道，也没有任何设施，一年只有一万多人次来。名字是 1930 年代 Bob Marshall 起的，他把 Koyukuk 河北叉两岸对峙的 Frigid Crags 和 Boreal Mountain 叫作“北极之门”。普通游客有两种去法：从费尔班克斯沿砂石为主的 Dalton 公路开约 6 小时到 Coldfoot、Wiseman，公园东界就在公路以西几公里到十来公里，但没有路，要自己越野走进去；或者从 Coldfoot、Bettles、费尔班克斯坐小飞机飞进山里，在湖上降落看一看。": "The northernmost and second-largest national park in the U.S., lying entirely north of the Arctic Circle. Its roughly 13,000 square miles of wilderness in the central Brooks Range have no roads, no trails, and no facilities of any kind, and it sees only about 10,000 visits a year. The name comes from Bob Marshall, who in the 1930s called Frigid Crags and Boreal Mountain, facing each other across the North Fork of the Koyukuk River, the “gates of the Arctic.” There are two ways for most visitors to go. Drive about six hours from Fairbanks up the mostly gravel Dalton Highway to Coldfoot and Wiseman; the park's eastern boundary is just a few miles to about 7 miles west of the highway, but there's no road, so you'd have to hike in cross-country. Or take a small plane from Coldfoot, Bettles, or Fairbanks into the mountains and land on a lake for a look around.",
  "6–8 月是主要季节：午夜太阳、苔原开花，Coldfoot 的观光飞行 6 月到 9 月中营业，但 6 月中到 8 月蚊子极多；8 月下旬到 9 月初秋色最好、开始能看到极光，也可能下雪。Dalton 公路全年通车，但 10 月下旬到次年 4 月上旬冰雪、极寒，BLM 不建议自驾，冬天去 Coldfoot 看极光一般跟团。": "June–August is the main season, with the midnight sun and tundra in bloom; flightseeing from Coldfoot runs June to mid-September, but mosquitoes are intense from mid-June through August. Late August to early September has the best fall color and the first northern lights, but it can also snow. The Dalton Highway is open year-round, but from late October to early April it's icy and bitterly cold, and the BLM advises against driving it; winter aurora trips to Coldfoot are generally done with a tour.",
  "Dalton 公路南段（育空河 · 北极圈）": "Dalton Highway, south (Yukon River, Arctic Circle)",
  "Dalton 公路北段（Sukakpak 山 · Atigun 山口）": "Dalton Highway, north (Sukakpak Mountain, Atigun Pass)",
  "坐小飞机进园": "Flying into the park",
  "北极跨部门游客中心（Coldfoot，Dalton 公路 175 英里处）": "Arctic Interagency Visitor Center (Coldfoot, Dalton Highway Mile 175)",
  "园内没有任何住宿和营地设施。开车去的话住 Dalton 公路 175 英里处的 Coldfoot Camp：全年营业，旅馆由输油管工地的工人宿舍改建，每间两张单人床、带卫浴，2026 年 $269/晚，夏季旅行团多、要早订；也可以住往北约 20 分钟的 Wiseman 村里两家家庭经营的小木屋民宿（房间很少），自带帐篷的可以住 Coldfoot Camp 的免费营地或北边 5 英里的 BLM Marion Creek 营地。往返路上的第一晚、最后一晚住费尔班克斯，想把 6 小时的路拆开可以住 56 英里处育空河边的 Yukon River Camp。另一个门户村 Bettles 只能坐飞机去（从费尔班克斯约 1 小时），村里的 Bettles Lodge 全年营业，常和观光飞行、极光打包卖；园内和园边还有 Iniakuk Lake 这类只能飞进去的荒野小屋，都要提前订。": "There's no lodging or campground of any kind in the park. If you're driving, stay at Coldfoot Camp at Mile 175 of the Dalton Highway. It's open year-round; the inn is converted from pipeline construction worker housing, and each room has two twin beds and a private bath ($269 a night in 2026). Summer tour groups fill it, so book early. You can also stay in one of the two family-run cabin B&Bs in Wiseman, about 20 minutes north (very few rooms). With your own tent, you can camp free at Coldfoot Camp or at the BLM's Marion Creek Campground, 5 miles north. Spend your first and last nights in Fairbanks; to split up the six-hour drive, stay at Yukon River Camp, at Mile 56 by the Yukon River. The other gateway village, Bettles, is reachable only by air (about an hour from Fairbanks); Bettles Lodge there is open year-round and is often sold as a package with flightseeing and aurora viewing. In and around the park there are also fly-in wilderness lodges such as Iniakuk Lake; book all of these ahead.",
  "科伯克谷": "Kobuk Valley",
  "北极圈里的沙丘与驯鹿渡口": "Arctic sand dunes and caribou crossings",
  "布鲁克斯山脉南麓的一片宽谷，在北极圈以北约 50 公里，最出名的是冰期留下的沙丘：三片沙丘共约 78 平方公里，最大的科伯克大沙丘高约 30 米，夏天沙面能晒到 38°C，是北极最大的活动沙丘。Kobuk（Iñupiaq 语“大河”）河从谷中穿过，西部北极驯鹿群每年春秋渡河，Onion Portage 一带的渡口已有 8,000 多年的狩猎历史。公园没有路、步道和任何设施，要从海边小城 Kotzebue 坐小飞机进去，降落在沙丘上或河面上。": "A broad valley on the south side of the Brooks Range, about 30 miles north of the Arctic Circle, best known for sand dunes left by the Ice Age. Three dunefields cover about 30 square miles; the largest, the Great Kobuk Sand Dunes, rise about 100 feet, and in summer the sand can heat up to 100°F. They're the largest active dunes in the Arctic. The Kobuk River (“big river” in Iñupiaq) runs through the valley, and the Western Arctic caribou herd crosses it every spring and fall; the crossing at Onion Portage has been a hunting site for more than 8,000 years. The park has no roads, trails, or facilities of any kind. You fly in by small plane from the coastal town of Kotzebue, landing on the dunes or on the river.",
  "6–9 月才有观光飞行和背包客：7 月最暖，6、7 月蚊子最多，8、9 月虫子少、秋色好，晚上开始能看到极光；驯鹿秋季南迁渡河 2000 年以前多在 8 月中下旬开始，近年常拖到 9 月以后甚至 10–11 月。9 月中下旬河面开始结冰，10 月到次年 5 月冰雪覆盖，只有天气好时的包机。": "Flightseeing and backpacking happen only June–September. July is warmest; June and July have the most mosquitoes; August and September have fewer bugs, good fall color, and the first northern lights at night. Before 2000, the caribou's fall migration across the river usually began in mid- to late August; in recent years it has often been delayed to after September, or even to October–November. The river starts freezing in mid- to late September, and from October to May the valley is covered in ice and snow, with charter flights only in good weather.",
  "Kotzebue（科策布）": "Kotzebue",
  "科伯克河谷（坐小飞机）": "Kobuk River valley (by small plane)",
  "西北极遗产中心（Kotzebue 的公园游客中心）": "Northwest Arctic Heritage Center (park visitor center in Kotzebue)",
  "园内没有住宿和营地设施，进园前后都住 Kotzebue：Nullagvik 酒店最大（79 间房，原住民公司 NANA 开的），离机场、游客中心和小飞机机库都走得到；另有几家家庭民宿，有的挂在 Airbnb 上。镇上房间不多，夏季和秋季打猎季常被工作的人订满，订好机票就订房。Kotzebue 没有户外装备出租，要在园里露营就自带装备，防熊食物桶可以在遗产中心借；漂流 Kobuk 河的人从上游的 Ambler 村下水、到下游的 Kiana 村上岸，两个村子都只有很少的补给，吃的用的在 Kotzebue 买齐。": "There's no lodging or campground in the park, so stay in Kotzebue before and after. The Nullagvik Hotel is the largest (79 rooms, owned by the Alaska Native corporation NANA), within walking distance of the airport, the visitor center, and the air taxi hangars. There are also a few family-run B&Bs, some listed on Airbnb. The town has few rooms, and in summer and fall hunting season they're often booked by people working there, so book your room as soon as you book your flight. Kotzebue has no outdoor gear rentals: if you're camping in the park, bring your own gear; bear-resistant food containers can be borrowed at the Heritage Center. River trips on the Kobuk put in at the upstream village of Ambler and take out at Kiana downstream; both villages have very limited supplies, so buy everything in Kotzebue.",
  "卡特迈": "Katmai",
  "Brooks 瀑布的棕熊与万烟谷": "Brooks Falls bears and the Valley of Ten Thousand Smokes",
  "全园估计有约 2,200 头棕熊，是世界上看熊最好的地方之一：7 月红鲑逆流跳过 Brooks 瀑布，棕熊就站在瀑布顶上张嘴接鱼；太平洋海岸的草甸和泥滩上，熊在吃莎草、挖蛤蜊。1912 年 Novarupta 火山爆发是 20 世纪最大的一次喷发，火山灰把一整条山谷填成了“万烟谷”。公园不通公路，要从 Homer、安克雷奇或 King Salmon 坐小飞机进去，多数人当天来回。": "The park has an estimated 2,200 brown bears and is one of the best places in the world to watch them. In July, sockeye salmon leap up Brooks Falls while bears stand at the lip with their mouths open to catch them; on the Pacific coast, bears graze on sedge and dig for clams in the meadows and mudflats. The 1912 eruption of Novarupta was the largest of the 20th century, and its ash filled an entire valley, creating the Valley of Ten Thousand Smokes. No road reaches the park. You fly in by small plane from Homer, Anchorage, or King Salmon, and most people make it a day trip.",
  "Brooks Camp 的护林员、Brooks Lodge 和定期航班大约只在 6 月 1 日到 9 月 17 日（2026 年 Brooks Lodge、Katmai Air 到 9 月 18 日）；Brooks 瀑布熊最多的是 7 月（抓跳跃的红鲑）和 9 月（在下游吃产完卵的鱼），6 月和 8 月有时一整天看不到熊。海岸看熊 6–8 月最好，Homer 的看熊航班大约 5 月中到 9 月中飞；冬季没有服务。": "Brooks Camp rangers, Brooks Lodge, and scheduled flights operate only from about June 1 to September 17 (in 2026, Brooks Lodge and Katmai Air run through September 18). Brooks Falls has the most bears in July (catching jumping sockeye) and September (eating spent salmon downstream); in June and August you may go a whole day without seeing a bear. Coastal bear viewing is best June–August, and bear-viewing flights from Homer run from about mid-May to mid-September. There are no services in winter.",
  "Brooks Camp（坐水上飞机）": "Brooks Camp (by floatplane)",
  "卡特迈海岸（坐小飞机）": "Katmai Coast (by small plane)",
  "万烟谷": "Valley of Ten Thousand Smokes",
  "Homer（Beluga 湖水上飞机基地，看熊一日游出发地）": "Homer (Beluga Lake floatplane base, bear-viewing day trip departures)",
  "园内的住处都只能坐飞机进去：Brooks Camp 的 Brooks Lodge 只有 16 间房，旺季要提前一年半抽签（2028 年的在 2026 年 12 月 1–30 日报名），旁边的 Brooks Camp 营地在 Recreation.gov 预约，另外还有几家飞进去的钓鱼、看熊度假屋。所以多数人住在开车能到的出发地、当天来回：Homer 的 Beluga 湖边、市区和 Homer Spit 都有酒店民宿，去 Brooks 和海岸看熊都从这里飞，离安克雷奇约 4.5 小时车程；不想去 Homer 的可以住安克雷奇，坐 Katmai Air、Rust's 的一日游。经 King Salmon 进出的住镇上的小旅馆，那里和公路网不通。": "All lodging in the park is fly-in only. Brooks Lodge at Brooks Camp has just 16 rooms, and peak-season stays are awarded by lottery about a year and a half ahead (for 2028, apply December 1–30, 2026). The adjacent Brooks Camp Campground is reserved on Recreation.gov, and there are a few fly-in fishing and bear-viewing lodges. So most people stay somewhere they can drive to and make a day trip. Homer has hotels and B&Bs along Beluga Lake, in town, and on the Homer Spit; flights to Brooks and the coast both leave from here, and it's about 4.5 hours' drive from Anchorage. If you'd rather not go to Homer, stay in Anchorage and take a day trip with Katmai Air or Rust's. If you're going through King Salmon, stay at one of the small inns in town, which isn't connected to the road system.",
  "克拉克湖": "Lake Clark",
  "火山、冰川湖与海岸棕熊": "Volcanoes, glacial lakes, and coastal brown bears",
  "在安克雷奇西南约 200 公里，阿拉斯加山脉和阿留申山脉在这里相接：Redoubt、Iliamna 两座活火山终年积雪，山谷里挂着冰川，Lake Clark、Twin Lakes、Crescent 湖这些冰川湖是青绿色的。Cook 湾海岸的盐沼和泥滩上常能一次看到一二十头棕熊；Twin Lakes 湖边是 Dick Proenneke 1960 年代末亲手盖、独自住了约 30 年的小木屋。公园不通公路，从安克雷奇坐小飞机约 1 小时，多数人当天来回。": "About 125 miles southwest of Anchorage, where the Alaska Range meets the Aleutian Range. Two active volcanoes, Redoubt and Iliamna, are snowcapped year-round, glaciers hang in the valleys, and glacial lakes such as Lake Clark, Twin Lakes, and Crescent Lake are a milky turquoise. On the salt marshes and mudflats of the Cook Inlet coast you can often see 10 or 20 brown bears at once. On the shore of Twin Lakes is the cabin Dick Proenneke built by hand in the late 1960s and lived in alone for about 30 years. No road reaches the park; it's about an hour by small plane from Anchorage, and most people make it a day trip.",
  "6–9 月看熊团、航班最多，Port Alsworth 的游客中心只在 6–8 月开；海岸看熊 6 月到 8 月最好（初夏在盐沼吃莎草，夏末到溪口抓鲑鱼），Crescent 湖看熊在 8–9 月鲑鱼季；Proenneke 小屋大约 5 月底湖面化冰后到 9 月底开放。冬季基本只能包机。": "June–September has the most bear-viewing trips and flights; the visitor center in Port Alsworth is open only June–August. Coastal bear viewing is best June–August (in early summer bears graze sedge in the salt marshes; in late summer they fish for salmon at creek mouths), and bear viewing at Crescent Lake peaks with the salmon run in August–September. Proenneke's cabin is open from about late May, after the lake ice melts, to late September. In winter, access is basically by charter only.",
  "Cook 湾海岸（坐小飞机）": "Cook Inlet coast (by small plane)",
  "Crescent 湖（坐水上飞机）": "Crescent Lake (by floatplane)",
  "Twin Lakes（坐水上飞机）": "Twin Lakes (by floatplane)",
  "Port Alsworth · Lake Clark 湖": "Port Alsworth / Lake Clark",
  "安克雷奇 Lake Hood 水上飞机基地（一日游出发地）": "Lake Hood Seaplane Base, Anchorage (day-trip departures)",
  "园内的住处都只能飞进去：Port Alsworth 有八九家小旅馆和一个私营营地，海岸的 Silver Salmon Creek、Chinitna 湾和 Crescent 湖边有几家看熊、钓鱼的度假屋，Lake Clark 湖边还有两座在 Recreation.gov 预订的公共小木屋，Twin Lakes 有不用预约的简易营地。多数人住在安克雷奇当天来回：Lake Hood 旁的机场酒店区离水上飞机最近，市中心选择最多。去海岸看熊也可以住 Homer 或 Soldotna，从那里飞更近、更便宜。": "All lodging in the park is fly-in only. Port Alsworth has eight or nine small lodges and a private campground. On the coast, Silver Salmon Creek, Chinitna Bay, and Crescent Lake have a few bear-viewing and fishing lodges. There are also two public-use cabins on Lake Clark, reserved on Recreation.gov, and a primitive campground at Twin Lakes that doesn't take reservations. Most people stay in Anchorage and make a day trip: the airport hotels near Lake Hood are closest to the floatplanes, and downtown has the most choices. For coastal bear viewing, you can also stay in Homer or Soldotna; flights from there are shorter and cheaper.",
  "夏威夷火山": "Hawaiʻi Volcanoes",
  "活火山口边的熔岩红光": "Glowing lava at the edge of an active crater",
  "公园里有地球上最活跃的火山之一基拉韦厄（Kīlauea），和体积最大的活火山冒纳罗亚（Mauna Loa）。基拉韦厄山顶的破火山口边上有一圈观景台和步道，能看到 2018 年塌陷后的 Halemaʻumaʻu 火山口、冒着蒸汽的喷气孔、熔岩管和 1959 年的熔岩湖；火山口链公路（Chain of Craters Road）从山顶一路下到海边，沿途是几十年间新流出的熔岩原。2024 年 12 月起，山顶的 Halemaʻumaʻu 火山口里间歇喷发：每次熔岩喷泉持续几个小时，间隔几天到几周，喷发时在火山口边的观景台就能看到。": "The park holds Kīlauea, one of the most active volcanoes on Earth, and Mauna Loa, the largest active volcano by volume. Overlooks and trails ring the caldera at Kīlauea's summit, with views of Halemaʻumaʻu crater after its 2018 collapse, steaming vents, lava tubes, and the 1959 lava lake. Chain of Craters Road descends from the summit to the sea, crossing lava fields laid down over recent decades. Since December 2024, Halemaʻumaʻu has been erupting episodically: each episode's lava fountains last a few hours, with days to weeks between them, and during an eruption you can watch from the overlooks on the crater rim.",
  "全年开放、24 小时都能进。山顶海拔约 1,200 米，常年凉爽多雨，夜里常在 10°C 上下；12–1 月和 6–7 月游客最多、停车最难，4–5 月和 9–10 月人少一些。火山喷发不分季节，出发前看 USGS 夏威夷火山观测站的每日公告；6–11 月是飓风季，2026 年 8 月（飓风 Lala）和 9 月（Nolo）公园都因风暴临时关过。": "Open year-round, 24 hours a day. The summit sits at about 4,000 feet and is cool and rainy all year, with nights often around 50°F. December–January and June–July are the busiest months, with the hardest parking; April–May and September–October are quieter. Eruptions don't follow the seasons, so check the USGS Hawaiian Volcano Observatory's daily update before you go. June–November is hurricane season; in 2026 the park closed temporarily for storms in August (Hurricane Lala) and September (Nolo).",
  "Kīlauea 山顶 · 火山口边缘": "Kīlauea summit / caldera rim",
  "火山口链公路（Chain of Craters Road）": "Chain of Craters Road",
  "冒纳罗亚路（Mauna Loa Road）": "Mauna Loa Road",
  "Kahuku 园区（Kaʻū 南部，周四到周日开）": "Kahuku Unit (southern Kaʻū, open Thursday–Sunday)",
  "园外顺路（希洛、Punaluʻu 黑沙滩）": "On the way (Hilo, Punaluʻu Black Sand Beach)",
  "夏威夷火山国家公园入口（Volcano 村旁）": "Hawaiʻi Volcanoes National Park entrance (next to Volcano Village)",
  "园内开车能到的住处只有火山口边上的 Volcano House 酒店（33 间房）和往西约 5 公里 Nāmakanipaio 营地的 10 间小木屋，都由 Volcano House 经营，常常很早订满。多数人住入口外约 2 公里的 Volcano 村：雨林里的民宿、小木屋很多，有两家小超市和加油站，开到山顶观景台约 10 分钟，夜里看完火山红光回去最方便。希洛（Hilo）酒店、餐馆多，到公园约 45 分钟；科纳（Kona）的度假酒店单程约 2.5 小时，只适合当天来回或者顺路过来。园内的 Kilauea Military Camp 只接待军人等有资格的客人，一般游客不能住。": "The only in-park lodging you can drive to is the Volcano House hotel on the crater rim (33 rooms) and the 10 cabins at Nāmakanipaio Campground, about 3 miles west; both are run by Volcano House and often book up early. Most people stay in Volcano Village, about a mile outside the entrance. It has plenty of B&Bs and cabins in the rain forest, two small grocery stores, and gas, about 10 minutes from the summit overlooks—the easiest place to get back to after watching the glow at night. Hilo has more hotels and restaurants, about 45 minutes from the park. The resort hotels in Kona are about 2.5 hours each way, suitable only for a day trip or if the park is on your route. Kilauea Military Camp in the park hosts only military members and other eligible guests; the general public can't stay there.",
  "哈莱阿卡拉": "Haleakalā",
  "云海之上的火山口日出": "Sunrise over the clouds from a volcanic summit",
  "茂宜岛东半边就是一座巨大的盾状火山，最高点 Puʻuʻulaʻula 海拔 3,055 米。山顶的“火山口”其实是雨水侵蚀出来的大山谷，长约 12 公里、宽约 4 公里，谷底散落着红、黑、橙色的渣锥；在云海之上看日出、日落和星空是这里的招牌，还能看到只长在这座山上的银剑草和夏威夷雁。公园的另一半在东南海岸的 Kīpahulu，和山顶不通路，要走哈纳公路过去：雨林、竹林步道和一串流进大海的瀑布水潭。": "The eastern half of Maui is one huge shield volcano, topping out at 10,023 feet at Puʻuʻulaʻula. The summit “crater” is actually a great valley eroded by rain, about 7 miles long and 2.5 miles wide, its floor scattered with red, black, and orange cinder cones. Sunrise, sunset, and stars above the clouds are the signature experiences, and you can see silverswords, found only on this mountain, and nēnē (Hawaiian geese). The other half of the park is Kīpahulu, on the southeast coast; no road connects it to the summit, so you take the Road to Hāna to get there, for rain forest, a bamboo-forest trail, and a string of waterfall pools flowing into the sea.",
  "全年开放、24 小时都能进，但凌晨 3–7 点进山顶区要提前订日出预约。山顶比海边冷十几到二十几度，日出前常在 0°C 上下，冬天偶尔下雪结冰；12–3 月游客最多，日落前山顶停车场常满。5–10 月是夏威夷的旱季，银剑草多在夏天开花；Kīpahulu 一年到头湿热多雨，冬天雨更多、溪水容易暴涨。": "Open year-round, 24 hours a day, but entering the Summit District between 3 and 7 a.m. requires a sunrise reservation made in advance. The summit is roughly 20–40°F colder than the coast, often around freezing before sunrise, with occasional snow and ice in winter. December–March is the busiest season, and the summit parking lot often fills before sunset. May–October is Hawaiʻi's dry season, and silverswords mostly bloom in summer. Kīpahulu is hot, humid, and rainy year-round, wetter in winter, when streams can rise suddenly.",
  "山顶区（Summit District）": "Summit District",
  "Kīpahulu 区（哈纳以南的海岸）": "Kīpahulu District (coast south of Hāna)",
  "哈纳公路（去 Kīpahulu 的路上）": "Road to Hāna (on the way to Kīpahulu)",
  "哈莱阿卡拉公园总部游客中心（山顶区）": "Haleakalā Park Headquarters Visitor Center (Summit District)",
  "园内没有酒店，只有山顶区的 Hosmer Grove 和海边的 Kīpahulu 两个小营地（都要在 Recreation.gov 提前 30 天内订），以及要徒步下到火山口里的三间荒野小屋。看日出的人多住山腰的 Kula 或 Pukalani、Makawao 一带，开到山顶约 1–1.5 小时；住机场旁的卡胡卢伊或北岸小镇 Paia 约 1.5–2 小时，Paia 也是哈纳公路的起点。去 Kīpahulu 最好在哈纳（Hāna）住一晚，开到瀑布步道约 30 分钟。南岸的 Kīhei、Wailea 度假区去山顶要 2–2.5 小时，凌晨出发看日出很辛苦。": "There are no hotels in the park, only two small campgrounds, Hosmer Grove in the Summit District and Kīpahulu on the coast (both reserved on Recreation.gov, up to 30 days ahead), plus three wilderness cabins you hike down into the crater to reach. For sunrise, most people stay upcountry in Kula, Pukalani, or Makawao, about 1–1.5 hours' drive to the summit. Kahului, by the airport, or the north shore town of Paia is about 1.5–2 hours away; Paia is also where the Road to Hāna begins. For Kīpahulu, spend a night in Hāna, about 30 minutes' drive from the waterfall trail. The south shore resorts of Kīhei and Wailea are 2–2.5 hours from the summit, a tough predawn drive for sunrise.",
  "美属萨摩亚": "National Park of American Samoa",
  "南太平洋的雨林、果蝠和珊瑚礁": "Rainforest, fruit bats, and coral reefs in the South Pacific",
  "美国唯一在赤道以南的国家公园，在夏威夷西南约 4,200 公里，分在三座火山岛上：主岛图图伊拉岛北岸的雨林和海崖，东边曼努阿群岛的 Ofu 岛珊瑚礁潟湖和 Ta'u 岛（美属萨摩亚最高的 Lata 山，966 米）。林子是和亚洲、非洲同源的旧热带雨林，唯一的本地哺乳动物是翼展近 1 米的果蝠，白天也常在树冠上飞；海里记录到 950 多种鱼、250 多种珊瑚。公园的土地是向当地村子租来的，萨摩亚人的生活方式（fa'asamoa）就在公园里：进村前先问许可，周日要安静，傍晚的祈祷时间（sā）要停下来等。几乎没有一般国家公园的设施，适合有探险精神的人。": "The only U.S. national park south of the equator, about 2,600 miles southwest of Hawaiʻi, spread across three volcanic islands: the rainforest and sea cliffs on the north shore of Tutuila, the main island, and, in the Manu'a Islands to the east, the coral reef lagoon of Ofu and the island of Ta'u, home to Lata Mountain, the highest point in American Samoa at 3,170 feet. The forest is paleotropical rainforest, related to the forests of Asia and Africa. The only native mammals are fruit bats with wingspans of nearly 3 feet, often seen flying over the canopy even in daytime. More than 950 species of fish and more than 250 species of coral have been recorded offshore. The park's land is leased from local villages, and fa'asamoa, the Samoan way of life, is part of the park: ask permission before entering a village, keep quiet on Sundays, and stop and wait during the evening prayer time (sā). The park has almost none of the usual national park facilities, so it suits travelers with a sense of adventure.",
  "全年都是 28–31°C 左右的高温高湿。6–9 月是稍凉、稍干的季节，最适合徒步；10 月到次年 5 月是漫长的雨季，热带风暴多，12–2 月雨最多。8–11 月常能看到南半球的座头鲸。周日几乎所有商店关门、公交停开，很多村子不让游泳、不让上部分步道，排行程时把周日当休息日。": "It's hot and humid year-round, around 82–88°F. June–September is a bit cooler and drier and the best time for hiking; October–May is a long rainy season with frequent tropical storms, and December–February is the wettest. Humpback whales from the Southern Hemisphere are often seen August–November. On Sundays almost every store closes and the buses stop running, and many villages don't allow swimming or use of some trails, so plan Sunday as a rest day.",
  "帕果帕果和港湾（游客中心）": "Pago Pago and the harbor (visitor center)",
  "Vatia 一带（北岸）": "Vatia area (north shore)",
  "Mount 'Alava 山脊": "Mount 'Alava ridge",
  "'Aunu'u 岛（园外）": "'Aunu'u Island (outside the park)",
  "Ofu 岛（坐小飞机）": "Ofu (by small plane)",
  "Ta'u 岛（坐小飞机）": "Ta'u (by small plane)",
  "帕果帕果（公园游客中心）": "Pago Pago (park visitor center)",
  "公园里没有住宿。图图伊拉岛上住帕果帕果港湾一带（Utulei 的 Sadie's by the Sea 在海边、Fagatogo 有老旅馆 Sadie Thompson Inn）或机场附近的 Tafuna（Tradewinds Hotel 最大，还有几家小旅馆和 Airbnb），到公园北岸开车都在 30–40 分钟以内。曼努阿群岛只有几家小旅馆（Ofu 岛的 Vaoto Lodge、Ta'u 岛的 Fitiuta Lodge 等），要和机票一起提前订，岛上没有餐馆和商店，吃住都靠旅馆。公园以前协助安排的村民家寄宿（homestay，Vatia、Fagasā、Fiti'uta 等村）现在开不开没能确认，想住要先发邮件问公园。": "There's no lodging in the park. On Tutuila, stay around Pago Pago Harbor (Sadie's by the Sea on the water in Utulei, or the historic Sadie Thompson Inn in Fagatogo) or in Tafuna near the airport (Tradewinds Hotel is the largest, plus a few small hotels and Airbnbs); from either, the park's north shore is a 30–40-minute drive. The Manu'a Islands have only a few small lodges (such as Vaoto Lodge on Ofu and Fitiuta Lodge on Ta'u); book them well ahead, along with your flights. There are no restaurants or stores on those islands, so you rely on your lodge for meals. The park used to help arrange homestays with village families (in Vatia, Fagasā, Fiti'uta, and other villages); we couldn't confirm whether the program is running now, so email the park first if you're interested.",
  "班夫": "Banff",
  "加拿大国家公园管理局（Parks Canada）": "Parks Canada",
  "冰川湖与落基山雪峰": "Glacial lakes and Rocky Mountain peaks",
  "1885 年设立的加拿大第一座国家公园，也是落基山最热门的一座：露易丝湖、梦莲湖、佩托湖这些冰川湖被冰川磨出的岩粉染成青绿色，班夫小镇就在公园里，缆车、温泉和餐厅都在镇上。北边的冰原大道经弓湖、佩托湖一路通到贾斯珀，往西翻过大陆分水岭就是幽鹤。梦莲湖全年不让私家车进，旺季露易丝湖也很难停车，要提前预约 Parks Canada 班车。": "Established in 1885 as Canada's first national park, and the most popular in the Rockies. Glacial lakes like Lake Louise, Moraine Lake, and Peyto Lake are colored turquoise by rock flour ground by glaciers. The town of Banff is inside the park, with the gondola, hot springs, and restaurants all in town. To the north, the Icefields Parkway runs past Bow Lake and Peyto Lake all the way to Jasper; to the west, over the Continental Divide, is Yoho. Moraine Lake is closed to private vehicles year-round, and parking at Lake Louise is very hard in peak season, so reserve a Parks Canada shuttle in advance.",
  "7–9 月湖水颜色最好、高处步道基本化雪，9 月中下旬看金色落叶松；梦莲湖只在 6 月到 10 月中旬通班车，冬天以滑雪和冰湖为主。": "July–September has the best lake color, and the high trails are mostly snow-free; in mid- to late September the larches turn gold. Shuttles to Moraine Lake run only from June to mid-October. Winter is mainly for skiing and frozen lakes.",
  "班夫镇周边": "Around the town of Banff",
  "明尼万卡湖环线": "Lake Minnewanka Loop",
  "弓河谷景观道 / 约翰斯顿峡谷": "Bow Valley Parkway / Johnston Canyon",
  "冰原大道南段（弓湖 / 佩托湖）": "Icefields Parkway, south (Bow Lake / Peyto Lake)",
  "班夫游客中心": "Banff Visitor Centre",
  "园内住宿集中在班夫镇和露易丝湖：露易丝湖城堡酒店、梦莲湖旅馆（夏季营业，住客可以开车上梦莲湖）最贵也最难订，班夫镇酒店多但夏季房价很高，通常要提前几个月订。东门外约 20 分钟的坎莫尔（Canmore）价格低一些、度假公寓多，是很多人的大本营；想早起去两个湖可以住露易丝湖村，走冰原大道可以在 Saskatchewan River Crossing 住一晚。": "Lodging in the park is concentrated in the town of Banff and at Lake Louise. Fairmont Chateau Lake Louise and Moraine Lake Lodge (open in summer; guests can drive up to Moraine Lake) are the most expensive and hardest to book. Banff has many hotels, but summer prices are very high, and you usually need to book months ahead. Canmore, about 20 minutes outside the east gate, is cheaper, with lots of condo-style rentals, and is many visitors' base. To reach both lakes early in the morning, stay in Lake Louise village; if you're driving the Icefields Parkway, you can spend a night at Saskatchewan River Crossing.",
  "贾斯珀": "Jasper",
  "冰原、碧湖与暗夜星空": "Icefields, turquoise lakes, and dark skies",
  "加拿大落基山面积最大的国家公园，冰原大道的北半段在这里：哥伦比亚冰原、阿萨巴斯卡冰川和桑瓦普塔、阿萨巴斯卡两座瀑布都在去贾斯珀镇的路上，镇东边的玛琳湖可以坐船去看精灵岛。这里是世界上最大的暗夜保护区之一，人比班夫少，路边常见马鹿、大角羊和熊。2024 年 7 月的山火烧毁了镇上约三分之一的建筑和周边大片森林，2026 年大部分步道已经重开，但玛琳峡谷和伊迪丝·卡维尔山路仍然关闭。": "The largest national park in the Canadian Rockies, containing the northern half of the Icefields Parkway. The Columbia Icefield, Athabasca Glacier, and Sunwapta and Athabasca Falls are all on the way to the town of Jasper, and east of town you can take a boat across Maligne Lake to see Spirit Island. It's one of the largest dark-sky preserves in the world, with fewer people than Banff, and elk, bighorn sheep, and bears are often seen along the road. The July 2024 wildfire destroyed about a third of the buildings in town and large areas of the surrounding forest. By 2026 most trails had reopened, but Maligne Canyon and the Mount Edith Cavell Road remain closed.",
  "6–9 月冰川车、玛琳湖游船和各条山路都开，9 月人少、马鹿发情；冬季冰原大道常因风雪和雪崩风险临时封路，11 月到次年 3 月必须装冬季轮胎或带防滑链。": "June–September, the glacier tours, Maligne Lake cruises, and all mountain roads are open; September is quieter, with the elk rut. In winter the Icefields Parkway often closes temporarily for storms and avalanche risk, and from November through March you must have winter tires or carry chains.",
  "贾斯珀镇周边": "Around the town of Jasper",
  "玛琳峡谷 / 玛琳湖": "Maligne Canyon / Maligne Lake",
  "冰原大道北段（瀑布）": "Icefields Parkway, north (waterfalls)",
  "哥伦比亚冰原": "Columbia Icefield",
  "16 号公路（米耶特温泉 / 罗布森山）": "Highway 16 (Miette Hot Springs / Mount Robson)",
  "贾斯珀国家公园信息中心": "Jasper National Park Information Centre",
  "园内住宿集中在贾斯珀镇和周边的度假村（费尔蒙贾斯珀公园小屋酒店、金字塔湖度假村等）。2024 年山火烧毁了几家酒店和不少私人民宿，房源比以前少，夏季要提前几个月订；订不到可以住东边约 1 小时车程的 Hinton，或西边 BC 省的 Valemount。走冰原大道可以在哥伦比亚冰原的冰川景观酒店或桑瓦普塔瀑布的木屋住一晚。": "Lodging in the park is concentrated in the town of Jasper and nearby resorts (Fairmont Jasper Park Lodge, Pyramid Lake Resort, and others). The 2024 wildfire destroyed several hotels and many private guest rooms, so there's less to choose from than before; book months ahead for summer. If you can't find anything, stay in Hinton, about an hour's drive east, or Valemount, B.C., to the west. If you're driving the Icefields Parkway, you can spend a night at the Glacier View Lodge at the Columbia Icefield or in the cabins at Sunwapta Falls.",
  "幽鹤": "Yoho",
  "翡翠湖、瀑布与化石": "Emerald lakes, waterfalls, and fossils",
  "在大陆分水岭西侧的 BC 省，名字来自克里语里表示惊叹的词。公园不大，离露易丝湖只有二十多分钟，常和班夫连着玩：翡翠湖、天然桥、塔卡考瀑布和螺旋隧道都在路边，欧哈拉湖的高山湖群只能坐抽签巴士或徒步 11 公里上去。伯吉斯页岩里有 5 亿多年前的寒武纪化石，只能跟 Parks Canada 的导览徒步进去。": "Yoho lies on the British Columbia side of the Continental Divide; its name comes from a Cree expression of awe. The park is small, just over 20 minutes from Lake Louise, and is often combined with Banff. Emerald Lake, the Natural Bridge, Takakkaw Falls, and the Spiral Tunnels are all right by the road, while the alpine lakes of Lake O'Hara are reachable only by lottery bus or a hike of about 7 miles (11 km). The Burgess Shale holds Cambrian fossils more than 500 million years old and can be visited only on guided hikes with Parks Canada.",
  "塔卡考瀑布所在的幽鹤谷路约 6 月中到 10 月中开放，欧哈拉湖巴士 6 月下旬到 10 月初；7–9 月最好，冬季只有翡翠湖一带和 1 号公路沿线能去。": "Yoho Valley Road, the route to Takakkaw Falls, is open from about mid-June to mid-October, and the Lake O'Hara bus runs from late June to early October. July–September is best; in winter only the Emerald Lake area and the Highway 1 corridor are accessible.",
  "Field 镇 / 1 号公路沿线": "Field / Highway 1",
  "翡翠湖 / 天然桥": "Emerald Lake / Natural Bridge",
  "幽鹤谷（塔卡考瀑布）": "Yoho Valley (Takakkaw Falls)",
  "幽鹤国家公园游客中心（Field）": "Yoho National Park Visitor Centre (Field)",
  "园内住宿不多：翡翠湖旅馆在湖边、价格高，幽鹤谷路口的大教堂山木屋酒店只在夏季营业，Field 小村有一家小旅馆和十几家民宅客房；欧哈拉湖旅馆和山屋要很早预订或抽签。更多人住西边约 45 分钟的 Golden（酒店多、价格低），或住东边的露易丝湖、班夫镇，当天往返幽鹤。": "Lodging in the park is limited. Emerald Lake Lodge sits on the lake and is expensive; Cathedral Mountain Lodge, at the turnoff for Yoho Valley Road, is open only in summer; and the small village of Field has one small inn and a dozen or so guest rooms in private homes. Lake O'Hara Lodge and the alpine huts must be booked very early or through a lottery. More people stay in Golden, about 45 minutes west (lots of hotels at lower prices), or stay east at Lake Louise or in Banff and visit Yoho as a day trip."
};
